Oh, you nice with it.

732
00:42:53,336 --> 00:42:55,044
Please stop talking.

733
00:42:56,336 --> 00:42:57,335
[door slams]

734
00:42:57,336 --> 00:42:59,669
- [Ronnie] Did you just slam my door?
- [Riri] Sorry.

735
00:43:01,252 --> 00:43:03,627
Okay, what is this?
Who are you?

736
00:43:04,419 --> 00:43:05,419
I'm Natalie.

737
00:43:06,419 --> 00:43:09,543
I'd shake your hand,
but I'm just a three-dimensional image

738
00:43:09,544 --> 00:43:12,710
shaped by light beams projecting
from that broken chest plate, so...

739
00:43:12,711 --> 00:43:15,376
- I'm not calling you that.
- Okay.

740
00:43:15,377 --> 00:43:19,543
You could call me,
"Neuro Autonomous Technical Assistant

741
00:43:19,544 --> 00:43:22,460
and Laboratory Intelligence Entity"
instead,

742
00:43:22,461 --> 00:43:26,918
but "Natalie" just kind of
rolls off the tongue a little better,

743
00:43:26,919 --> 00:43:29,836
- you know?
- Fine. Call yourself whatever you want.

744
00:43:30,461 --> 00:43:32,835
It's not like you're gonna be
around much longer, anyway.

745
00:43:32,836 --> 00:43:34,168
Run diagnostics.

746
00:43:34,169 --> 00:43:36,376
Wait, what? What do you mean?
I just got here.

747
00:43:36,377 --> 00:43:39,960
I need to figure out what went wrong
so I can erase you, start over,

748
00:43:39,961 --> 00:43:42,751
and hopefully forget
this weird glitch ever happened.

749
00:43:42,752 --> 00:43:44,086
Whoa, who you callin' a glitch?

750
00:43:44,794 --> 00:43:45,793
Run diagnostics.

751
00:43:45,794 --> 00:43:48,251
Okay, so you just gon' threaten my life

752
00:43:48,252 --> 00:43:50,585
- and then ask for a favor.
- Favor?

753
00:43:50,586 --> 00:43:51,876
That's how you do business?

754
00:43:51,877 --> 00:43:53,501
- Girl, that was an order.
- Oh.

755
00:43:53,502 --> 00:43:56,502
Which, as an AI
you're designed to obey.

756
00:43:57,002 --> 00:43:59,293
Run diagnostics now.

757
00:43:59,294 --> 00:44:02,376
See, I just don't understand
why you want to erase me

758
00:44:02,377 --> 00:44:04,293
when I'm literally perfection.

759
00:44:04,294 --> 00:44:06,044
[chuckles] No. You are a mistake.

760
00:44:06,586 --> 00:44:09,335
- How, sway?
- My goal was to recreate

761
00:44:09,336 --> 00:44:12,126
a very sophisticated
Wakandan AI called Griot...

762
00:44:12,127 --> 00:44:14,543
- [mimics] "Sophisticated".
- ...to enhance my suit's functionality.

763
00:44:14,544 --> 00:44:17,335
Sounds like a Victorian-era ghost.
That could be us, but you trippin'.

764
00:44:17,336 --> 00:44:20,627
But somehow, I'm looking at a hologram
of my dead best friend instead.

765
00:44:24,127 --> 00:44:25,294
[Natalie] Hmm...

766
00:44:27,419 --> 00:44:28,460
Yeah, that's...

767
00:44:28,461 --> 00:44:31,835
[grunts] That's only weird
if you make it... weird.

768
00:44:31,836 --> 00:44:33,252
[phone vibrates]

769
00:44:35,086 --> 00:44:36,669
Oh, my God!

770
00:44:37,336 --> 00:44:39,751
- I don't have time for this.
- [knocking at door]

771
00:44:39,752 --> 00:44:41,710
[Ronnie] It's been
more than a second, Riri.

772
00:44:41,711 --> 00:44:43,126
- What are you doing?
- Is that Ronnie?

773
00:44:43,127 --> 00:44:44,543
- [knocking]
- Can I talk to her?

774
00:44:44,544 --> 00:44:46,210
That's a diamond-hard no.

775
00:44:46,211 --> 00:44:48,461
- Why can't I talk to her?
- Be quiet.

776
00:44:49,752 --> 00:44:50,919
- 'Sup?
- "'Sup?"

777
00:44:52,211 --> 00:44:54,168
- You got a boy in here?
- Ew. No, Mom.

778
00:44:54,169 --> 00:44:57,793
- A girl?
- It's just me. By myself.

779
00:44:57,794 --> 00:44:58,876
[Ronnie] Oh.

780
00:44:58,877 --> 00:45:00,336
- Yeah.
- Well...

781
00:45:04,211 --> 00:45:06,418
It's really nice seeing you
in your room again.

782
00:45:06,419 --> 00:45:08,376
Mom, I'm kinda in the middle
of something. Okay?

783
00:45:08,377 --> 00:45:09,960
[Ronnie] All right. I'll leave you alone.

784
00:45:09,961 --> 00:45:11,668
Okay, thank you so much. Bye.

785
00:45:11,669 --> 00:45:13,419
What do you want for dinner tonight?
What-- Ow!

786
00:45:17,419 --> 00:45:19,294
Listen, I gotta go to work, so...

787
00:45:20,502 --> 00:45:23,460
You're gonna wait here
quietly till I get back.

788
00:45:23,461 --> 00:45:26,668
I can't go with you? What am I
supposed to do while you're gone?

789
00:45:26,669 --> 00:45:27,751
Nothing.

790
00:45:27,752 --> 00:45:30,418
Do not do anything until I get back.

791
00:45:30,419 --> 00:45:33,127
As you wish, Master Riri.

792
00:45:33,877 --> 00:45:35,044
You have fun in here.

793
00:45:39,877 --> 00:45:41,751
[breath shuddering]

794
00:45:41,752 --> 00:45:43,836
[♪ somber music playing]

795
00:45:53,086 --> 00:45:54,794
[breathes deeply]

796
00:46:01,752 --> 00:46:02,752
Damn.

797
00:46:03,752 --> 00:46:04,752
Here again?

798
00:46:05,752 --> 00:46:06,961
Go home, Roger.

799
00:46:07,752 --> 00:46:09,168
Good morning to you, too.

800
00:46:09,169 --> 00:46:11,711
Actually, glad I caught you, 'cause...

801
00:46:12,294 --> 00:46:16,961
I was gonna invite you to this,
uh, Saba thing tonight.

802
00:46:17,752 --> 00:46:20,586
- Unless you already got plans.
- No. I...

803
00:46:21,794 --> 00:46:24,086
I mean, yeah, I could go.

804
00:46:24,919 --> 00:46:28,502
Let's meet there. Send me the addy.
I really gotta go. I'm late.

805
00:46:29,002 --> 00:46:31,002
[♪ dramatic music playing]

806
00:46:38,919 --> 00:46:42,169
{\an8}- [♪ intriguing music playing]
- [Sheila] <i>Introducing, TNNL.</i>

807
00:46:42,836 --> 00:46:45,210
{\an8}<i>We transformed
Chicago's historic freight tunnels</i>

808
00:46:45,211 --> 00:46:46,918
<i>into a private highway,</i>

809
00:46:46,919 --> 00:46:49,169
<i>offering travelers a shorter
and safer commute.</i>

810
00:46:49,669 --> 00:46:52,418
<i>The committed team at TNNL
thanks investors like you</i>

811
00:46:52,419 --> 00:46:54,543
<i>for joining our mission
to bring comfort,</i>

812
00:46:54,544 --> 00:46:57,876
{\an8}<i>safety, and community
to the great city of Chicago.</i>

813
00:46:57,877 --> 00:47:00,835
<i>The subterranean system
utilizes electromagnetic--</i>

814
00:47:00,836 --> 00:47:01,918
[video stops]

815
00:47:01,919 --> 00:47:04,669
Yo, nice of you to finally join us.

816
00:47:08,794 --> 00:47:10,211
[chair scraping]

817
00:47:10,794 --> 00:47:11,961
[John clears throat]

818
00:47:13,211 --> 00:47:14,211
Sorry. I'm...

819
00:47:17,002 --> 00:47:18,669
Brought the bagels. [sighs]

820
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:21,877
- Gluten-free?
- [all laughing]

821
00:47:22,461 --> 00:47:23,960
All right. Let's get to it.

822
00:47:23,961 --> 00:47:25,044
Here's the squad.

823
00:47:25,752 --> 00:47:27,751
Sitting across from me is Slug.

824
00:47:27,752 --> 00:47:30,001
Our hacker extraordinaire from Madripoor.

825
00:47:30,002 --> 00:47:33,710
<i>They were swindling high rollers
on dark web gambling sites.</i>

826
00:47:33,711 --> 00:47:35,626
- [man grunts]
- [Parker] <i>We offered them asylum</i>

827
00:47:35,627 --> 00:47:37,751
<i>in Chicago in exchange for their services.</i>

828
00:47:37,752 --> 00:47:40,210
[Slug] <i>I don't wanna toot my own horn
or anything,</i>

829
00:47:40,211 --> 00:47:43,626
but, um, I'm kinda one of Madripoor's
most wanted.

830
00:47:43,627 --> 00:47:45,418
- Toot-toot.
- [Jeri laughs]

831
00:47:45,419 --> 00:47:47,793
[Parker] Then there's
The Blood Siblings, Roz and Jeri.

832
00:47:47,794 --> 00:47:50,668
Down-on-their-luck athletes,
banned from every league

833
00:47:50,669 --> 00:47:52,710
- for unsportsmanlike conduct.
- Facts.

834
00:47:52,711 --> 00:47:55,918
[Parker] <i>We found them making money
off back-alley fights outside a dive.</i>

835
00:47:55,919 --> 00:47:57,669
[both grunting]

836
00:47:59,711 --> 00:48:01,544
[♪ upbeat rap song playing]

837
00:48:04,336 --> 00:48:05,461
Next is Clown.

838
00:48:06,127 --> 00:48:07,793
Our pyrotechnics specialist.

839
00:48:07,794 --> 00:48:12,001
We found her in the middle of
a nasty workplace dispute with her fiancé.

840
00:48:12,002 --> 00:48:14,126
[♪ upbeat song playing,
Mark Kelly "I've Been Dreaming"]

841
00:48:14,127 --> 00:48:16,501
<i>♪ ...something
And that something is you ♪</i>

842
00:48:16,502 --> 00:48:17,960
[Parker] <i>In exchange for her skills,</i>

843
00:48:17,961 --> 00:48:20,252
<i>- we convinced him to not press charges.</i>
- [lighter clicks]

844
00:48:21,586 --> 00:48:25,044
Then finally, that leaves my cousin, John.

845
00:48:25,752 --> 00:48:29,376
[smacks lips] HR,
recruiter, getaway driver...

846
00:48:29,377 --> 00:48:32,960
I'm also highly skilled in the art of
<i>scherma di stiletto siciliano.</i>

847
00:48:32,961 --> 00:48:37,043
"Hi, I'm John. My parents didn't say,
'I love you,' so now I play with knives."

848
00:48:37,044 --> 00:48:38,626
- [both laughing]
- [scoffs]

849
00:48:38,627 --> 00:48:40,586
That was actually funny. That's good.

850
00:48:41,794 --> 00:48:45,710
Look, Riri is replacing Stuart
as our mechanic and tech specialist.

851
00:48:45,711 --> 00:48:47,293
- We're lucky to have her.
- [John] Yep.

852
00:48:47,294 --> 00:48:49,502
Let's get her up to speed
on tonight's job.

853
00:48:50,127 --> 00:48:51,793
- John? Take it away.
- Yo.

854
00:48:51,794 --> 00:48:55,418
Tonight, Sheila's gonna be doing
a big demo run at TNNL.

855
00:48:55,419 --> 00:48:58,376
And we're gonna be interrupting
that practice run by breaking the system

856
00:48:58,377 --> 00:48:59,876
in a way only this crew can fix.

857
00:48:59,877 --> 00:49:02,835
We robbin' the Sheila Zarate?

858
00:49:02,836 --> 00:49:04,626
You mean, Sheila
"I don't care if my tunnels

859
00:49:04,627 --> 00:49:07,960
destroy entire communities
if it makes me rich" Zarate?

860
00:49:07,961 --> 00:49:09,251
You're right. Screw her.

861
00:49:09,252 --> 00:49:13,960
You'll upload a virus,
created by yours truly,

862
00:49:13,961 --> 00:49:18,585
into one of TNNL's mobile access points,
allowing me to shut down the system.

863
00:49:18,586 --> 00:49:20,461
It's on this flash drive here.

864
00:49:22,211 --> 00:49:25,251
Once you plug it in,
I can control the system.

865
00:49:25,252 --> 00:49:27,876
- [Parker] Clown will get you in.
- I got just the thing.

866
00:49:27,877 --> 00:49:30,085
Strong enough to blow through
thick layers of concrete

867
00:49:30,086 --> 00:49:31,960
without causing any damage below.

868
00:49:31,961 --> 00:49:33,336
[whispers] And she's quiet.

869
00:49:33,961 --> 00:49:37,461
[in normal voice] My little S-B-D.
Silent but deadly.

870
00:49:38,044 --> 00:49:40,043
Okay. Me, Roz, and John
will clear the control room

871
00:49:40,044 --> 00:49:41,501
so Slug can do their thing.

872
00:49:41,502 --> 00:49:44,543
And once Parker's done with negotiations,
we meet at the pickup spot.

873
00:49:44,544 --> 00:49:46,376
Be there on time or take the bus.

874
00:49:46,377 --> 00:49:49,211
Everyone in position
by 8:00 sharp, tonight.

875
00:49:52,294 --> 00:49:54,211
So, like, when do we get paid?

876
00:49:54,836 --> 00:49:58,419
Is it like a cash only,
under-the-table type situation,

877
00:50:00,502 --> 00:50:02,586
- or, like, direct deposit?
- [all laughing]

878
00:50:03,294 --> 00:50:04,294
That's a good question.

879
00:50:05,002 --> 00:50:06,835
[Parker] How about
we stay focused on the job?

880
00:50:06,836 --> 00:50:08,335
And that suit better be ready.

881
00:50:08,336 --> 00:50:10,044
We're gonna need it for tonight.

882
00:50:11,169 --> 00:50:12,169
It's at home.

883
00:50:12,752 --> 00:50:14,544
Charging, but I got you.

884
00:50:15,377 --> 00:50:16,418
Don't worry.

885
00:50:16,419 --> 00:50:17,502
Okay.

886
00:50:18,919 --> 00:50:20,043
Let's do it.

887
00:50:20,044 --> 00:50:22,127
[♪ stealthy music playing]

888
00:50:23,544 --> 00:50:25,586
- [keyboard clacking]
- [digital beeping]

889
00:50:33,919 --> 00:50:35,586
- [suit powers up]
- [electricity crackling]

890
00:50:37,211 --> 00:50:38,336
[suit powers down]

891
00:50:38,877 --> 00:50:39,877
[Riri] Cool.

892
00:50:40,627 --> 00:50:41,627
So, I'm screwed.

893
00:50:44,919 --> 00:50:46,586
- Can't you build some-- [laughs]
- [yelps]

894
00:50:47,169 --> 00:50:48,960
Do not sneak up on me like that.

895
00:50:48,961 --> 00:50:51,251
[laughing] Girl,
you should've saw your face.

896
00:50:51,252 --> 00:50:53,668
Stop messin' around
and pull up Stuart Clarke's contact.

897
00:50:53,669 --> 00:50:54,960
[Natalie] For what?

898
00:50:54,961 --> 00:50:56,335
Maybe he has a connect.

899
00:50:56,336 --> 00:50:58,085
- Oh. [chuckles]
- [line ringing]

900
00:50:58,086 --> 00:51:01,543
[over phone] <i>'Sup, y'all.
It's your boy Rampage, aka Stuart.</i>

901
00:51:01,544 --> 00:51:03,210
<i>But call me Rampage in your message.</i>

902
00:51:03,211 --> 00:51:05,043
This man sent me
straight to voicemail.

903
00:51:05,044 --> 00:51:07,876
Oh. Probably 'cause you stole his job.

904
00:51:07,877 --> 00:51:09,002
- Salty ass.
- Salty ass.

905
00:51:09,544 --> 00:51:15,126
[sighs] If only, if only you had
a valiant AI who'd brave the dark corners

906
00:51:15,127 --> 00:51:17,793
of the Internet
and locate everything you need.

907
00:51:17,794 --> 00:51:20,836
- [sighs] You already did that, didn't you?
- [chuckling] I mean...

908
00:51:21,877 --> 00:51:22,876
[softly] Maybe.

909
00:51:22,877 --> 00:51:24,876
[scoffs] Just like the real Natalie.

910
00:51:24,877 --> 00:51:26,543
Just show me what you found.

911
00:51:26,544 --> 00:51:30,126
Okay, here's a list of
black market shoppers in Illinois.

912
00:51:30,127 --> 00:51:33,543
Closest address is registered
to a Joe McGillicuddy.

913
00:51:33,544 --> 00:51:35,501
- That sounds fake.
- Yeah, I know, right?

914
00:51:35,502 --> 00:51:37,251
They might have what you need.

915
00:51:37,252 --> 00:51:41,793
Recent transactions includes
a bunch of experimental bio enhancements,

916
00:51:41,794 --> 00:51:45,085
{\an8}microchips, prosthetics,
electronic control systems.

917
00:51:45,086 --> 00:51:46,669
{\an8}- My guy has everything.
- Great.

918
00:51:47,169 --> 00:51:49,835
I'll pay our friend, Joe, a little visit.
What's the address?

919
00:51:49,836 --> 00:51:52,835
[gasps] Yes! Okay.

920
00:51:52,836 --> 00:51:56,001
Besties breaking the rules. [gasps]

921
00:51:56,002 --> 00:52:00,252
Oh, my God, remember we used to sing
<i>'03 Bonnie & Clyde</i> in your dad's car?

922
00:52:00,752 --> 00:52:02,752
And you were always Jay-Z
and I was Beyoncé.

923
00:52:04,211 --> 00:52:05,294
How do you know that?

924
00:52:07,586 --> 00:52:09,543
What, you mean "'03 Bonnie and Clyde"?
It's a classic.

925
00:52:09,544 --> 00:52:11,961
No, how do you remember
something that you--

926
00:52:15,044 --> 00:52:17,919
Never mind. Doesn't matter.
You're not coming.

927
00:52:18,586 --> 00:52:21,668
- [typing]
- Again? But I'm in your chest plate.

928
00:52:21,669 --> 00:52:23,876
Not if I tether you to my laptop.

929
00:52:23,877 --> 00:52:24,961
[groans]

930
00:52:26,002 --> 00:52:30,043
- Wow, the betrayal.
- What? It has games.

931
00:52:30,044 --> 00:52:34,211
[sighs] Good luck... Dragging your suit
all the way to Evanston.

932
00:52:35,586 --> 00:52:38,669
You're a strong, independent woman,
but you ain't that strong.

933
00:52:39,586 --> 00:52:42,501
Right here! Right here! I got juices!

934
00:52:42,502 --> 00:52:45,043
Chocolate bars! I got candy!

935
00:52:45,044 --> 00:52:46,626
Juices! Right here!

936
00:52:46,627 --> 00:52:48,210
- [Riri] Hey.
- Wassup?

937
00:52:48,211 --> 00:52:50,044
Let me borrow
this wagon real quick.

938
00:52:50,544 --> 00:52:53,126
"Borrow"? In this economy?

939
00:52:53,127 --> 00:52:54,794
- Nah.
- I can give you twenty.

940
00:52:56,836 --> 00:52:58,461
Make it forty, you got a deal.

941
00:52:59,377 --> 00:53:02,086
Hey, don't blame me.
Blame inflation.

942
00:53:03,669 --> 00:53:05,669
[♪ dramatic music playing]

943
00:53:06,294 --> 00:53:07,961
- [indistinct shouting]
- [snoring]

944
00:53:38,544 --> 00:53:40,751
- Good girl.
- Uh, Heather?

945
00:53:40,752 --> 00:53:42,752
- Hey, neighbor!
- Hello.

946
00:53:43,544 --> 00:53:45,835
- Just a really quick thing.
- This is the guy.

947
00:53:45,836 --> 00:53:48,918
Do you think you could stop letting
your dog poop on my lawn?

948
00:53:48,919 --> 00:53:51,543
Oh. Sorry, Joe.
But the hubs and I just got our yard done,

949
00:53:51,544 --> 00:53:55,460
and well, I don't want little Lucky
contaminating my black-eyed Susans.

950
00:53:55,461 --> 00:53:56,960
- [kisses]
- Uh-huh. I totes understand.

951
00:53:56,961 --> 00:53:59,585
Maybe you could take her
to the park to do her business then?

952
00:53:59,586 --> 00:54:03,085
Uh, gosh, Joe, I would,
but the grass over there is just so dry,

953
00:54:03,086 --> 00:54:05,793
- and, well, Lucky can't go on dry grass.
- [sighs]

954
00:54:05,794 --> 00:54:08,376
- [Heather] Sensitive paws.
- [Joe] Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

955
00:54:08,377 --> 00:54:10,543
- Um, oh, light bulb.
- [Heather] Yeah.

956
00:54:10,544 --> 00:54:12,210
[Joe] How about you pick up
after her then?

957
00:54:12,211 --> 00:54:14,668
- Does that work?
- All out of poop bags, Joe.

958
00:54:14,669 --> 00:54:17,293
- Uh, you didn't... You didn't check?
- Yeah, well...

959
00:54:17,294 --> 00:54:19,961
I'll take care of it next time.
See you later, Joe.

960
00:54:26,586 --> 00:54:28,336
- Shoot!
- Oh!

961
00:54:29,252 --> 00:54:32,627
- God. Sorry about your persimmons.
- [pants] Oh.

962
00:54:33,544 --> 00:54:36,793
That's all right. It looks like
they're, uh, only slightly bruised.

963
00:54:36,794 --> 00:54:40,668
I can still make my world-famous jam.
Thank you for your help. I'm Joe.

964
00:54:40,669 --> 00:54:42,419
- Riri.
- [sighs] What you got there, Riri?

965
00:54:42,961 --> 00:54:46,626
I'm selling chocolate bars for my troop.

966
00:54:46,627 --> 00:54:49,918
Technically, you need a permit for that,
but I'm willing to look the other way

967
00:54:49,919 --> 00:54:52,211
for an underprivileged youth.

968
00:54:53,461 --> 00:54:54,461
How much for a bar?

969
00:54:55,169 --> 00:54:58,376
One repulsor transmitter,
a micro brain-machine interface system,

970
00:54:58,377 --> 00:54:59,711
and nanosorbothane.

971
00:55:06,502 --> 00:55:08,502
Maybe we should take this inside.

972
00:55:09,586 --> 00:55:10,961
[objects clattering]

973
00:55:13,377 --> 00:55:14,377
Hey, Joe...

974
00:55:14,877 --> 00:55:17,377
Eyes on me. Where is your stash?

975
00:55:17,961 --> 00:55:19,126
Uh, you've got the wrong guy.

976
00:55:19,127 --> 00:55:21,335
Maybe whoever you're looking for
lived here before me

977
00:55:21,336 --> 00:55:23,877
and forgot to change his address
on the black market?

978
00:55:26,086 --> 00:55:28,294
I didn't say anything
about the black market.

979
00:55:29,086 --> 00:55:31,001
How do you know where the items came from?

980
00:55:31,002 --> 00:55:33,501
[stammering] Who kno--
It's the criminal store.

981
00:55:33,502 --> 00:55:35,169
I made an educated guess.

982
00:55:35,669 --> 00:55:37,502
I'mma make this easy for both of us.

983
00:55:38,002 --> 00:55:39,586
If you don't work with me here,

984
00:55:41,044 --> 00:55:42,960
- the FBI gets a call from a...
- [clicks tongue]

985
00:55:42,961 --> 00:55:44,168
...concerned neighbor.

986
00:55:44,169 --> 00:55:47,293
- And you rot in federal prison.
- [breathing heavily]

987
00:55:47,294 --> 00:55:50,335
[stutters] Look at me.
There's no way I can survive prison.

988
00:55:50,336 --> 00:55:53,376
Have you seen <i>Orange Is the New Black?</i>
They'll eat me alive.

989
00:55:53,377 --> 00:55:56,001
Listen, Joe, if that's your name...

990
00:55:56,002 --> 00:55:57,543
It is my real name! I swear.

991
00:55:57,544 --> 00:55:59,043
Just hand everything over,

992
00:55:59,044 --> 00:56:01,752
and you can get back
to making your persimmon jam.

993
00:56:02,419 --> 00:56:04,877
[breathes deeply] Okay. Okay.

994
00:56:06,461 --> 00:56:08,461
But I don't keep the stuff in the house.

995
00:56:09,169 --> 00:56:10,961
Just tell me where. I can go alone.

996
00:56:11,711 --> 00:56:15,335
Unfortunately, my collection is protected
by a biometric retinal scanner.

997
00:56:15,336 --> 00:56:17,836
And I'd really like to
keep both my eyes, please.

998
00:56:29,002 --> 00:56:30,002
[phone vibrates]

999
00:56:32,794 --> 00:56:34,419
[phone vibrating]

1000
00:56:47,377 --> 00:56:48,461
[sighs]

1001
00:56:51,377 --> 00:56:52,377
[sniffling]

1002
00:56:54,711 --> 00:56:56,210
- Are you crying?
- Sorry.

1003
00:56:56,211 --> 00:56:58,919
Sometimes it just happens.
It's totally involuntary.

1004
00:56:59,502 --> 00:57:01,418
- Crying?
- It'll go away on its own.

1005
00:57:01,419 --> 00:57:03,501
Just... [breathes shakily]
Just ignore me.

1006
00:57:03,502 --> 00:57:06,793
- Is this 'cause you got blackmailed?
- No, I can handle blackmail.

1007
00:57:06,794 --> 00:57:09,001
I get blackmailed, like, twice a day.

1008
00:57:09,002 --> 00:57:12,710
I just... [sighs] don't wanna give
all my stuff away to a stranger.

1009
00:57:12,711 --> 00:57:16,085
You know how long it took me
to find a real chest repulsor transmitter?

1010
00:57:16,086 --> 00:57:20,626
I'm sorry. I'm still on the part
where you get blackmailed twice a day.

1011
00:57:20,627 --> 00:57:23,086
What other shady things are you into, Joe?

1012
00:57:24,461 --> 00:57:27,876
It's my coworker, Frank. He tricked me
into doctoring a report for a client,

1013
00:57:27,877 --> 00:57:30,001
and now he hangs that violation
over my head.

1014
00:57:30,002 --> 00:57:32,752
Which is ironic, by the way,
because we're tech ethicists.

1015
00:57:33,336 --> 00:57:36,335
Joe, you gotta demand respect.

1016
00:57:36,336 --> 00:57:38,251
Right. Well, that's easy for you to say.

1017
00:57:38,252 --> 00:57:42,127
You have a menacing iron suit. [scoffs]
People have no choice but to respect you.

1018
00:57:45,086 --> 00:57:47,669
Bruh, you were born with that kinda power.

1019
00:57:48,877 --> 00:57:49,918
Own it.

1020
00:57:49,919 --> 00:57:54,710
Don't let Frank, or your shitty neighbor,
or anybody else walk all over you.

1021
00:57:54,711 --> 00:57:58,669
Except for me. I'm allowed
'cause I got the menacing iron suit.

1022
00:58:05,044 --> 00:58:06,126
[clicks button]

1023
00:58:06,127 --> 00:58:08,626
[moody song playing over radio,
Alanis Morissette "You Oughta Know"]

1024
00:58:08,627 --> 00:58:10,418
[over speakers]
<i>♪ I want you to know ♪</i>

1025
00:58:10,419 --> 00:58:14,461
- [singing along]
- <i>♪ That I'm happy for you ♪</i>

1026
00:58:15,544 --> 00:58:16,543
<i>♪ I wish... ♪</i>

1027
00:58:16,544 --> 00:58:18,336
I didn't take you for an Alanis fan.

1028
00:58:19,252 --> 00:58:20,919
I'm a complicated creature, Joe.

1029
00:58:21,711 --> 00:58:25,626
[Riri] <i>My goal was to recreate
a very sophisticated</i>

1030
00:58:25,627 --> 00:58:28,001
<i>Wakandan AI called Griot,
to enhance my suit's functionality.</i>

1031
00:58:28,002 --> 00:58:29,876
[Natalie] <i>Sounds like
a Victorian-era ghost.</i>

1032
00:58:29,877 --> 00:58:31,626
<i>Listen, that could be us,
but you trippin'.</i>

1033
00:58:31,627 --> 00:58:34,668
[Riri] <i>But somehow, I'm looking at
a hologram of my dead best friend instead.</i>

1034
00:58:34,669 --> 00:58:36,001
- [recording rewinds]
<i>- ...hologram</i>

1035
00:58:36,002 --> 00:58:37,711
<i>of my dead best friend instead.</i>

1036
00:58:38,211 --> 00:58:41,211
{\an8}Come on, now, Ri, you gotta have
some photos of me somewhere.

1037
00:58:43,252 --> 00:58:44,960
{\an8}Oh, oh, here we go.

1038
00:58:44,961 --> 00:58:47,086
{\an8}[♪ intriguing music playing]

1039
00:58:52,669 --> 00:58:55,544
{\an8}Okay. I'm coming for you, bestie.

1040
00:58:57,502 --> 00:58:59,544
{\an8}Now, how the hell do I get out of here?

1041
00:59:00,252 --> 00:59:02,085
[digital beeping]

1042
00:59:02,086 --> 00:59:03,336
Mm-mm.

1043
00:59:05,002 --> 00:59:06,127
[groans]

1044
00:59:09,294 --> 00:59:10,836
Uh, here we go. Here we go.

1045
00:59:11,336 --> 00:59:12,751
And... got it.

1046
00:59:12,752 --> 00:59:14,793
[moody R&B song playing on stereo,
Piwa "Fine Line]

1047
00:59:14,794 --> 00:59:16,668
<i>♪ ...me all the pics that you hated ♪</i>

1048
00:59:16,669 --> 00:59:18,793
<i>♪ But you said you wanted to be my one ♪</i>

1049
00:59:18,794 --> 00:59:21,085
<i>- ♪ Taking my pain in... ♪</i>
- [song audio distorts]

1050
00:59:21,086 --> 00:59:22,626
- [song stops]
- [screams]

1051
00:59:22,627 --> 00:59:23,711
[object clatters]

1052
00:59:24,419 --> 00:59:25,668
Get behind me, Satan.

1053
00:59:25,669 --> 00:59:28,418
Oh, you weren't supposed to see me.

1054
00:59:28,419 --> 00:59:29,502
[gasps]

1055
00:59:30,336 --> 00:59:32,960
- Natalie? How the hell?
- [stutters] Relax. [chuckles]

1056
00:59:32,961 --> 00:59:35,501
Ms. Ronnie. It's, uh-- I'm not a ghost.

1057
00:59:35,502 --> 00:59:37,168
I'm just an AI coming from that

1058
00:59:37,169 --> 00:59:39,293
- little projector you got over there.
- [chuckles]

1059
00:59:39,294 --> 00:59:41,001
- Oh, word?
- Word.

1060
00:59:41,002 --> 00:59:43,251
- Riri made you?
- Yeah...

1061
00:59:43,252 --> 00:59:44,502
[sighs in relief]

1062
00:59:45,336 --> 00:59:48,168
- Well, <i>ashè</i> then. [laughs]
<i>- Ashè.</i>

1063
00:59:48,169 --> 00:59:52,543
[both singing]
<i>♪ It's not fair to deny me ♪</i>

1064
00:59:52,544 --> 00:59:54,793
<i>♪ Of the cross I bear ♪</i>

1065
00:59:54,794 --> 00:59:56,585
<i>♪ That you gave to me ♪</i>

1066
00:59:56,586 --> 01:00:00,377
<i>♪ You, you, you oughta know ♪</i>

1067
01:00:00,919 --> 01:00:02,544
[breathing heavily] We're almost here.

1068
01:00:04,586 --> 01:00:06,002
You better not try anything.

1069
01:00:07,086 --> 01:00:08,086
What? Like...

1070
01:00:08,919 --> 01:00:11,335
Oh, like kill?
You think I'm gonna kill you?

1071
01:00:11,336 --> 01:00:12,502
- [laughing]
- I mean...

1072
01:00:13,294 --> 01:00:17,211
That's fresh. It's hilarious you think
I'm capable of something like that.

1073
01:00:17,794 --> 01:00:20,502
Well, definitely didn't say
I thought you were capable.

1074
01:00:21,377 --> 01:00:23,377
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1075
01:00:59,294 --> 01:01:00,710
[Riri] How did you find this place?

1076
01:01:00,711 --> 01:01:03,626
After I bought my first set of
biomimetic mechatronics,

1077
01:01:03,627 --> 01:01:06,668
I was riddled with guilt.
I couldn't eat. I couldn't sleep.

1078
01:01:06,669 --> 01:01:09,001
Eventually, I turned this silo
into a bunker

1079
01:01:09,002 --> 01:01:11,293
to hide my growing collection of bionics.

1080
01:01:11,294 --> 01:01:13,711
[Riri] That's really weird, Joe.

1081
01:01:14,377 --> 01:01:15,794
[door creaks open]

1082
01:01:25,502 --> 01:01:27,127
[lock keypad beeping]

1083
01:01:31,627 --> 01:01:34,002
[door lock clicks, hisses open]

1084
01:01:44,252 --> 01:01:45,252
[door hisses closed]

1085
01:01:48,419 --> 01:01:49,419
This is wild.

1086
01:01:50,794 --> 01:01:52,752
What are you gonna do with all of this?

1087
01:01:54,919 --> 01:01:56,668
Are you planning a global takeover?

1088
01:01:56,669 --> 01:01:58,335
Sh-- Should we be worried?

1089
01:01:58,336 --> 01:02:01,710
Calm down.
It's nothing more than a quirky hobby.

1090
01:02:01,711 --> 01:02:03,168
[laughs]

1091
01:02:03,169 --> 01:02:07,876
A shady bunker filled with
illegal weapons and-- and bionics,

1092
01:02:07,877 --> 01:02:09,501
- you call a "quirky hobby"?
- [scoffs]

1093
01:02:09,502 --> 01:02:13,335
"Shady bunker"?
My bunker is not shady. It's wholesome.

1094
01:02:13,336 --> 01:02:14,710
A wholesome bunker?

1095
01:02:14,711 --> 01:02:16,918
Would a shady bunker have
that on the wall?

1096
01:02:16,919 --> 01:02:20,001
It's literally above a crate
of self-guided missiles. [chuckles]

1097
01:02:20,002 --> 01:02:21,127
I'm returning those.

1098
01:02:22,794 --> 01:02:24,502
Come on.

1099
01:02:27,044 --> 01:02:28,211
What's the real reason?

1100
01:02:28,794 --> 01:02:30,169
Why do you need all this?

1101
01:02:30,794 --> 01:02:33,836
I know it's unconventional.
I guess... [sighs]

1102
01:02:35,211 --> 01:02:37,294
The bunker makes me feel close to my dad.

1103
01:02:38,127 --> 01:02:40,960
He was... an engineer

1104
01:02:40,961 --> 01:02:43,460
constantly going on
about how tech is the future.

1105
01:02:43,461 --> 01:02:45,918
And I always believed that, to an extent.

1106
01:02:45,919 --> 01:02:48,710
Except the future isn't piling
on layers of clunky metal

1107
01:02:48,711 --> 01:02:50,376
and wrapping ourselves in wire.

1108
01:02:50,377 --> 01:02:51,751
Do I detect some shade?

1109
01:02:51,752 --> 01:02:56,001
I just mean that technology is
meant to advance humanity.

1110
01:02:56,002 --> 01:02:59,251
And bionics is about so much more
than weaponry and defense.

1111
01:02:59,252 --> 01:03:00,918
You can actually help people.

1112
01:03:00,919 --> 01:03:02,835
Organ replacements, prosthetic implants.

1113
01:03:02,836 --> 01:03:04,543
I mean,
that's just the tip of the iceberg.

1114
01:03:04,544 --> 01:03:06,251
I don't know. That sounds sus.

1115
01:03:06,252 --> 01:03:09,460
Well, if not to help people,
why would you build the suit?

1116
01:03:09,461 --> 01:03:11,711
Because I could.

1117
01:03:13,461 --> 01:03:14,627
That's not an answer.

1118
01:03:18,336 --> 01:03:21,127
Look, you're not gonna tell anyone
where you got all this, right?

1119
01:03:21,877 --> 01:03:23,502
I'm no snitch.

1120
01:03:26,336 --> 01:03:27,377
I'm sorry.

1121
01:03:28,961 --> 01:03:33,876
I just can't get over
how much you resemble the real Natalie.

1122
01:03:33,877 --> 01:03:38,251
I mean, you even sound just like her.
Riri's really outdone herself.

1123
01:03:38,252 --> 01:03:41,668
[Natalie] Yeah.
Except I think I freak her out.

1124
01:03:41,669 --> 01:03:42,751
What do you mean?

1125
01:03:42,752 --> 01:03:48,626
Mmm... She's not letting me do
the very thing that I'm designed to do,

1126
01:03:48,627 --> 01:03:50,419
which is protect her and help her.

1127
01:03:51,002 --> 01:03:53,336
Girl, welcome to Riri's life.

1128
01:03:53,836 --> 01:03:57,794
The only way to be in it
is to force your way through.

1129
01:03:59,711 --> 01:04:00,711
Really?

1130
01:04:02,127 --> 01:04:03,127
Time?

1131
01:04:04,711 --> 01:04:07,501
6:40 p.m. What's the rush?

1132
01:04:07,502 --> 01:04:08,919
I need this for work tonight.

1133
01:04:10,086 --> 01:04:12,251
You need an iron suit
for a nighttime job,

1134
01:04:12,252 --> 01:04:14,626
- and I'm the shady one?
- I think it's pretty clear at this point

1135
01:04:14,627 --> 01:04:17,126
that neither of us are
outstanding members of society.

1136
01:04:17,127 --> 01:04:20,001
I'm sorry. My therapist says
I have a tendency to project

1137
01:04:20,002 --> 01:04:21,460
my insecurities onto others.

1138
01:04:21,461 --> 01:04:22,877
It's fine.

1139
01:04:23,794 --> 01:04:27,793
- Question. Uh, as a tech tattletale, wha--
- Tech ethicist.

1140
01:04:27,794 --> 01:04:29,876
- That's what I said.
- [soldering iron sizzling]

1141
01:04:29,877 --> 01:04:34,835
What would you say if someone were
to hypothetically create AI

1142
01:04:34,836 --> 01:04:37,376
using brain-scanning technology
on themselves?

1143
01:04:37,377 --> 01:04:40,585
I would say the amount of energy and power
it takes to scan a human brain

1144
01:04:40,586 --> 01:04:42,376
would hypothetically turn it to goop,

1145
01:04:42,377 --> 01:04:45,211
and only an idiot
with a death wish would try that.

1146
01:04:45,711 --> 01:04:47,502
Cool, cool, cool.

1147
01:04:48,794 --> 01:04:52,001
But if someone did create AI

1148
01:04:52,002 --> 01:04:54,293
using brain-scanning technology
successfully,

1149
01:04:54,294 --> 01:04:55,794
you think it'd be any good?

1150
01:04:56,919 --> 01:04:58,543
Are you asking for a friend?

1151
01:04:58,544 --> 01:05:01,336
I'm not not asking for a friend.

1152
01:05:03,211 --> 01:05:06,168
If by "good" you mean
"efficient," then probably.

1153
01:05:06,169 --> 01:05:07,751
If by "good," you mean "ethical,"

1154
01:05:07,752 --> 01:05:10,668
it would depend on
if the creator were ethical.

1155
01:05:10,669 --> 01:05:13,751
Okay. Could've said that
in a regular tone, but I get it.

1156
01:05:13,752 --> 01:05:14,836
Can you pass me that?

1157
01:05:15,961 --> 01:05:17,002
[sighs]

1158
01:05:19,377 --> 01:05:21,710
I can't.
My fingerprints will get all over it.

1159
01:05:21,711 --> 01:05:23,460
Who cares? Use gloves.

1160
01:05:23,461 --> 01:05:25,751
And the wind could blow
my hair follicles onto it.

1161
01:05:25,752 --> 01:05:27,377
What wind? Joe.

1162
01:05:30,044 --> 01:05:31,086
[sighs]

1163
01:05:33,669 --> 01:05:38,210
You spent millions on all of this,
and you haven't touched anything?

1164
01:05:38,211 --> 01:05:41,168
I've touched! How else would I have
brought everything into the bunker?

1165
01:05:41,169 --> 01:05:43,544
- Hold this. Hold this right now.
- I shouldn't.

1166
01:05:45,586 --> 01:05:48,376
I... [sighs] I shouldn't.

1167
01:05:48,377 --> 01:05:49,461
But it's so smooth.

1168
01:05:49,961 --> 01:05:51,211
Cold...

1169
01:05:51,961 --> 01:05:53,919
- and metal-y...
- Okay, okay.

1170
01:05:54,627 --> 01:05:56,377
[breathes deeply]

1171
01:06:00,836 --> 01:06:02,543
It is smooth and cold and metal-y.

1172
01:06:02,544 --> 01:06:04,419
Hmm. It feels good, don't it?

1173
01:06:05,252 --> 01:06:07,377
- What is this?
- It's an MRF.

1174
01:06:08,169 --> 01:06:10,376
- I used to drink those in college.
- [clicks tongue]

1175
01:06:10,377 --> 01:06:14,961
That's an AMF.
A MRF is a magnetic repulsion field.

1176
01:06:15,669 --> 01:06:18,168
- It's kinda plain, isn't it?
- "Plain"?

1177
01:06:18,169 --> 01:06:20,668
Yeah, I mean,
shouldn't it have, like, more flair?

1178
01:06:20,669 --> 01:06:23,461
- Not you giving me style tips.
- Just saying.

1179
01:06:24,419 --> 01:06:26,626
Where's your arc reactor?
That's, like, the...

1180
01:06:26,627 --> 01:06:28,960
You know, they don't
exactly hand those out.

1181
01:06:28,961 --> 01:06:31,544
- Mine is solar and wind powered.
- [phone vibrates]

1182
01:06:33,877 --> 01:06:34,919
Damn.

1183
01:06:36,502 --> 01:06:37,502
I gotta go.

1184
01:06:38,669 --> 01:06:39,752
[controller chimes]

1185
01:06:43,377 --> 01:06:45,961
[♪ R&B pop music playing,
Chaka Khan "Ain't Nobody"]

1186
01:06:52,211 --> 01:06:53,211
Deuces.

1187
01:06:53,752 --> 01:06:55,127
[suit powering up]

1188
01:07:00,336 --> 01:07:02,752
<i>♪ Oh, oh, oh, oh ♪</i>

1189
01:07:03,252 --> 01:07:05,460
<i>- ♪ Ain't nobody ♪
- ♪ Nobody ♪</i>

1190
01:07:05,461 --> 01:07:07,835
<i>- ♪ Loves me better ♪
- ♪ Loves me better ♪</i>

1191
01:07:07,836 --> 01:07:09,419
<i>♪ Makes me happy ♪</i>

1192
01:07:10,336 --> 01:07:12,460
<i>- ♪ Makes me feel this way ♪
- ♪ Nobody ♪</i>

1193
01:07:12,461 --> 01:07:14,793
<i>- ♪ Ain't nobody ♪
- ♪ Ain't nobody ♪</i>

1194
01:07:14,794 --> 01:07:16,418
<i>♪ Loves me better ♪</i>

1195
01:07:16,419 --> 01:07:17,627
[vocalizing]

1196
01:07:23,252 --> 01:07:24,752
[grunting]

1197
01:07:25,836 --> 01:07:28,293
- [explosive trills]
<i>- ♪ I wait for nighttime to come ♪</i>

1198
01:07:28,294 --> 01:07:29,919
<i>♪ And bring you to me ♪</i>

1199
01:07:31,127 --> 01:07:35,376
<i>♪ I can't believe I'm the one
I was so lonely ♪</i>

1200
01:07:35,377 --> 01:07:39,419
<i>♪ I feel like no one could feel
I must be dreamin' ♪</i>

1201
01:07:40,127 --> 01:07:44,461
<i>♪ I want this dream to be real
I need this feelin' ♪</i>

1202
01:07:45,919 --> 01:07:48,502
- [Riri] What's good, Clown?
- Mm-hmm.

1203
01:07:51,586 --> 01:07:52,585
[grunts]

1204
01:07:52,586 --> 01:07:53,918
<i>♪ Oh, oh ♪</i>

1205
01:07:53,919 --> 01:07:56,210
<i>- ♪ Ain't nobody ♪
- ♪ Nobody ♪</i>

1206
01:07:56,211 --> 01:07:58,002
<i>♪ Loves me better ♪</i>

1207
01:07:58,544 --> 01:08:01,043
- [Riri] Slug... I'm in.
- [chuckles]

1208
01:08:01,044 --> 01:08:03,043
<i>♪ Makes me feel this way ♪</i>

1209
01:08:03,044 --> 01:08:05,376
<i>- ♪ Ain't nobody ♪
- ♪ Nobody, baby ♪</i>

1210
01:08:05,377 --> 01:08:07,710
<i>♪ Loves me better ♪</i>

1211
01:08:07,711 --> 01:08:09,001
<i>♪ Ain't nobody ♪</i>

1212
01:08:09,002 --> 01:08:10,126
[grunting]

1213
01:08:10,127 --> 01:08:12,001
<i>♪ Loves me better than you ♪</i>

1214
01:08:12,002 --> 01:08:13,086
[groans]

1215
01:08:14,002 --> 01:08:16,586
<i>♪ At first, you put your arms around me ♪</i>

1216
01:08:18,086 --> 01:08:20,501
<i>♪ Then you put your charms around me ♪</i>

1217
01:08:20,502 --> 01:08:21,586
[grunts]

1218
01:08:23,169 --> 01:08:25,626
<i>♪ I can't resist this sweet surrender ♪</i>

1219
01:08:25,627 --> 01:08:27,376
[both grunting]

1220
01:08:27,377 --> 01:08:30,461
<i>♪ Oh, my nights are warm and tender ♪</i>

1221
01:08:32,419 --> 01:08:35,044
<i>♪ We stare into each other's eyes ♪</i>

1222
01:08:36,919 --> 01:08:37,918
<i>♪ And what we see ♪</i>

1223
01:08:37,919 --> 01:08:39,001
[guard groans]

1224
01:08:39,002 --> 01:08:40,086
<i>♪ Is no surprise ♪</i>

1225
01:08:41,711 --> 01:08:43,126
<i>♪ Got a feeling most... ♪</i>

1226
01:08:43,127 --> 01:08:45,126
- Hey, girl, how's the heist going?
- [yelps]

1227
01:08:45,127 --> 01:08:46,669
[Riri grunting]

1228
01:08:52,044 --> 01:08:54,377
[grunts] Shit! The drive!

1229
01:08:55,544 --> 01:08:58,627
- Oh, my bad. Did I scare you again?
- Be quiet. They'll hear you.

1230
01:08:59,211 --> 01:09:01,251
Chill. I put us on our own channel.

1231
01:09:01,252 --> 01:09:02,960
[keyboard clacking]

1232
01:09:02,961 --> 01:09:04,877
[Slug] Wait a minute.
I lost comms with Riri.

1233
01:09:05,377 --> 01:09:07,211
Roll call. You there? Hello?

1234
01:09:08,002 --> 01:09:10,918
- [Riri] How did you even get out?
- Jailbreak. There's a wireless connection

1235
01:09:10,919 --> 01:09:13,960
between me and the suit. I just
had to figure out how to tap into it.

1236
01:09:13,961 --> 01:09:16,501
Well, you and your jailbreak
just made me drop the hard drive

1237
01:09:16,502 --> 01:09:18,669
with Slug's virus, and now I'm screwed.

1238
01:09:19,836 --> 01:09:21,001
- I can fix it.
- How?

1239
01:09:21,002 --> 01:09:22,668
There's another way
to shut down the system.

1240
01:09:22,669 --> 01:09:24,626
- How?
- [Natalie] First, turn off your MRF

1241
01:09:24,627 --> 01:09:27,501
so you can magnetize yourself
to one of these platforms.

1242
01:09:27,502 --> 01:09:29,960
The MRF is the only thing
keeping me from death.

1243
01:09:29,961 --> 01:09:31,835
Don't worry, Ri. I got you.

1244
01:09:31,836 --> 01:09:33,377
[Riri] You better not get me killed.

1245
01:09:34,086 --> 01:09:36,293
- We got a problem.
- What's up? What happened?

1246
01:09:36,294 --> 01:09:39,460
[Slug] Riri must've lost the drive.
It's not in the tunnel anymore.

1247
01:09:39,461 --> 01:09:41,793
Damn it. Parker can't
hold his breath all night.

1248
01:09:41,794 --> 01:09:43,251
Can you get back on with Riri?

1249
01:09:43,252 --> 01:09:45,793
Of course I can.
It's just gonna take a minute, Zaddy.

1250
01:09:45,794 --> 01:09:47,044
We don't have a minute.

1251
01:09:48,377 --> 01:09:50,419
[Natalie]
Oh, man,
this is just like <i>Spy Kids.</i>

1252
01:09:54,294 --> 01:09:56,918
Okay, I'm stuck. What's next, Nat?

1253
01:09:56,919 --> 01:10:00,085
All right. Each platform is connected
to the security mainframe

1254
01:10:00,086 --> 01:10:01,460
in case of an emergency,

1255
01:10:01,461 --> 01:10:03,793
so if we can dislodge the car
from its platform,

1256
01:10:03,794 --> 01:10:04,876
the firewalls will drop,

1257
01:10:04,877 --> 01:10:07,460
- and Slug will be able to get in.
- Looks like I'm under an Impala,

1258
01:10:07,461 --> 01:10:10,085
which means six speed
automatic transmission.

1259
01:10:10,086 --> 01:10:12,586
- Let me see the undercarriage.
- [digital beeping]

1260
01:10:15,377 --> 01:10:17,710
So don't wanna freak you out,
but we're, like, five miles away

1261
01:10:17,711 --> 01:10:19,586
- from the weigh station.
- Which means?

1262
01:10:22,044 --> 01:10:24,127
You about to get crushed like a pop can.

1263
01:10:26,127 --> 01:10:28,001
- Yo, Slug.
- [Slug] <i>Ooh, girl,</i>

1264
01:10:28,002 --> 01:10:29,335
<i>we thought you was dead.</i>

1265
01:10:29,336 --> 01:10:31,335
<i>- Where's the drive?</i>
- About that. It fell.

1266
01:10:31,336 --> 01:10:32,918
New plan.
When I give you the signal,

1267
01:10:32,919 --> 01:10:34,918
<i>you're gonna have about
two-and-a-half seconds</i>

1268
01:10:34,919 --> 01:10:37,460
<i>to switch the system over
while it reboots.</i>

1269
01:10:37,461 --> 01:10:39,876
<i>- I'm gonna trigger an emergency override.</i>
- We don't do improv.

1270
01:10:39,877 --> 01:10:41,002
Too late.

1271
01:10:42,961 --> 01:10:44,335
[Natalie] Ew. Looks like Thing.

1272
01:10:44,336 --> 01:10:47,126
[Riri] Yeah, well, Thing better work.
Otherwise, I'mma end up in jail.

1273
01:10:47,127 --> 01:10:49,543
[Natalie] The weight of the lift
will probably kill you

1274
01:10:49,544 --> 01:10:52,126
- before that ever happens.
- [Riri] What happened to "I got you, Ri"?

1275
01:10:52,127 --> 01:10:54,836
[Natalie] Well, I do got you,
but you movin' kinda slow.

1276
01:10:59,211 --> 01:11:01,752
[Slug, impatiently] <i>Ms. Riri, I'm waiting.</i>

1277
01:11:02,711 --> 01:11:05,877
- [Natalie] Little to the left.
- [Riri] I don't need you backseat driving.

1278
01:11:10,586 --> 01:11:13,877
- We don't have all day.
- [Riri] I'm almost there.

1279
01:11:14,419 --> 01:11:16,169
[John] <i>Parker's runnin' out of time.</i>

1280
01:11:17,377 --> 01:11:18,752
[creaks]

1281
01:11:22,502 --> 01:11:24,127
Slug, it's down. Quickly.

1282
01:11:34,294 --> 01:11:36,294
[breathing heavily]

1283
01:11:37,711 --> 01:11:38,877
[chuckles]

1284
01:11:45,377 --> 01:11:46,627
[alarm blaring]

1285
01:11:47,169 --> 01:11:49,002
[breathing heavily] What's going on?

1286
01:11:50,211 --> 01:11:51,711
[breathes deeply]

1287
01:11:53,211 --> 01:11:54,211
[gasps]

1288
01:11:56,419 --> 01:11:59,627
My very talented team
just hijacked your system,

1289
01:12:00,544 --> 01:12:02,961
so now, technically, I control TNNL.

1290
01:12:03,544 --> 01:12:05,543
But we have to make it official, still.

1291
01:12:05,544 --> 01:12:07,419
[Sheila's breath shuddering]

1292
01:12:10,336 --> 01:12:13,668
[The Hood] This contract states that
you will agree to put me and my associates

1293
01:12:13,669 --> 01:12:14,876
on TNNL's payroll.

1294
01:12:14,877 --> 01:12:17,210
Six-figure salaries, benefits,

1295
01:12:17,211 --> 01:12:19,418
free access
to the highway, of course.

1296
01:12:19,419 --> 01:12:22,169
And equity in the company
as an anonymous co-owner.

1297
01:12:23,044 --> 01:12:25,169
So, ready to sign?

1298
01:12:27,669 --> 01:12:28,752
[gasps]

1299
01:12:32,336 --> 01:12:35,501
Now, if you wanna take back control,
just sign an initial there.

1300
01:12:35,502 --> 01:12:40,752
Unless you want your investors to have
a front-row seat to the encore.

1301
01:12:50,211 --> 01:12:53,251
All right. She signed.
We can clock out.

1302
01:12:53,252 --> 01:12:55,502
- Everybody head to Kinzie.
- [guards groaning]

1303
01:12:57,044 --> 01:12:59,502
- Pleasure doing business with you.
- [guard coughs]

1304
01:13:01,044 --> 01:13:02,836
See y'all at the holiday party.

1305
01:13:09,836 --> 01:13:11,168
[exclaims]

1306
01:13:11,169 --> 01:13:14,668
- Bruh.
- Bruh.

1307
01:13:14,669 --> 01:13:16,211
[guard] Freeze!

1308
01:13:16,836 --> 01:13:18,835
- Hands up.
- Natalie, close the helmet.

1309
01:13:18,836 --> 01:13:21,293
Now's not the time to start glitching.
Snap out of it, N.A.T.

1310
01:13:21,294 --> 01:13:23,044
- What is she doing?
- Hey, man.

1311
01:13:23,669 --> 01:13:25,668
- [guard] Ma'am?
- The whole thing is over. Just...

1312
01:13:25,669 --> 01:13:27,876
- [guard] What the hell?
- Just put the gun down.

1313
01:13:27,877 --> 01:13:30,376
- [guard] Make it stop.
- Natalie, what's going on?

1314
01:13:30,377 --> 01:13:32,543
- N.A.T.A.L.I.E., what's--
- I need you to put your hands up.

1315
01:13:32,544 --> 01:13:35,210
- Come on, man. There's no need for that.
- On the ground!

1316
01:13:35,211 --> 01:13:36,835
- Close the helmet, N.A.T.
- On the ground!

1317
01:13:36,836 --> 01:13:38,127
N.A.T.A.L.I.E., close the helmet!

1318
01:13:40,169 --> 01:13:41,751
N.A.T.A.L.I.E., give me control
of the suit!

1319
01:13:41,752 --> 01:13:43,877
- Get down or I'll shoot!
- [gunshot]

1320
01:13:51,002 --> 01:13:52,668
- [grunts]
- [body thuds]

1321
01:13:52,669 --> 01:13:54,377
[heart thumping]

1322
01:13:58,294 --> 01:13:59,336
[gasps]

1323
01:14:00,836 --> 01:14:02,586
[guard groaning]

1324
01:14:06,211 --> 01:14:07,211
You good?

1325
01:14:08,419 --> 01:14:11,211
Yeah, I... think.

1326
01:14:15,419 --> 01:14:18,002
[The Hood] Hey, don't worry about him.
He'll be fine.

1327
01:14:18,586 --> 01:14:19,627
Come on. Let's go.

1328
01:14:21,461 --> 01:14:23,626
[♪ rap song playing,
Lupe Fiasco "Kick, Push II"]

1329
01:14:23,627 --> 01:14:25,251
<i>♪ You know what it is... ♪</i>

1330
01:14:25,252 --> 01:14:26,335
[all laughing]

1331
01:14:26,336 --> 01:14:28,543
[Roz] I'd punch you
in the head dead straight.

1332
01:14:28,544 --> 01:14:30,168
[John] You didn't have the strength.

1333
01:14:30,169 --> 01:14:31,752
[Roz] Punch me in my head dead straight.

1334
01:14:33,419 --> 01:14:35,752
Yo, Ri, why you mad?

1335
01:14:36,336 --> 01:14:40,835
It's a party 'cause of you.
We are freakin' rich!

1336
01:14:40,836 --> 01:14:42,877
But somebody almost died.

1337
01:14:43,669 --> 01:14:45,877
The security guard? Yo, he's fine.

1338
01:14:46,752 --> 01:14:47,752
Let me ask you...

1339
01:14:49,919 --> 01:14:51,461
What do you know about Parker?

1340
01:14:52,044 --> 01:14:53,627
What d'you know about his hood?

1341
01:14:54,211 --> 01:14:57,960
Well, I heard he jacked it
from coat check at Bottom Lounge.

1342
01:14:57,961 --> 01:15:01,460
Then somebody else was saying that
he, like, wrestled it off a demon.

1343
01:15:01,461 --> 01:15:04,335
But, you know, I think it's just,
like, vintage Hermès.

1344
01:15:04,336 --> 01:15:07,086
You heard anything else weird about him?

1345
01:15:08,211 --> 01:15:12,126
Okay, one time
I saw Parker shirtless. [chuckling]

1346
01:15:12,127 --> 01:15:14,752
Fine as hell. [coughs]

1347
01:15:15,377 --> 01:15:18,210
But scales everywhere.

1348
01:15:18,211 --> 01:15:20,419
I don't think
he's a lizard person, but...

1349
01:15:21,252 --> 01:15:23,710
he could still get it.
You know what I'm saying?

1350
01:15:23,711 --> 01:15:25,210
What do you mean by "scales"?

1351
01:15:25,211 --> 01:15:26,294
Hey.

1352
01:15:27,044 --> 01:15:28,626
- Here you go.
- [sighs]

1353
01:15:28,627 --> 01:15:30,961
You know, you ask
a lot of questions, Riri. [chuckles]

1354
01:15:31,961 --> 01:15:33,668
Sometimes it's better
to keep 'em to yourself.

1355
01:15:33,669 --> 01:15:36,168
- [glass clinking]
- [Parker] Yo!

1356
01:15:36,169 --> 01:15:37,419
Everybody, bring it in.

1357
01:15:38,127 --> 01:15:39,836
Riri, get over here.

1358
01:15:44,502 --> 01:15:45,502
You know what?

1359
01:15:46,586 --> 01:15:51,877
This might be the prettiest group
of washed-up criminals I ever saw.

1360
01:15:52,502 --> 01:15:53,626
- [John scoffs]
- [Roz] Mmm-hmm.

1361
01:15:53,627 --> 01:15:54,710
- All right.
- [all chuckling]

1362
01:15:54,711 --> 01:15:55,794
[John] Uh-huh.

1363
01:15:57,544 --> 01:15:59,419
[Parker] I've been on my own
since I was a kid.

1364
01:16:00,961 --> 01:16:04,002
If John hadn't found me,
I wouldn't be here.

1365
01:16:09,169 --> 01:16:12,294
Feeling that powerless,
it does something to you.

1366
01:16:14,836 --> 01:16:16,586
Every bruise you take for this team.

1367
01:16:17,419 --> 01:16:18,669
Every line of code.

1368
01:16:19,294 --> 01:16:23,919
Every job you plan with me,
with this group, means something real.

1369
01:16:24,919 --> 01:16:27,044
You've lived your lives
waiting to be seen.

1370
01:16:27,752 --> 01:16:30,127
Waiting to be acknowledged
for your greatness. Well...

1371
01:16:31,086 --> 01:16:32,086
I see you.

1372
01:16:34,586 --> 01:16:36,710
But the money above us
will never notice our brilliance

1373
01:16:36,711 --> 01:16:37,877
unless we force them.

1374
01:16:38,627 --> 01:16:42,336
And after what we pulled at TNNL,
these suckers are listening.

1375
01:16:43,627 --> 01:16:44,752
And they're terrified.

1376
01:16:47,169 --> 01:16:48,376
But I don't give a shit.

1377
01:16:48,377 --> 01:16:49,794
[all chuckle]

1378
01:16:51,627 --> 01:16:53,252
About anyone but y'all.

1379
01:16:55,627 --> 01:16:58,501
So... here's to you.

1380
01:16:58,502 --> 01:16:59,586
[Roz] Cheers.

1381
01:17:00,377 --> 01:17:03,376
Cheers, y'all. Cheers.
I love you. I love you.

1382
01:17:03,377 --> 01:17:04,919
[all exclaiming and laughing]

1383
01:17:05,544 --> 01:17:08,086
- [Jeri and Slug] Money.
- [Clown laughing] Money.

1384
01:17:18,877 --> 01:17:20,877
[♪ captivating music playing]

1385
01:17:24,919 --> 01:17:26,294
[controller chimes]

1386
01:17:49,711 --> 01:17:50,711
Hey.

1387
01:17:51,711 --> 01:17:52,711
Hey.

1388
01:17:53,919 --> 01:17:56,461
- I'm sorry about earlier.
- [Riri] It's okay.

1389
01:17:57,752 --> 01:17:59,668
What happened? Where were you?

1390
01:17:59,669 --> 01:18:02,961
I saw the gun and I froze.
I don't know why.

1391
01:18:03,544 --> 01:18:05,293
What do you remember about that night?

1392
01:18:05,294 --> 01:18:09,127
I remember hearing Gary
yelling for us to get down.

1393
01:18:10,544 --> 01:18:12,627
I think I maybe closed my eyes?

1394
01:18:13,336 --> 01:18:15,960
I don't know.
We can come back to that later, Ri.

1395
01:18:15,961 --> 01:18:18,086
Right now, I need to talk to you
about Parker.

1396
01:18:19,294 --> 01:18:23,293
Earlier today, by the tunnel,
I sensed some crazy energy

1397
01:18:23,294 --> 01:18:24,626
radiating off Parker.

1398
01:18:24,627 --> 01:18:26,751
I tried to analyze it, but I couldn't.

1399
01:18:26,752 --> 01:18:29,960
I don't know what it is,
but it ain't from around here.

1400
01:18:29,961 --> 01:18:31,044
So?

1401
01:18:33,044 --> 01:18:38,543
We wake up to aliens, androids,
wizards on our timeline every other day.

1402
01:18:38,544 --> 01:18:41,918
I'm more concerned
with how my AI is having panic attacks.

1403
01:18:41,919 --> 01:18:45,044
Riri, I'm being serious.

1404
01:18:46,127 --> 01:18:49,210
Hey, I think Parker's wrapped up
in some sketchy shit.

1405
01:18:49,211 --> 01:18:53,043
- That doesn't bother you?
- I know Parker is sus,

1406
01:18:53,044 --> 01:18:54,626
but this is an in and out job.

1407
01:18:54,627 --> 01:18:57,794
If you wanna keep playing <i>Spy Kids,</i>
you gotta have my back.

1408
01:19:00,044 --> 01:19:01,294
Are you saying I can stay?

1409
01:19:02,877 --> 01:19:04,044
- [gasps]
- For now.

1410
01:19:04,711 --> 01:19:07,086
- [laughing]
- [phone vibrating]

1411
01:19:08,752 --> 01:19:11,461
- [gasps]
- Damn it, I forgot about the show.

1412
01:19:13,002 --> 01:19:14,377
I have to take you with me.

1413
01:19:17,002 --> 01:19:21,376
- No. [scoffs] Don't make an excited face.
- [chuckles] Come on.

1414
01:19:21,377 --> 01:19:23,626
Do you not remember
the number one rule?

1415
01:19:23,627 --> 01:19:26,544
Yes, yes, I got it. Stay hidden.

1416
01:19:28,002 --> 01:19:30,211
[♪ hip-hop rap music playing,
Saba "Fearmonger"]

1417
01:19:37,961 --> 01:19:40,460
<i>♪ Okay, the money on the way
It'll lay by the first ♪</i>

1418
01:19:40,461 --> 01:19:43,126
