2607
02:27:16,615 --> 02:27:19,698
I wanna make sure we're perfect
on our next job.

2608
02:27:20,323 --> 02:27:21,864
We stick with the plan.

2609
02:27:21,865 --> 02:27:22,948
Continue your work.

2610
02:27:23,782 --> 02:27:24,782
All right.

2611
02:27:31,240 --> 02:27:34,157
Uh, Parker, you got anything for me?

2612
02:27:39,948 --> 02:27:40,948
Yeah...

2613
02:27:42,240 --> 02:27:43,240
I got plans for you.

2614
02:27:48,365 --> 02:27:49,365
Okay.

2615
02:27:51,698 --> 02:27:53,073
You just let me know, then.

2616
02:28:00,907 --> 02:28:03,365
- [shop bell dings]
- [♪ suspenseful music playing]

2617
02:28:08,240 --> 02:28:11,365
[♪ rap music plays] <i>♪ I fell from the sky
without a parachute ♪</i>

2618
02:28:11,948 --> 02:28:14,073
<i>♪ Baby, this is game
I'mma shoot at you ♪</i>

2619
02:28:14,782 --> 02:28:17,822
<i>♪ Look up and look around
It's going down ♪</i>

2620
02:28:17,823 --> 02:28:20,365
<i>♪ Say she call me King
I'mma wear the crown ♪</i>

2621
02:28:21,782 --> 02:28:22,907
[Natalie] Riri?

2622
02:28:25,615 --> 02:28:26,615
Riri?

2623
02:28:28,782 --> 02:28:29,782
Riri--

2624
02:28:30,990 --> 02:28:32,323
Riri! Hello!

2625
02:28:33,323 --> 02:28:34,906
Inside voices, please.

2626
02:28:34,907 --> 02:28:37,239
I've been trying to get your attention
for a whole minute.

2627
02:28:37,240 --> 02:28:38,489
What's up?

2628
02:28:38,490 --> 02:28:42,781
This creepy piece of fabric
that you jacked from Parker's cloak?

2629
02:28:42,782 --> 02:28:43,865
Find anything yet?

2630
02:28:44,407 --> 02:28:46,322
[Riri] It looks like internal combustion.

2631
02:28:46,323 --> 02:28:48,072
You know, like a heat engine?

2632
02:28:48,073 --> 02:28:50,615
Powers its host. Or in this case, Parker.

2633
02:28:51,407 --> 02:28:54,406
Okay, so we know where all the energy
goes, but where does it come from?

2634
02:28:54,407 --> 02:28:56,657
Huh, according to my analysis, nowhere.

2635
02:28:57,198 --> 02:29:00,865
I've cross-referenced this heat signature
with every known energy source.

2636
02:29:01,448 --> 02:29:05,072
Wakandan. Kree, Stark, Pym.
And I got nothing.

2637
02:29:05,073 --> 02:29:09,697
But that's impossible.
Energy doesn't just pop up outta nowhere.

2638
02:29:09,698 --> 02:29:12,239
It defies laws and physics.

2639
02:29:12,240 --> 02:29:15,532
And to be honest, I don't know how much
more Parker's body can take before...

2640
02:29:17,573 --> 02:29:19,322
He was acting so weird this morning.

2641
02:29:19,323 --> 02:29:22,406
- You're being paranoid.
- Yeah, it's more than that, okay?

2642
02:29:22,407 --> 02:29:23,989
I know he's plotting something.

2643
02:29:23,990 --> 02:29:26,447
I need to understand his powers,
so I can fight back

2644
02:29:26,448 --> 02:29:28,281
when he inevitably comes for me.

2645
02:29:28,282 --> 02:29:29,448
[Ronnie] Riri?

2646
02:29:30,365 --> 02:29:32,114
Incoming. Lock the door.

2647
02:29:32,115 --> 02:29:35,615
You know, my mama don't believe
in locked doors unless you pay bills.

2648
02:29:38,407 --> 02:29:39,407
[door opens]

2649
02:29:40,615 --> 02:29:42,072
[Ronnie] What are you two up to?

2650
02:29:42,073 --> 02:29:44,031
- [both] Nothing.
- [Ronnie] Uh-huh.

2651
02:29:44,032 --> 02:29:46,740
I came to see if you need to come clean.

2652
02:29:48,490 --> 02:29:50,697
- "Come clean"?
- [♪ uneasy music playing]

2653
02:29:50,698 --> 02:29:52,365
Come clean about what?

2654
02:29:52,948 --> 02:29:55,906
I said, if you need anything cleaned,
I'm on my way to the laundromat.

2655
02:29:55,907 --> 02:29:59,239
Oh. Right. Nah, I'm... I'm good.

2656
02:29:59,240 --> 02:30:00,323
Riri...

2657
02:30:00,948 --> 02:30:03,239
is there something
you need to talk about?

2658
02:30:03,240 --> 02:30:04,322
What do you mean?

2659
02:30:04,323 --> 02:30:08,739
Well, ever since you started this new job,
you've been coming home late,

2660
02:30:08,740 --> 02:30:10,197
buying expensive gifts.

2661
02:30:10,198 --> 02:30:13,157
And we haven't even talked
about your dead coworker.

2662
02:30:13,948 --> 02:30:15,489
[softly] You know about that?

2663
02:30:15,490 --> 02:30:17,865
The police told us, when they were here.

2664
02:30:19,823 --> 02:30:21,531
- Right.
- [softly] Right.

2665
02:30:21,532 --> 02:30:22,615
Right.

2666
02:30:26,698 --> 02:30:31,198
Okay. Well, call me if you need
anything while I'm out, okay?

2667
02:30:32,865 --> 02:30:33,865
Will do.

2668
02:30:35,198 --> 02:30:36,615
Okay. Bye.

2669
02:30:47,698 --> 02:30:49,323
[♪ ominous music playing]

2670
02:30:49,865 --> 02:30:51,365
[Natalie] Where did it go?

2671
02:30:51,948 --> 02:30:53,073
Oh, no. He's here.

2672
02:30:54,032 --> 02:30:55,740
We gotta get Mom out of the house.

2673
02:30:57,157 --> 02:30:59,781
[Natalie] Oh, wait, wait!
Wait! It's back!

2674
02:30:59,782 --> 02:31:03,365
Okay. See? We're good.

2675
02:31:05,323 --> 02:31:06,407
How can you say that?

2676
02:31:09,532 --> 02:31:10,907
Why are you acting so calm?

2677
02:31:12,032 --> 02:31:14,447
Like I didn't just let John die.

2678
02:31:14,448 --> 02:31:16,447
You did what you had to do to survive.

2679
02:31:16,448 --> 02:31:18,906
John would've done the same. Okay?

2680
02:31:18,907 --> 02:31:21,239
- [scoffs]
- As he said. Listen! Ri!

2681
02:31:21,240 --> 02:31:24,614
You need to focus
on understanding Parker's hood.

2682
02:31:24,615 --> 02:31:28,531
Stressing over an act of self-defense
is going to get you killed.

2683
02:31:28,532 --> 02:31:31,323
I don't even know what to do.

2684
02:31:32,198 --> 02:31:34,989
- Call Shuri. Maybe she can help.
- Call her?

2685
02:31:34,990 --> 02:31:36,073
Okay.

2686
02:31:37,115 --> 02:31:40,823
"Uh, hello?
Yeah! Shuri! What's--

2687
02:31:41,490 --> 02:31:44,864
"Oh, what have I been up to?
Since causing an interspecies war

2688
02:31:44,865 --> 02:31:46,906
"on both land and sea?

2689
02:31:46,907 --> 02:31:50,697
"Um, well, I got kicked outta MIT.

2690
02:31:50,698 --> 02:31:54,031
"I joined a crew
of ragged-ass criminals, and--

2691
02:31:54,032 --> 02:31:57,489
"Oh, now I'm about to get my ass popped
by a deranged man in a cape.

2692
02:31:57,490 --> 02:31:58,573
"Can you help?

2693
02:32:00,448 --> 02:32:01,448
"Hello?

2694
02:32:01,990 --> 02:32:04,115
"Hello, Sh-- Shuri?"

2695
02:32:05,907 --> 02:32:06,907
She hung up.

2696
02:32:07,657 --> 02:32:10,781
- When you say it like that--
- Have you heard anything from Joe yet?

2697
02:32:10,782 --> 02:32:12,489
He's gotta have some ideas.

2698
02:32:12,490 --> 02:32:15,740
No. I keep getting his voicemail.
Do you want me to keep trying?

2699
02:32:16,365 --> 02:32:17,365
That's weird.

2700
02:32:18,490 --> 02:32:19,489
Nah, it's fine.

2701
02:32:19,490 --> 02:32:22,197
I'll just go see him in person.
Gotta go tell him

2702
02:32:22,198 --> 02:32:23,989
- about his bio-mesh, anyways.
- [door closes]

2703
02:32:23,990 --> 02:32:26,073
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

2704
02:32:40,782 --> 02:32:42,364
- Excuse me.
- Mm-hmm?

2705
02:32:42,365 --> 02:32:44,864
You wouldn't happen to know
why Joe's house is surrounded

2706
02:32:44,865 --> 02:32:46,281
in police tape, would you?

2707
02:32:46,282 --> 02:32:47,906
[sighs] Joe.

2708
02:32:47,907 --> 02:32:50,114
You mean Ezekiel Stane?

2709
02:32:50,115 --> 02:32:52,614
Yeah. Cops came and got him this morning.

2710
02:32:52,615 --> 02:32:54,490
What? Why?

2711
02:32:55,407 --> 02:32:59,073
Well, for one thing, have you seen what
he's done to my Black-eyed Susans?

2712
02:33:00,240 --> 02:33:03,281
This is a beautiful neighborhood.
Although, if something were to happen,

2713
02:33:03,282 --> 02:33:05,239
I could've told you
it would've come from that house.

2714
02:33:05,240 --> 02:33:07,114
{\an8}<i>The evidence found
at the Heirlum crime scene</i>

2715
02:33:07,115 --> 02:33:11,157
{\an8}<i>has been traced back
to Ezekiel Stane of Evanston, Illinois.</i>

2716
02:33:11,698 --> 02:33:15,781
{\an8}<i>Again, this is a very active scene
that is very quickly evolving.</i>

2717
02:33:15,782 --> 02:33:18,156
<i>Ezekiel Stane,
who legally changed his name</i>

2718
02:33:18,157 --> 02:33:22,739
<i>to Joe McGillicuddy,
is the son of the late Obadiah Stane.</i>

2719
02:33:22,740 --> 02:33:28,531
<i>Obadiah was fondly remembered
as the former COO of Stark Industries,</i>

2720
02:33:28,532 --> 02:33:31,989
<i>who tragically died in a plane crash
more than 15 years ago.</i>

2721
02:33:31,990 --> 02:33:36,614
{\an8}<i>So, this is devastating, and the community
in this area simply cannot believe it.</i>

2722
02:33:36,615 --> 02:33:38,864
- You're up, Stane.
- [door buzzes]

2723
02:33:38,865 --> 02:33:41,239
[reporter 1] <i>Stane faces
a multitude of charges,</i>

2724
02:33:41,240 --> 02:33:44,197
<i>including illegal possession
of bionic technology</i>

2725
02:33:44,198 --> 02:33:45,781
<i>and domestic terrorism.</i>

2726
02:33:45,782 --> 02:33:48,947
[reporter 2] <i>It's really unfortunate
what this scandal is doing</i>

2727
02:33:48,948 --> 02:33:50,197
<i>to the Stane family name.</i>

2728
02:33:50,198 --> 02:33:52,989
<i>I mean, Obadiah was a beloved man.</i>

2729
02:33:52,990 --> 02:33:57,822
<i>He was an inventor, philanthropist,
and mentor to the great Tony Stark.</i>

2730
02:33:57,823 --> 02:34:01,447
<i>May he also rest in peace.
I mean, poor Obadiah's gotta be</i>

2731
02:34:01,448 --> 02:34:03,031
<i>rolling in his grave over this.</i>

2732
02:34:03,032 --> 02:34:06,156
[reporter 1] <i>Looks like this bad apple
fell very far from the tree,</i>

2733
02:34:06,157 --> 02:34:09,115
<i>rolled down the hill,
and landed straight in the gutter.</i>

2734
02:34:09,865 --> 02:34:11,282
<i>Good one, Samantha.</i>

2735
02:34:11,782 --> 02:34:13,239
<i>- Thank you, Judy.
- Now here's--</i>

2736
02:34:13,240 --> 02:34:16,072
You know there's a whole Reddit thread
on Obadiah Stane sightings?

2737
02:34:16,073 --> 02:34:17,906
- Obadiah Stane's dead, bruh.
- Yeah.

2738
02:34:17,907 --> 02:34:19,447
Um, allegedly. No body.

2739
02:34:19,448 --> 02:34:22,614
Yeah. Well, that's because
it was all engulfed in flames.

2740
02:34:22,615 --> 02:34:25,406
Is anyone else wondering
how Ezekiel Stane's tech ended up

2741
02:34:25,407 --> 02:34:26,739
in the middle of our heist?

2742
02:34:26,740 --> 02:34:29,656
- No. Nobody's wondering that.
- Leave it alone, Clown.

2743
02:34:29,657 --> 02:34:31,447
This is the best thing
that could happen to us.

2744
02:34:31,448 --> 02:34:33,156
Somebody else is gonna take the fall.

2745
02:34:33,157 --> 02:34:36,406
I just feel bad.
That guy's not gonna survive prison.

2746
02:34:36,407 --> 02:34:38,740
[scoffs] You don't feel bad.
You have a crush.

2747
02:34:39,448 --> 02:34:40,572
No, I don't.

2748
02:34:40,573 --> 02:34:44,156
You know, you do kinda
give pen-pal-prison-wife vibes.

2749
02:34:44,157 --> 02:34:47,365
Y'all, I'm serious. Isn't it a little odd?

2750
02:34:48,032 --> 02:34:51,572
John's dead, some random bionic guy
is being framed for our work,

2751
02:34:51,573 --> 02:34:53,864
and now Hood's being weird.

2752
02:34:53,865 --> 02:34:56,114
[Jeri] Hood's not being weird,
he's grieving.

2753
02:34:56,115 --> 02:34:57,739
It's completely understandable.

2754
02:34:57,740 --> 02:34:59,781
Not everyone grieves
in the same way, Clown.

2755
02:34:59,782 --> 02:35:05,531
[Clown] It's not grief, okay?
We're here, and he's somewhere else.

2756
02:35:05,532 --> 02:35:07,448
[♪ ominous music playing]

2757
02:35:18,073 --> 02:35:19,240
[breathes heavily]

2758
02:35:20,240 --> 02:35:22,364
[reporter] <i>Thank you.
Yeah, reporting to you live.</i>

2759
02:35:22,365 --> 02:35:26,197
<i>This is a situation
nobody could have possibly imagined</i>

2760
02:35:26,198 --> 02:35:31,032
<i>as multiple bodies continue to be
identified at the Heirlum crime scene.</i>

2761
02:35:31,740 --> 02:35:33,322
<i>We have to ask the question,</i>

2762
02:35:33,323 --> 02:35:37,822
<i>"How did this tech prodigy become
a suspected murderer?"</i>

2763
02:35:37,823 --> 02:35:41,697
<i>Of course, we'll keep you updated
on this story as it develops.</i>

2764
02:35:41,698 --> 02:35:46,365
{\an8}<i>Stay tuned for the local traffic report,
and much more, right after this.</i>

2765
02:35:48,323 --> 02:35:49,740
[door buzzes, opens]

2766
02:35:50,907 --> 02:35:51,907
Hey.

2767
02:35:54,198 --> 02:35:55,823
Looks like they got
your favorite color.

2768
02:35:57,948 --> 02:35:59,073
Khaki.

2769
02:36:09,865 --> 02:36:11,365
Look, I know you're mad at me.

2770
02:36:12,573 --> 02:36:14,198
And you have every right to be.

2771
02:36:18,365 --> 02:36:19,990
You're at a loss for words.

2772
02:36:21,698 --> 02:36:22,864
That makes two of us.

2773
02:36:22,865 --> 02:36:24,407
I'm gonna get you outta here.

2774
02:36:25,532 --> 02:36:26,865
Okay? I promise.

2775
02:36:27,657 --> 02:36:29,697
- Is that why you're here?
- Yes.

2776
02:36:29,698 --> 02:36:31,490
And how do you expect to do that?

2777
02:36:34,615 --> 02:36:35,907
[softly] I'm working on it.

2778
02:36:36,407 --> 02:36:37,573
Mm. [scoffs]

2779
02:36:38,448 --> 02:36:41,114
I should've known never to trust you.

2780
02:36:41,115 --> 02:36:43,906
You're just a selfish kid

2781
02:36:43,907 --> 02:36:46,447
who can't take
any responsibility for herself.

2782
02:36:46,448 --> 02:36:50,365
You lie, you cheat, you manipulate.

2783
02:36:50,907 --> 02:36:53,447
You'll do anything you can
to save yourself,

2784
02:36:53,448 --> 02:36:56,282
even if that means hurting
other people in the process.

2785
02:36:57,282 --> 02:36:59,657
- [breath shuddering]
- [♪ somber music playing]

2786
02:37:01,490 --> 02:37:03,407
Guard, I'm ready to go now, please.

2787
02:37:07,407 --> 02:37:08,698
[guard] All right, let's go.

2788
02:37:09,657 --> 02:37:10,907
[door buzzes, opens]

2789
02:37:12,240 --> 02:37:15,407
[♪ hip-hop music playing,
The Roots "Concerto of the Desperado"]

2790
02:37:30,407 --> 02:37:31,573
[Riri] What's going on?

2791
02:37:33,198 --> 02:37:34,615
Yo, Ri! Where you been?

2792
02:37:35,198 --> 02:37:37,365
Just up to my eyeballs.

2793
02:37:37,948 --> 02:37:41,365
Yo, it's a good thing Parker's getting
that new tech specialist to help out.

2794
02:37:42,740 --> 02:37:44,364
Another tech specialist?

2795
02:37:44,365 --> 02:37:46,448
Yeah, he didn't tell you? That's weird.

2796
02:37:46,948 --> 02:37:48,156
[Riri] Oh, right.

2797
02:37:48,157 --> 02:37:51,822
Yeah. Yes. Just... slipped my mind.

2798
02:37:51,823 --> 02:37:53,740
[♪ uneasy music playing]

2799
02:38:06,407 --> 02:38:07,740
[Parker] He's a friend of yours?

2800
02:38:09,282 --> 02:38:10,740
Why would you say that?

2801
02:38:11,323 --> 02:38:14,532
Nah, I just... I just assumed
everybody in tech knew each other.

2802
02:38:15,407 --> 02:38:18,114
I mean, we might have crossed paths.

2803
02:38:18,115 --> 02:38:19,532
You hate to see it, right?

2804
02:38:21,157 --> 02:38:24,032
Poor guy's probably gonna
rot in jail for our crimes.

2805
02:38:25,615 --> 02:38:28,739
- But, what a happy accident.
- [chuckles dryly]

2806
02:38:28,740 --> 02:38:30,740
Your outsourcing
really helped us, big time.

2807
02:38:32,115 --> 02:38:33,157
Outsourcing?

2808
02:38:33,740 --> 02:38:37,572
I just wish that, if you needed help,
Zeke Stane's or anyone else's,

2809
02:38:37,573 --> 02:38:38,990
you would have come to me.

2810
02:38:42,323 --> 02:38:43,323
But it's all good.

2811
02:38:45,115 --> 02:38:47,697
So, we'll bring someone in
to help pick up the slack.

2812
02:38:47,698 --> 02:38:49,364
Yeah, Clown mentioned that.

2813
02:38:49,365 --> 02:38:51,615
Here you go, Hood. It's all there.

2814
02:38:52,448 --> 02:38:53,448
[Parker] Thanks.

2815
02:38:58,448 --> 02:39:00,073
Hope you have a great day, Riri.

2816
02:39:01,615 --> 02:39:02,823
[Riri chuckles lightly]

2817
02:39:09,948 --> 02:39:12,698
- [♪ upbeat music playing on speakers]
- [camera whirring]

2818
02:39:16,282 --> 02:39:18,657
- [objects clattering]
- [dog barking in distance]

2819
02:39:20,865 --> 02:39:22,115
Ain't nobody there, girl.

2820
02:39:23,740 --> 02:39:25,531
Thought I heard something.

2821
02:39:25,532 --> 02:39:27,572
Okay. You're paranoid.

2822
02:39:27,573 --> 02:39:32,656
You just need to stop, for a second, okay?
Just stop and process and just be.

2823
02:39:32,657 --> 02:39:35,032
[scoffs] I'm sorry.

2824
02:39:35,907 --> 02:39:37,490
- "Just be"?
- Just be.

2825
02:39:39,032 --> 02:39:40,947
You know what?
If I didn't know any better,

2826
02:39:40,948 --> 02:39:43,031
I'd just say meditate,
but then you're gonna do

2827
02:39:43,032 --> 02:39:45,281
the whole rolling-the-eyes thing and...

2828
02:39:45,282 --> 02:39:46,448
There it is.

2829
02:39:49,115 --> 02:39:50,447
I'm finna go lay down.

2830
02:39:50,448 --> 02:39:52,073
Please get some rest, baby.

2831
02:39:53,115 --> 02:39:54,823
Oh, wait! I got something for you.

2832
02:40:01,740 --> 02:40:02,740
[Ronnie] Thank you.

2833
02:40:04,615 --> 02:40:05,615
You can put it on now.

2834
02:40:06,198 --> 02:40:08,407
- Why do I need a watch to go to bed?
- Just--

2835
02:40:09,490 --> 02:40:13,864
Don't take it off, for any reason.
Or at least not till I tell you to.

2836
02:40:13,865 --> 02:40:16,282
Riri, what is going on with you?

2837
02:40:16,823 --> 02:40:20,198
I promise I will explain everything later.

2838
02:40:21,907 --> 02:40:24,698
For now, I... I gotta get back to work.

2839
02:40:25,198 --> 02:40:26,490
So, can you...

2840
02:40:27,323 --> 02:40:29,282
Okay. Good night.

2841
02:40:30,990 --> 02:40:34,073
Thank you. Good night.

2842
02:40:35,240 --> 02:40:37,322
- [♪ music continues playing]
- What are you doing?

2843
02:40:37,323 --> 02:40:39,990
"What am I do--"
I'm shaking off my anxiety.

2844
02:40:40,823 --> 02:40:42,989
Hey! Where are we...
Where are we, um, headed?

2845
02:40:42,990 --> 02:40:44,907
I am gonna see Xavier.

2846
02:40:45,657 --> 02:40:48,197
What, just you?
You know I wanna see my brother.

2847
02:40:48,198 --> 02:40:51,447
- Come on.
- He's not your brother, okay?

2848
02:40:51,448 --> 02:40:53,197
You're just gonna freak him out.

2849
02:40:53,198 --> 02:40:55,865
And you remember how I reacted?
When you arrived?

2850
02:40:57,240 --> 02:40:58,281
Can't ambush him.

2851
02:40:58,282 --> 02:41:02,406
Okay. But just imagine
how pissed off he'll be once you tell him

2852
02:41:02,407 --> 02:41:05,281
- how long you've been hiding me from him.
- All right.

2853
02:41:05,282 --> 02:41:09,072
Just not now. Okay?
Can we just focus? Please?

2854
02:41:09,073 --> 02:41:12,072
On not getting got
by an invisible gunslinger

2855
02:41:12,073 --> 02:41:14,365
with magic bullets? Huh?

2856
02:41:15,573 --> 02:41:17,906
I'm gonna need you to put that suit back.

2857
02:41:17,907 --> 02:41:20,822
[♪ hip-hop music playing]
<i>♪ Make a whole lot of juice with that ♪</i>

2858
02:41:20,823 --> 02:41:22,531
<i>♪ Gettin' all these loop ♪</i>

2859
02:41:22,532 --> 02:41:24,115
<i>♪ Buy a brand new suit with that ♪</i>

2860
02:41:25,157 --> 02:41:26,739
[Riri] Wear it at all times.

2861
02:41:26,740 --> 02:41:30,447
Uh, thanks,
but I'm not much of a watch guy.

2862
02:41:30,448 --> 02:41:32,948
- It's not for fashion.
- Clearly.

2863
02:41:33,698 --> 02:41:35,240
Should I even bother asking why?

2864
02:41:35,740 --> 02:41:36,740
No.

2865
02:41:38,615 --> 02:41:39,615
Okay, weirdo.

2866
02:41:44,365 --> 02:41:46,115
Xa, do you think I'm a good person?

2867
02:41:52,240 --> 02:41:54,864
Never mind. Just forget I asked.

2868
02:41:54,865 --> 02:41:57,573
"Good." "Bad."
Them words don't really mean anything.

2869
02:41:59,323 --> 02:42:01,948
It's all depending on who's labeling you.

2870
02:42:03,698 --> 02:42:08,032
I guess, if you were asking me
to describe you as a person...

2871
02:42:09,532 --> 02:42:11,365
I'd say you're a smart person.

2872
02:42:12,365 --> 02:42:13,365
And a...

2873
02:42:14,490 --> 02:42:15,907
a hard-working person.

2874
02:42:17,740 --> 02:42:19,073
A protective person.

2875
02:42:21,823 --> 02:42:22,823
And a...

2876
02:42:25,657 --> 02:42:27,323
You're a complex person.

2877
02:42:29,323 --> 02:42:30,323
You're like...

2878
02:42:31,615 --> 02:42:32,906
[chuckles] Spock.

2879
02:42:32,907 --> 02:42:34,657
- "Spock"?
- Mm.

2880
02:42:35,573 --> 02:42:38,614
I always think of myself as Uhura but...

2881
02:42:38,615 --> 02:42:42,614
Please. The only thing y'all got
in common is that little complexion.

2882
02:42:42,615 --> 02:42:44,072
[Riri chuckles]

2883
02:42:44,073 --> 02:42:48,615
Now, look, all that being said,
you don't always let people in.

2884
02:42:50,448 --> 02:42:53,073
But I think underneath all that armor
is a soft heart.

2885
02:42:54,907 --> 02:42:59,447
So, with all that you are,
is "good" really a label you need?

2886
02:42:59,448 --> 02:43:01,157
[♪ gentle music playing]

2887
02:43:06,823 --> 02:43:09,448
Uh, gotta get back to work.

2888
02:43:10,907 --> 02:43:13,031
- Yeah.
- [clears throat] Thanks for the watch.

2889
02:43:13,032 --> 02:43:14,115
[Riri] Mm.

2890
02:43:32,907 --> 02:43:33,948
Finally!

2891
02:43:34,615 --> 02:43:35,615
You're back!

2892
02:43:36,532 --> 02:43:38,781
Come on, what happened?
Did y'all kiss?

2893
02:43:38,782 --> 02:43:41,614
Oh, my God. This does not seem
like the time to be making out.

2894
02:43:41,615 --> 02:43:45,739
[sighs] So, you're just gonna die?
Without having your first kiss, Ri?

2895
02:43:45,740 --> 02:43:47,282
You know the goal is to not die.

2896
02:43:47,865 --> 02:43:50,822
So, I need to start thinking
outside the box,

2897
02:43:50,823 --> 02:43:52,989
if I'm gonna protect us
from The Hood's magic.

2898
02:43:52,990 --> 02:43:54,657
Ri, you need to get some sleep.

2899
02:43:58,115 --> 02:43:59,698
Ri! Seriously.

2900
02:44:00,740 --> 02:44:01,740
For real.

2901
02:44:03,573 --> 02:44:05,364
Okay. Maybe just like

2902
02:44:05,365 --> 02:44:07,115
- 30 minutes.
- That's a start.

2903
02:44:08,532 --> 02:44:09,740
[breathing deeply]

2904
02:44:15,615 --> 02:44:16,615
[grunts softly]

2905
02:44:19,282 --> 02:44:21,282
[♪ suspenseful music building]

2906
02:44:22,698 --> 02:44:24,365
[clattering in distance]

2907
02:44:28,073 --> 02:44:29,073
[softly] Okay.

2908
02:44:43,448 --> 02:44:45,448
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

2909
02:45:06,032 --> 02:45:08,114
- [man, muffled] <i>Scully!</i>
- [mulled gunshots]

2910
02:45:08,115 --> 02:45:09,822
- [Ronnie] Riri!
- [Riri] Mom.

2911
02:45:09,823 --> 02:45:11,323
[♪ tense music playing]

2912
02:45:12,740 --> 02:45:13,907
What's wrong?

2913
02:45:14,407 --> 02:45:17,739
You tell me. One moment
I'm on the case with Scully,

2914
02:45:17,740 --> 02:45:21,198
and the next thing I know,
your watch decides to airbag me!

2915
02:45:21,948 --> 02:45:23,656
It must've heard the gunshots from the TV.

2916
02:45:23,657 --> 02:45:25,447
[Ronnie] Get me out of this thing.

2917
02:45:25,448 --> 02:45:26,782
[breathing heavily]

2918
02:45:28,823 --> 02:45:31,782
Riri? Are you okay?

2919
02:45:32,823 --> 02:45:34,406
You ready to talk to me?

2920
02:45:34,407 --> 02:45:36,406
- About what's going on?
- Ma, I'm fine.

2921
02:45:36,407 --> 02:45:39,156
Girl, you just busted down
my door like the Kool-Aid Man.

2922
02:45:39,157 --> 02:45:41,822
Because you screamed.
I thought you were in trouble.

2923
02:45:41,823 --> 02:45:46,614
Look at me.
I'm fine, but I'm worried about you.

2924
02:45:46,615 --> 02:45:48,365
I could tell something's wrong.

2925
02:45:49,032 --> 02:45:51,572
Now, would you please let me help?

2926
02:45:51,573 --> 02:45:56,115
I know I can't help
with all the science-y stuff, but, shoot.

2927
02:45:57,073 --> 02:45:59,573
Maybe you can use
a different kind of genius.

2928
02:46:00,157 --> 02:46:02,906
I mean, I can do a lot
with some patchouli and smoke.

2929
02:46:02,907 --> 02:46:05,073
Abracadabra all that anxiety away.

2930
02:46:10,740 --> 02:46:11,865
You know,
I think you're right.

2931
02:46:12,907 --> 02:46:16,365
I've been all wrapped up in work and...

2932
02:46:18,365 --> 02:46:22,822
maybe I could use a... aura bath...

2933
02:46:22,823 --> 02:46:24,531
- [snickers]
- ...or, you know,

2934
02:46:24,532 --> 02:46:27,573
a sound-cleansing chakra reading.

2935
02:46:28,032 --> 02:46:30,364
Some of that magic that
you're always talking about.

2936
02:46:30,365 --> 02:46:33,740
Oh. You want magic?
[chuckles]

2937
02:46:35,490 --> 02:46:36,823
Mama's got the plug.

2938
02:46:37,490 --> 02:46:39,615
- Don't say plug.
- [laughs]

2939
02:46:41,198 --> 02:46:42,697
That chamomile is hitting, ain't it?

2940
02:46:42,698 --> 02:46:45,031
- [Riri] Mm.
- [Ronnie laughs]

2941
02:46:45,032 --> 02:46:47,656
[♪ hip-hop music playing,
Floetry "Floetic"]

2942
02:46:47,657 --> 02:46:48,990
<i>♪ Floetry ♪</i>

2943
02:46:49,657 --> 02:46:52,156
<i>♪ Uh, it's floetic
Uh, it's floetic ♪</i>

2944
02:46:52,157 --> 02:46:53,739
<i>♪ Uh, it's floetic... ♪</i>

2945
02:46:53,740 --> 02:46:54,823
[Ronnie] Here we go.

2946
02:46:58,115 --> 02:46:59,322
[Riri] Really?

2947
02:46:59,323 --> 02:47:01,864
- [Ronnie] What?
- [Riri] Miss Stanton? That's your plug?

2948
02:47:01,865 --> 02:47:03,073
Girl, come on.

2949
02:47:07,490 --> 02:47:10,364
{\an8}[Riri] So, I asked for magic
and you heard Willy Wonka?

2950
02:47:10,365 --> 02:47:11,990
Is Willy Wonka not a magician?

2951
02:47:12,865 --> 02:47:18,448
Welcome to Stanton's. We got sweets.
We got reads. All your wishes guaranteed.

2952
02:47:18,948 --> 02:47:19,947
How can I help you?

2953
02:47:19,948 --> 02:47:21,864
[Ronnie] Zelma,
it hasn't been that long.

2954
02:47:21,865 --> 02:47:23,115
Where's your mama?

2955
02:47:23,948 --> 02:47:24,947
Is she around?

2956
02:47:24,948 --> 02:47:26,032
Yeah.

2957
02:47:28,157 --> 02:47:29,281
- Ma, this--
- [shushes]

2958
02:47:29,282 --> 02:47:30,447
- [Zelma] There she is.
- A-ha!

2959
02:47:30,448 --> 02:47:32,656
- Ah, yes!
- [Ronnie] Maddie!

2960
02:47:32,657 --> 02:47:35,781
- Ay, Ronnie.
- Bring it in, my sister.

2961
02:47:35,782 --> 02:47:37,572
[Madeline] It's good to see you, too!

2962
02:47:37,573 --> 02:47:39,864
- Oh! You brought Riri.
- Mm-hmm.

2963
02:47:39,865 --> 02:47:42,781
It's nice to see you again.
You met my kid, Zelma.

2964
02:47:42,782 --> 02:47:44,364
The dutiful Oompa-Loompa.

2965
02:47:44,365 --> 02:47:46,572
[Madeline] So, what brings you in today?

2966
02:47:46,573 --> 02:47:49,364
Uh, Riri is looking for
some spiritual guidance.

2967
02:47:49,365 --> 02:47:52,489
- [Madeline] Oh?
- [Riri] Yeah, like crystals or...

2968
02:47:52,490 --> 02:47:53,573
some sage.

2969
02:47:55,032 --> 02:47:56,406
Or what's in your pocket?

2970
02:47:56,407 --> 02:47:57,490
[Madeline] Uh-huh.

2971
02:47:59,490 --> 02:48:00,947
[chuckles slightly] Um, it's--

2972
02:48:00,948 --> 02:48:02,532
You gonna answer her question?

2973
02:48:04,782 --> 02:48:06,782
Yo! No. Not here.

2974
02:48:08,198 --> 02:48:09,365
Okay. Uh...

2975
02:48:10,365 --> 02:48:13,114
Mom? Please don't be mad.

2976
02:48:13,115 --> 02:48:15,282
- Why would I be--
- [rumbling]

2977
02:48:17,573 --> 02:48:18,864
- [objects clinking]
- [Ronnie gasps]

2978
02:48:18,865 --> 02:48:19,948
Mad?

2979
02:48:20,698 --> 02:48:22,031
Holy shit!

2980
02:48:22,032 --> 02:48:25,489
Sorry. Was it too fast?
I'm still learning how to hit the brakes.

2981
02:48:25,490 --> 02:48:28,406
How did you even do that?
I barely blinked.

2982
02:48:28,407 --> 02:48:29,822
Transportation spell.

2983
02:48:29,823 --> 02:48:31,364
Is that a thing? 'Cause you're saying it

2984
02:48:31,365 --> 02:48:34,031
- like it's a thing, but--
- Zelma, where are we right now?

2985
02:48:34,032 --> 02:48:36,114
The Western Cortex of Neverish.

2986
02:48:36,115 --> 02:48:38,322
- Huh?
- A parallel plane of--

2987
02:48:38,323 --> 02:48:41,572
Now, you know you are not allowed to visit
other realms without my permission.

2988
02:48:41,573 --> 02:48:44,322
Y'all gonna casually throw around
the term "parallel plane"?

2989
02:48:44,323 --> 02:48:46,864
Okay. Right. I know,
but this one's not that far away--

2990
02:48:46,865 --> 02:48:49,947
Or build secret rooms in other realms
without my permission.

2991
02:48:49,948 --> 02:48:52,447
You never actually said that, though.

2992
02:48:52,448 --> 02:48:54,573
Oh, we're gonna talk
about this shit later.

2993
02:48:55,823 --> 02:48:56,823
Give me the thing.

2994
02:48:58,573 --> 02:49:01,656
[Madeline] Let's hope your little act
of rebellion gives us something.

2995
02:49:01,657 --> 02:49:03,407
[Zelma] Oh, it will. I've been studying.

2996
02:49:08,157 --> 02:49:09,657
Well, is it enchanted?

2997
02:49:10,615 --> 02:49:12,072
Do you think it's witchcraft?

2998
02:49:12,073 --> 02:49:15,781
- It's possible, but unlikely.
- I don't know. Seems natural.

2999
02:49:15,782 --> 02:49:17,032
[energy whooshes]

3000
02:49:18,323 --> 02:49:20,698
- [both] It's natural.
- Uh, Riri? I thought...

3001
02:49:21,865 --> 02:49:23,822
Is this about your Iron suit stuff?

3002
02:49:23,823 --> 02:49:27,948
It's not... not about my Iron suit stuff.

3003
02:49:28,657 --> 02:49:30,239
What do you mean by "natural"?

3004
02:49:30,240 --> 02:49:32,989
It means it was created
in a different dimension.

3005
02:49:32,990 --> 02:49:34,572
[Riri] How do you know that?

3006
02:49:34,573 --> 02:49:36,906
I mean, the disappearing
and reappearing is a tell.

3007
02:49:36,907 --> 02:49:38,031
It's unstable.

3008
02:49:38,032 --> 02:49:40,781
[Madeline] Yeah, this thing
isn't from our realm.

3009
02:49:40,782 --> 02:49:44,156
- And it's very old.
- Uh, how does this work?

3010
02:49:44,157 --> 02:49:48,406
Oh. "Making the unknown known
is the greatest magic.

3011
02:49:48,407 --> 02:49:52,322
"Therefore, learning
and teaching, the truest spell."

3012
02:49:52,323 --> 02:49:54,281
Is that supposed to mean something to me?

3013
02:49:54,282 --> 02:49:56,739
Girl, it's a saying
she got from the Kamar-Taj.

3014
02:49:56,740 --> 02:49:58,239
What's Kamar-Taj?

3015
02:49:58,240 --> 02:50:00,322
Thank you. It's my reach school.

3016
02:50:00,323 --> 02:50:03,239
All the way in Nepal,
where all the greatest sorcerers

3017
02:50:03,240 --> 02:50:05,948
of our dimension trained
in magic arts and sciences.

3018
02:50:07,865 --> 02:50:09,614
Y'all ever heard of Doctor Strange?

3019
02:50:09,615 --> 02:50:12,281
- [high-pitched screeching]
- Hey, please don't touch those.

3020
02:50:12,282 --> 02:50:15,031
Once they get in your brain,
they're kinda hard to get out.

3021
02:50:15,032 --> 02:50:17,781
- Who gave you brain maggots?
- No one.

3022
02:50:17,782 --> 02:50:21,864
Hold up.
Madeline, you're an actual sorcerer?

3023
02:50:21,865 --> 02:50:22,989
Or whatever?

3024
02:50:22,990 --> 02:50:24,656
No, she's a dropout.

3025
02:50:24,657 --> 02:50:26,073
Excuse you.

3026
02:50:26,573 --> 02:50:30,572
I chose to leave
because I had a little witchling to raise.

3027
02:50:30,573 --> 02:50:33,322
And I still think you guys
could have raised me there.

3028
02:50:33,323 --> 02:50:35,739
I could have learned
from actual masters

3029
02:50:35,740 --> 02:50:39,031
instead of these old books
and baby witches off of TikTok.

3030
02:50:39,032 --> 02:50:42,364
Now, I've told you,
Kamar-Taj is no place for a child.

3031
02:50:42,365 --> 02:50:46,739
Besides, bringing you back to Chicago
forced you to make

3032
02:50:46,740 --> 02:50:48,948
a whole new magic of your own.

3033
02:50:49,615 --> 02:50:51,407
And it's amazing.

3034
02:50:52,365 --> 02:50:55,072
It's reckless, but amazing.

3035
02:50:55,073 --> 02:50:56,323
What are you doing now?

3036
02:50:57,407 --> 02:50:58,739
I'm reading tea leaves.

3037
02:50:58,740 --> 02:50:59,948
Oh. I know how to do that.

3038
02:51:02,073 --> 02:51:04,072
[splats, squelching]

3039
02:51:04,073 --> 02:51:05,157
Never mind.

3040
02:51:05,490 --> 02:51:07,490
[♪ low, ominous music playing]

3041
02:51:09,698 --> 02:51:10,989
[faint crackling]

3042
02:51:10,990 --> 02:51:12,323
Mom, why is it like that?

3043
02:51:13,282 --> 02:51:15,032
That's enough. We're done here.

3044
02:51:16,532 --> 02:51:17,698
Where did you get this?

3045
02:51:18,782 --> 02:51:20,781
I got it from this dude
with a magical red cloak,

3046
02:51:20,782 --> 02:51:22,781
and I think it's scarring his whole body.

3047
02:51:22,782 --> 02:51:25,072
- Oh, hell no.
- Oh, shit.

3048
02:51:25,073 --> 02:51:26,781
- [rumbling]
- Everybody out.

3049
02:51:26,782 --> 02:51:28,822
What's going on? What did you see?

3050
02:51:28,823 --> 02:51:30,031
- I saw--
- Zelma! Hush!

3051
02:51:30,032 --> 02:51:33,156
Maddie, mother to mother,
if Riri is into some dark stuff,

3052
02:51:33,157 --> 02:51:34,407
you have got to tell me.

3053
02:51:36,282 --> 02:51:39,406
Riri, I need you to stay
far, far away from that thing

3054
02:51:39,407 --> 02:51:41,031
and whoever it came from.

3055
02:51:41,032 --> 02:51:42,697
- Why?
- This shit is dark.

3056
02:51:42,698 --> 02:51:44,447
Like, real dark.

3057
02:51:44,448 --> 02:51:46,072
This itty-bitty piece of fabric?

3058
02:51:46,073 --> 02:51:49,406
This piece of fabric comes
from one of the darkest dimensions

3059
02:51:49,407 --> 02:51:50,989
known and probably unknown.

3060
02:51:50,990 --> 02:51:54,739
And the cloak that it's coming from
is likely possessing whoever's in it.

3061
02:51:54,740 --> 02:51:58,697
No. This entity doesn't possess,
it influences.

3062
02:51:58,698 --> 02:51:59,989
So, it's like a--

3063
02:51:59,990 --> 02:52:02,197
Does this entity have a name?

3064
02:52:02,198 --> 02:52:04,489
Wait! Just point me
to where I can learn more.

3065
02:52:04,490 --> 02:52:06,198
It's not that simple.

3066
02:52:06,907 --> 02:52:09,239
Magic is not like technology.

3067
02:52:09,240 --> 02:52:10,947
You know, we say, "There's no bad tech,

3068
02:52:10,948 --> 02:52:12,657
"just bad people who use tech."

3069
02:52:13,282 --> 02:52:14,822
Well, there is bad magic,

3070
02:52:14,823 --> 02:52:16,947
and it is dangerous for everyone.

3071
02:52:16,948 --> 02:52:18,240
Especially good people.

3072
02:52:18,823 --> 02:52:20,907
- Destroy it.
- Well, I could--

3073
02:52:27,115 --> 02:52:28,364
[door closes]

3074
02:52:28,365 --> 02:52:29,490
Okay.

3075
02:52:30,573 --> 02:52:33,282
Okay, so, at least we know
it's from another dimension.

3076
02:52:33,907 --> 02:52:35,657
But she didn't say how to destroy it.

3077
02:52:36,198 --> 02:52:37,322
[breathing heavily]

3078
02:52:37,323 --> 02:52:39,072
Do you think burning it will work?

3079
02:52:39,073 --> 02:52:41,947
My laser cutter divided the particles,
but it didn't destroy it.

3080
02:52:41,948 --> 02:52:43,531
There must be another way.

3081
02:52:43,532 --> 02:52:45,573
Or I could try dissolving it.

3082
02:52:46,198 --> 02:52:48,656
Yeah, I could find some
antimony pentafluoride

3083
02:52:48,657 --> 02:52:50,657
and fluorosulfonic acid.
Yeah, I could--

3084
02:52:51,198 --> 02:52:52,198
Whatchu think?

3085
02:52:53,157 --> 02:52:55,489
- Ma!
- Why didn't you just say you needed help?

3086
02:52:55,490 --> 02:52:56,822
- I did.
- No.

3087
02:52:56,823 --> 02:52:58,947
You manipulated me,
acting like you needed

3088
02:52:58,948 --> 02:53:00,197
some sage and crystals.

3089
02:53:00,198 --> 02:53:04,365
And you smuggled something dangerous
in my friend's shop, behind my back.

3090
02:53:05,198 --> 02:53:06,572
Are you the one
messing with this hood

3091
02:53:06,573 --> 02:53:08,531
- or cloak or whatever it is?
- I promise, I'm not.

3092
02:53:08,532 --> 02:53:10,490
Then why do you even have that?

3093
02:53:11,157 --> 02:53:14,114
Ma, I can't do this with you right now.

3094
02:53:14,115 --> 02:53:16,239
- Please.
- I am worried about you.

3095
02:53:16,240 --> 02:53:19,656
Don't, okay? I am fine.

3096
02:53:19,657 --> 02:53:21,197
"Fine"? You're fine?

3097
02:53:21,198 --> 02:53:23,822
Leaving the house at night,
coming home in the early morning?

3098
02:53:23,823 --> 02:53:25,614
Lying about where you are?

3099
02:53:25,615 --> 02:53:28,489
Gifting me safety watches
that trapped me in protective bubbles?

3100
02:53:28,490 --> 02:53:30,072
Having panic attacks?

3101
02:53:30,073 --> 02:53:31,572
Sleeping in your suit?

3102
02:53:31,573 --> 02:53:35,364
One coworker dead, another arrested for
domestic terrorism? That's fine to you?

3103
02:53:35,365 --> 02:53:38,198
If you don't want me to lie to you,
then don't ask me these questions.

3104
02:53:43,365 --> 02:53:44,532
Don't you trust me?

3105
02:53:45,990 --> 02:53:47,281
What are you talking about?

3106
02:53:47,282 --> 02:53:50,823
You could always go to
Gary for help, never me.

3107
02:53:51,407 --> 02:53:53,239
It has been five years
since he died--

3108
02:53:53,240 --> 02:53:54,822
This is why I don't tell you shit,

3109
02:53:54,823 --> 02:53:58,447
because you push me to deal with things
the way that you want me to.

3110
02:53:58,448 --> 02:54:01,739
And then if I don't,
you make me talk about my dead stepdad.

3111
02:54:01,740 --> 02:54:02,823
Okay. I...

3112
02:54:03,948 --> 02:54:04,948
I am not you...

3113
02:54:06,240 --> 02:54:08,156
and you actually can't take that.

3114
02:54:08,157 --> 02:54:09,823
[rumbling]

3115
02:54:11,073 --> 02:54:13,197
I swear to God, Riri,
you better not get in that.

3116
02:54:13,198 --> 02:54:14,490
Or what?

3117
02:54:16,615 --> 02:54:21,114
Riri! I can't help you
if you end up dead or in jail.

3118
02:54:21,115 --> 02:54:23,323
- [suit whirring]
- Where are you going?

3119
02:54:25,865 --> 02:54:26,865
Riri!

3120
02:54:32,323 --> 02:54:33,573
[door buzzing]

3121
02:54:35,907 --> 02:54:37,240
[indistinct chatter]

3122
02:54:43,782 --> 02:54:44,782
[door closes]

3123
02:54:46,323 --> 02:54:47,407
Ezekiel Stane.

3124
02:54:47,990 --> 02:54:50,740
Awesome. Hallucinations. Just what I need.

3125
02:54:51,240 --> 02:54:54,365
No. Ezekiel, this is... this is very real.

3126
02:54:56,907 --> 02:54:58,698
I'm sorry to barge in unannounced.

3127
02:54:59,323 --> 02:55:02,323
My name's Parker,
but you can call me Hood, if you like.

3128
02:55:03,365 --> 02:55:05,657
- It's a pleasure to meet you.
- How'd you get in here?

3129
02:55:07,115 --> 02:55:08,865
Are you like a lawyer or something?

3130
02:55:09,865 --> 02:55:12,615
Obviously not. Let me explain.

3131
02:55:16,865 --> 02:55:18,448
You and I have something in common.

3132
02:55:19,032 --> 02:55:20,365
Rather, someone in common.

3133
02:55:21,865 --> 02:55:23,073
Riri Williams.

3134
02:55:24,198 --> 02:55:26,657
I actually think,
based on what was left at Heirlum...

3135
02:55:27,157 --> 02:55:28,282
That was me, by the way.

3136
02:55:28,865 --> 02:55:32,114
...that you have the skill set
and drive to be something great.

3137
02:55:32,115 --> 02:55:34,697
Work for me,
and I'll get you your life back, Stane.

3138
02:55:34,698 --> 02:55:35,907
Is that a joke?

3139
02:55:36,407 --> 02:55:37,989
I can't go back to my job.

3140
02:55:37,990 --> 02:55:41,198
I can't go back to my house.
I can't even go back to my name.

3141
02:55:41,740 --> 02:55:43,073
My life is over.

3142
02:55:45,198 --> 02:55:46,365
How exciting.

3143
02:55:46,948 --> 02:55:49,614
- Excuse me?
- Joe's a pretty shitty name for you.

3144
02:55:49,615 --> 02:55:52,240
Probably shitty house. Shitty job, too.

3145
02:55:53,615 --> 02:55:55,406
Take my offer,
and you get to create

3146
02:55:55,407 --> 02:55:57,782
a whole new life
with this passion of yours.

3147
02:55:58,365 --> 02:56:01,282
- A whole new life as, what? A fugitive?
- As Zeke Stane.

3148
02:56:03,907 --> 02:56:06,822
Or you can rot in jail
as Joe McGillicuddy.

3149
02:56:06,823 --> 02:56:10,115
Have a think on it,
and get back to me tonight, at lights-out.

3150
02:56:12,032 --> 02:56:13,907
That's when you decide who you wanna be.

3151
02:56:18,865 --> 02:56:20,282
[door beeps, thuds]

3152
02:56:21,282 --> 02:56:23,115
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3153
02:56:34,240 --> 02:56:35,240
[sighs]

3154
02:56:48,323 --> 02:56:50,947
[Natalie] Oh, Riri, I don't think
there's gonna be anything here

3155
02:56:50,948 --> 02:56:53,614
to help us fight
dark, interdimensional magic.

3156
02:56:53,615 --> 02:56:56,532
You know, you're probably right,
but I need a quiet place to think.

3157
02:56:57,240 --> 02:57:00,365
Mom's kitchen doesn't exactly seem
like the right place right now.

3158
02:57:04,990 --> 02:57:05,990
[sighs]

3159
02:57:07,198 --> 02:57:08,323
Blast the door, N.A.T.

3160
02:57:09,115 --> 02:57:10,907
[Natalie] Check the mat, Ri.

3161
02:57:13,365 --> 02:57:14,448
[Riri scoffs]

3162
02:57:19,365 --> 02:57:23,615
[scoffs] Of course, Joe has a spare key
for his hideout.

3163
02:57:24,782 --> 02:57:25,989
Let's get to work.

3164
02:57:25,990 --> 02:57:28,573
[♪ soul music playing,
Erykah Badu "The Healer"]

3165
02:57:36,573 --> 02:57:39,656
{\an8}<i>♪ Alhamdulillah Allah Jehovah ♪</i>

3166
02:57:39,657 --> 02:57:42,572
{\an8}<i>♪ Yahweh Dios Ma'at Jah ♪</i>

3167
02:57:42,573 --> 02:57:45,031
<i>♪ Rastafari fyah dance ♪</i>

3168
02:57:45,032 --> 02:57:46,532
<i>♪ Sex, music ♪</i>

3169
02:57:51,490 --> 02:57:52,490
[muffled explosion]

3170
02:57:54,282 --> 02:57:55,948
[steam hissing]

3171
02:57:57,865 --> 02:58:01,156
<i>♪ Told you we ain't dead yet ♪</i>

3172
02:58:01,157 --> 02:58:02,615
- Thank you.
- [♪ music stops]

3173
02:58:05,740 --> 02:58:07,072
- Oh, my God.
- [♪ music resumes]

3174
02:58:07,073 --> 02:58:10,656
<i>♪ "We ain't dead,"
said the children ♪</i>

3175
02:58:10,657 --> 02:58:13,032
<i>♪ Don't believe it... ♪</i>

3176
02:58:14,282 --> 02:58:16,032
[Riri] What is this thing made of?

3177
02:58:16,948 --> 02:58:18,156
No.

3178
02:58:18,157 --> 02:58:20,781
<i>♪ Underwater, stovetop ♪</i>

3179
02:58:20,782 --> 02:58:23,614
<i>♪ Blue flame scientists ♪</i>

3180
02:58:23,615 --> 02:58:26,323
<i>♪ Come out with your scales up ♪</i>

3181
02:58:28,448 --> 02:58:32,114
<i>♪ Get baptized in the ocean... ♪</i>

3182
02:58:32,115 --> 02:58:34,365
[Riri] This is so frustrating.

3183
02:58:34,907 --> 02:58:37,490
Why is nothing working?

3184
02:58:38,073 --> 02:58:39,073
[♪ music stops]

3185
02:58:40,323 --> 02:58:44,072
[Natalie sighs]
Parker's hood must be like old, old.

3186
02:58:44,073 --> 02:58:46,698
Like, Stegosaurus old.

3187
02:58:48,032 --> 02:58:51,572
Could probably survive nuclear fallout.

3188
02:58:51,573 --> 02:58:55,240
Like, there's no way we're
the first people who tried to destroy it.

3189
02:58:55,865 --> 02:58:57,531
Maybe we could...

3190
02:58:57,532 --> 02:59:00,573
We could throw it
into the Arctic Ocean or some shit?

3191
02:59:01,115 --> 02:59:05,281
Uh... [snorts] No.
I just pictured a penguin wearing it.

3192
02:59:05,282 --> 02:59:07,447
You know, penguins don't even live
in the Arctic?

3193
02:59:07,448 --> 02:59:09,822
That's a little, little fun fact.

3194
02:59:09,823 --> 02:59:12,781
[muffled] Well, it's not that fun,
but it is a fact.

3195
02:59:12,782 --> 02:59:15,864
I don't know why the Arctic
just makes me think of penguins.

3196
02:59:15,865 --> 02:59:19,823
Damn, Ri,
what if the hood is indestructible?

3197
02:59:20,698 --> 02:59:22,656
That would be bad!

3198
02:59:22,657 --> 02:59:25,239
Wait, do you think
that it's indestructible?

3199
02:59:25,240 --> 02:59:26,698
- [muffling stops]
- I can't do this.

3200
02:59:29,157 --> 02:59:30,490
I can't figure this out.

3201
02:59:32,490 --> 02:59:34,115
I need to get outta here.

3202
02:59:37,157 --> 02:59:38,156
[sighs]

3203
02:59:38,157 --> 02:59:40,657
- [♪ tense music playing]
- [heart beating rapidly]

3204
02:59:42,240 --> 02:59:45,198
Hey, Ri? Your heart rate is way too high.

3205
02:59:45,823 --> 02:59:49,448
I'm gonna bring some fresh air in,
but you gotta breathe, okay?

3206
02:59:50,032 --> 02:59:52,489
Remember to breathe. Just breathe.

3207
02:59:52,490 --> 02:59:56,032
Stop telling me to breathe, N.A.T.A.L.I.E.

3208
02:59:56,907 --> 02:59:58,906
- I'm just trying to help.
- I can't breathe,

3209
02:59:58,907 --> 03:00:00,989
knowing everyone I love is going to die.

3210
03:00:00,990 --> 03:00:02,615
[breath shuddering]

3211
03:00:05,365 --> 03:00:07,407
Parker's gonna get us all...

3212
03:00:09,073 --> 03:00:10,365
How can I breathe?

3213
03:00:12,948 --> 03:00:14,282
This is too much.

3214
03:00:15,115 --> 03:00:16,864
- Let me out of the suit.
- Ri--

3215
03:00:16,865 --> 03:00:18,739
- Now! Let me out!
- [alarm beeps]

3216
03:00:18,740 --> 03:00:20,907
- I can't breathe.
- [heart beating faster]

3217
03:00:22,073 --> 03:00:23,072
[breathing heavily]

3218
03:00:23,073 --> 03:00:24,157
Okay.

3219
03:00:24,698 --> 03:00:27,407
Okay. I'll find us a spot to land.

3220
03:00:34,573 --> 03:00:37,864
- Riri? Should I get Ronnie? Probably not.
- [gasping]

3221
03:00:37,865 --> 03:00:40,697
Um... Oh! I'll be right back. Hang on.

3222
03:00:40,698 --> 03:00:42,365
[screams]

3223
03:00:46,490 --> 03:00:48,572
- [muffled laughter]
- [inmate 1] Hey, man, when you out?

3224
03:00:48,573 --> 03:00:50,072
[inmate 2] Thursday, I think.

3225
03:00:50,073 --> 03:00:52,032
- [inmate 1] Did you say next week?
- [inmate 2] Yeah.

3226
03:00:52,907 --> 03:00:54,656
- [inmate 1] All right.
- [laughter]

3227
03:00:54,657 --> 03:00:56,281
- Tomorrow.
- [guard] Lights out.

3228
03:00:56,282 --> 03:00:58,490
- [door buzzes]
- [switches clanging]

3229
03:01:00,240 --> 03:01:02,073
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3230
03:01:10,907 --> 03:01:13,365
- [door beeps and buzzes, unlocks]
- [♪ music stops]

3231
03:01:16,323 --> 03:01:18,282
[♪ sneaky music playing]

3232
03:01:28,240 --> 03:01:29,323
[electrical buzzing]

3233
03:01:40,657 --> 03:01:41,990
[door shuts]

3234
03:01:43,198 --> 03:01:44,573
[lights buzzing]

3235
03:01:49,407 --> 03:01:51,281
[Slug] Incoming. He's headed your way.

3236
03:01:51,282 --> 03:01:53,365
[♪ tense music playing]

3237
03:02:07,323 --> 03:02:08,323
My things.

3238
03:02:10,698 --> 03:02:11,698
[Jeri] Yeah.

3239
03:02:12,532 --> 03:02:13,865
Who the hell are you guys?

3240
03:02:14,532 --> 03:02:16,532
[♪ music playing on headphones]

3241
03:02:20,865 --> 03:02:22,115
[knocking at window]

3242
03:02:25,198 --> 03:02:26,490
[rhythmic knocking]

3243
03:02:40,698 --> 03:02:43,615
Well, Miss Riri Williams at my window.

3244
03:02:48,198 --> 03:02:50,282
Uh, no thanks.

3245
03:02:50,907 --> 03:02:52,739
[screaming]

3246
03:02:52,740 --> 03:02:54,531
Holy shit! Oh, shit.

3247
03:02:54,532 --> 03:02:58,740
[whimpers] Oh, shit.
Don't you ever do that shit again!

3248
03:02:59,323 --> 03:03:00,823
I'll-- Boy.

3249
03:03:02,115 --> 03:03:03,906
Oh, shit.

3250
03:03:03,907 --> 03:03:05,239
[breathes heavily]

3251
03:03:05,240 --> 03:03:07,864
I'm alive. I'm alive.

3252
03:03:07,865 --> 03:03:10,698
Xavier? What are you doing here?

3253
03:03:11,615 --> 03:03:13,365
Your suit just kidnapped me.

3254
03:03:14,615 --> 03:03:16,240
Wh-What are you doing here?

3255
03:03:18,490 --> 03:03:19,532
You okay, Ri?

3256
03:03:22,365 --> 03:03:25,240
- [breath shuddering] I'm...
- You don't have to say "fine."

3257
03:03:27,448 --> 03:03:30,365
I'm tired. [sniffles]

3258
03:03:37,698 --> 03:03:39,573
[♪ melancholy music playing]

3259
03:03:46,198 --> 03:03:48,947
Hey, how'd you do that?
That remote control thing?

3260
03:03:48,948 --> 03:03:52,323
To summon me here? That was a trip.

3261
03:03:52,948 --> 03:03:54,948
What remote control thing?

3262
03:03:55,740 --> 03:03:57,323
[Natalie] I brought you here.

3263
03:04:01,532 --> 03:04:02,532
Natalie?

3264
03:04:04,282 --> 03:04:05,448
How are you doing that?

3265
03:04:07,157 --> 03:04:08,823
Pleasure to meet you, finally.

3266
03:04:13,907 --> 03:04:15,032
What do you think?

3267
03:04:25,240 --> 03:04:26,698
[energy humming]

3268
03:04:28,907 --> 03:04:29,907
That is...

3269
03:04:32,115 --> 03:04:33,448
That is horrifying.

3270
03:04:34,032 --> 03:04:37,448
You had no right to use Natalie
as one of your little tech toys, Ri.

3271
03:04:38,532 --> 03:04:41,240
I thought if anybody would get me,
it'd be you.

3272
03:04:42,323 --> 03:04:45,572
If you think I like that,
then you don't know me at all.

3273
03:04:45,573 --> 03:04:50,990
Xa, wait. I swear it just happened.

3274
03:04:51,907 --> 03:04:55,447
But... I don't know,
you get kinda used to it.

3275
03:04:55,448 --> 03:04:58,156
It's nice in a way. Like your mixtape.

3276
03:04:58,157 --> 03:04:59,864
Oh, my God, Ri. That's not the same thing!

3277
03:04:59,865 --> 03:05:01,114
I'm honoring her!

3278
03:05:01,115 --> 03:05:03,656
You're freezing her in time,
faking like she's still alive!

3279
03:05:03,657 --> 03:05:07,240
Look at her. She is alive.

3280
03:05:08,115 --> 03:05:09,115
Sort of.

3281
03:05:09,865 --> 03:05:13,031
That is not my sister!
She's not sort of alive!

3282
03:05:13,032 --> 03:05:15,532
Wow. Okay. So, what would you do?

3283
03:05:16,323 --> 03:05:18,740
- If you were me, what would you do?
- Make her go away.

3284
03:05:19,657 --> 03:05:20,657
Delete...

3285
03:05:21,782 --> 03:05:22,782
it.

3286
03:05:23,740 --> 03:05:25,573
[♪ melancholy music playing]

3287
03:05:31,073 --> 03:05:32,198
Ri, really?

3288
03:05:35,532 --> 03:05:37,031
- N.A.T.A.L.I.E.
- [Natalie] I'm out.

3289
03:05:37,032 --> 03:05:38,365
[Riri] Wait.

3290
03:05:38,990 --> 03:05:40,781
[suit flies off]

3291
03:05:40,782 --> 03:05:42,115
Xa, I can't.

3292
03:05:42,907 --> 03:05:44,365
What you're asking is...

3293
03:05:46,448 --> 03:05:47,448
I can't.

3294
03:05:48,073 --> 03:05:49,656
Well, maybe you should try.

3295
03:05:49,657 --> 03:05:51,448
'Cause it's not gonna end well, Ri.

3296
03:05:54,698 --> 03:05:55,782
And keep your watch.

3297
03:05:57,115 --> 03:05:59,698
- [♪ melancholy music continues]
- [breath shudders]

3298
03:06:10,698 --> 03:06:11,864
[John] <i>Put the phone down.</i>

3299
03:06:11,865 --> 03:06:13,322
<i>- Don't listen to him.</i>
- [Parker] <i>Listen.</i>

3300
03:06:13,323 --> 03:06:15,781
<i>- Listen while I show you my tricks.</i>
- [John] <i>I swear to God,</i>

3301
03:06:15,782 --> 03:06:18,072
<i>- if you do this shit, man...
- I wanna show you what I can do!</i>

3302
03:06:18,073 --> 03:06:19,906
[laughing]

3303
03:06:19,907 --> 03:06:21,239
<i>- I love you, bro.
- He did.</i>

3304
03:06:21,240 --> 03:06:23,989
[John] <i>I love you with all my heart.
I guarantee you're wrong.</i>

3305
03:06:23,990 --> 03:06:25,073
[cell phone vibrating]

3306
03:06:34,823 --> 03:06:36,614
Please tell me these are
the last components

3307
03:06:36,615 --> 03:06:38,989
- for this heavy-ass machine.
- [Ezekiel] Yep.

3308
03:06:38,990 --> 03:06:40,239
[machine buzzes]

3309
03:06:40,240 --> 03:06:42,614
Parker asked me to help upgrade you.
You don't mind?

3310
03:06:42,615 --> 03:06:43,697
Sure.

3311
03:06:43,698 --> 03:06:46,531
Well, let's get you cleaned up
for your alterations.

3312
03:06:46,532 --> 03:06:47,782
[trimmer whirring]

3313
03:06:48,740 --> 03:06:49,907
I can handle that.

3314
03:06:53,698 --> 03:06:55,115
[keyboard clacking]

3315
