3531
03:19:37,641 --> 03:19:38,849
[Riri clears throat]

3532
03:19:40,099 --> 03:19:41,556
[both grunt]

3533
03:19:41,557 --> 03:19:42,891
[breath shudders]

3534
03:19:46,141 --> 03:19:47,349
[yells]

3535
03:19:52,557 --> 03:19:54,391
[strained groaning]

3536
03:20:00,974 --> 03:20:03,306
That headline tomorrow is gonna be rough.

3537
03:20:03,307 --> 03:20:04,640
"Girl Genius Dies."

3538
03:20:04,641 --> 03:20:06,098
My death won't make the news.

3539
03:20:06,099 --> 03:20:07,641
Well, damn, that was dark.

3540
03:20:08,307 --> 03:20:10,599
- Yeah, but I low-key felt it.
- Yeah, high-key.

3541
03:20:13,891 --> 03:20:15,516
Can y'all do me a favor? Just...

3542
03:20:18,266 --> 03:20:19,266
Just make it quick.

3543
03:20:21,766 --> 03:20:22,807
One clean shot.

3544
03:20:23,974 --> 03:20:24,974
Sure.

3545
03:20:25,641 --> 03:20:27,724
[♪ tense music builds]

3546
03:20:28,224 --> 03:20:30,307
[energy warbling and crackling]

3547
03:20:48,141 --> 03:20:49,140
[crackling intensifies]

3548
03:20:49,141 --> 03:20:50,516
- [Jeri] Whoa!
- [Clown] Hey, Riri.

3549
03:20:52,141 --> 03:20:53,807
Hey, girl, hey.

3550
03:20:54,557 --> 03:20:56,182
- [lock clacks]
- Aw!

3551
03:20:57,182 --> 03:21:00,973
You really think a locked door
is gonna keep me out? [laughs]

3552
03:21:00,974 --> 03:21:02,057
Okay.

3553
03:21:04,016 --> 03:21:05,181
- [device whines]
- Kee!

3554
03:21:05,182 --> 03:21:06,641
[beeping]

3555
03:21:07,182 --> 03:21:09,016
[♪ tense music playing]

3556
03:21:19,016 --> 03:21:21,015
Yo, let's make this quick.

3557
03:21:21,016 --> 03:21:22,766
Your girl's got a date.

3558
03:21:23,474 --> 03:21:25,766
- [♪ gripping music playing]
- [car horn blares]

3559
03:21:29,391 --> 03:21:30,932
[grunting]

3560
03:21:43,557 --> 03:21:44,807
Come on, Clown.

3561
03:21:45,516 --> 03:21:46,974
You don't have to do this.
You know, I--

3562
03:21:48,016 --> 03:21:49,141
I thought we were cool.

3563
03:21:50,057 --> 03:21:51,057
That...

3564
03:21:52,682 --> 03:21:54,056
was before you killed John.

3565
03:21:54,057 --> 03:21:55,932
[Riri] It's not like that.
I didn't mean to.

3566
03:21:59,182 --> 03:22:00,681
[Jeri, muffled] Clown, are you okay?
Clown?

3567
03:22:00,682 --> 03:22:01,766
[Roz, muffled] Hey, Clown.

3568
03:22:04,474 --> 03:22:06,140
[Jeri] I'm trying to...

3569
03:22:06,141 --> 03:22:07,224
Clown!

3570
03:22:19,266 --> 03:22:20,682
[explosion]

3571
03:22:21,641 --> 03:22:23,474
[grunts, pants]

3572
03:22:26,724 --> 03:22:31,932
Listen, I didn't like the guy either,
but we were working through our shit.

3573
03:22:33,057 --> 03:22:34,765
Anyway, he was part of the team.

3574
03:22:34,766 --> 03:22:36,141
What team?

3575
03:22:36,724 --> 03:22:40,141
Everyone on Parker's crew is disposable.
He killed Rampage.

3576
03:22:42,641 --> 03:22:44,515
You don't know what you're talking about.

3577
03:22:44,516 --> 03:22:46,307
[beeps, explodes]

3578
03:22:50,349 --> 03:22:51,682
[Riri] Come on, Clown.

3579
03:22:52,599 --> 03:22:53,682
Ask him.

3580
03:22:57,224 --> 03:22:58,391
[Clown] Listen, Riri...

3581
03:23:00,599 --> 03:23:02,391
I'm done talking. Okay?

3582
03:23:03,766 --> 03:23:08,348
Come out and let's fight.

3583
03:23:08,349 --> 03:23:09,891
[bomb beeps]

3584
03:23:10,516 --> 03:23:11,516
Is this thing on?

3585
03:23:14,682 --> 03:23:15,932
[Clown groans]

3586
03:23:16,974 --> 03:23:18,807
- [beeping rapidly]
- [gasps]

3587
03:23:20,807 --> 03:23:22,473
- [explosion]
- [yelps]

3588
03:23:22,474 --> 03:23:24,098
[coughs]

3589
03:23:24,099 --> 03:23:25,182
Shit.

3590
03:23:33,516 --> 03:23:34,723
Yo, she's getting away.

3591
03:23:34,724 --> 03:23:36,724
[♪ tense music playing]

3592
03:23:37,849 --> 03:23:39,766
- [tires screeching]
- [car honks]

3593
03:23:41,724 --> 03:23:43,057
I got eyes on her.

3594
03:23:47,099 --> 03:23:48,974
- [gasps]
- [horn blares]

3595
03:23:54,724 --> 03:23:56,974
- [engine accelerating]
- [truck thudding]

3596
03:23:59,974 --> 03:24:01,974
[♪ heroic music playing]

3597
03:24:17,141 --> 03:24:18,224
[♪ music stops]

3598
03:24:20,057 --> 03:24:22,391
[car alarms and horns sounding]

3599
03:24:23,682 --> 03:24:25,473
[muffled thudding]

3600
03:24:25,474 --> 03:24:26,766
[glass breaks]

3601
03:24:39,182 --> 03:24:40,182
[groaning]

3602
03:24:43,432 --> 03:24:44,515
[stomps]

3603
03:24:44,516 --> 03:24:46,516
[gasps] Whoa.

3604
03:24:47,432 --> 03:24:48,432
Mm-mm.

3605
03:24:51,432 --> 03:24:52,682
[exhales deeply]

3606
03:24:54,057 --> 03:24:55,849
[suit whines]

3607
03:24:57,349 --> 03:24:58,391
[vomits]

3608
03:25:02,932 --> 03:25:04,391
Ugh, you good?

3609
03:25:06,182 --> 03:25:07,516
I ate too much.

3610
03:25:08,099 --> 03:25:09,557
R-I-P your intestines.

3611
03:25:10,474 --> 03:25:11,931
Yo, what happened to my suit?

3612
03:25:11,932 --> 03:25:13,723
Your little friend tried to come for me.

3613
03:25:13,724 --> 03:25:15,848
And I'm fine. Thank you for asking.

3614
03:25:15,849 --> 03:25:18,473
You left me without any protection.
They could've killed me.

3615
03:25:18,474 --> 03:25:20,848
I'm sorry. I needed some time.

3616
03:25:20,849 --> 03:25:22,474
When Xavier saw me...

3617
03:25:24,224 --> 03:25:26,641
I wasn't expecting for him
to react that way.

3618
03:25:27,557 --> 03:25:28,556
I'm-- I'm hurt.

3619
03:25:28,557 --> 03:25:30,306
- Hurt?
- Okay.

3620
03:25:30,307 --> 03:25:32,015
You are a series of codes, okay?

3621
03:25:32,016 --> 03:25:34,056
Numbers and symbols.

3622
03:25:34,057 --> 03:25:36,431
Is that why you were
considering deleting me

3623
03:25:36,432 --> 03:25:38,724
at the junkyard when Xavier asked?

3624
03:25:40,516 --> 03:25:42,266
I am not the problem here, Ri.

3625
03:25:43,141 --> 03:25:44,141
You are.

3626
03:25:46,641 --> 03:25:47,931
[♪ pensive music playing]

3627
03:25:47,932 --> 03:25:49,016
You know what?

3628
03:25:51,891 --> 03:25:53,890
I don't need this. Shoot.

3629
03:25:53,891 --> 03:25:57,140
Um, I'm going to bed. Yeah.

3630
03:25:57,141 --> 03:25:59,099
- Bed?
- Peace.

3631
03:25:59,641 --> 03:26:02,641
Rest well. Don't let the bedbugs bite.

3632
03:26:13,224 --> 03:26:14,766
- [gasps]
- [alarm beeping]

3633
03:26:15,807 --> 03:26:17,973
Nat, wake up. Nat, I need you!

3634
03:26:17,974 --> 03:26:19,515
[alarms sounding]

3635
03:26:19,516 --> 03:26:21,223
Yo, look, I'm sorry.

3636
03:26:21,224 --> 03:26:23,557
Can you please-- Nat!

3637
03:26:24,557 --> 03:26:25,932
[grunts]

3638
03:26:30,057 --> 03:26:31,099
[grunts]

3639
03:26:34,057 --> 03:26:36,224
- [alarms stop sounding]
- [panting]

3640
03:26:38,432 --> 03:26:40,099
- [exhales deeply]
- [Ezekiel] Hey, Riri.

3641
03:26:41,266 --> 03:26:43,182
[♪ dramatic music playing]

3642
03:26:45,099 --> 03:26:46,265
Hello.

3643
03:26:46,266 --> 03:26:47,349
[beeping]

3644
03:26:57,766 --> 03:27:00,266
- [♪ music intensifies]
- [electrical crackling]

3645
03:27:01,724 --> 03:27:02,932
[Ezekiel chuckles]

3646
03:27:07,474 --> 03:27:08,932
What did you do to yourself?

3647
03:27:09,516 --> 03:27:10,682
Pretty neat, right?

3648
03:27:11,474 --> 03:27:15,390
I was bailed out
by a mutual friend, Parker Robbins.

3649
03:27:15,391 --> 03:27:16,474
[♪ music stops]

3650
03:27:17,141 --> 03:27:20,181
Compelling guy. Got me my stuff back.

3651
03:27:20,182 --> 03:27:21,557
What does he want in return?

3652
03:27:22,724 --> 03:27:23,724
You.

3653
03:27:24,682 --> 03:27:27,515
You know, I never understood
what my father's fascination was

3654
03:27:27,516 --> 03:27:29,098
with power until now.

3655
03:27:29,099 --> 03:27:30,891
[electricity crackles]

3656
03:27:33,266 --> 03:27:35,141
[♪ tense music playing]

3657
03:27:36,599 --> 03:27:37,807
Come on, Joe.

3658
03:27:39,266 --> 03:27:40,640
This ain't you.

3659
03:27:40,641 --> 03:27:42,681
This is me. It's a better me.

3660
03:27:42,682 --> 03:27:46,056
I never meant for you
to be involved in any of this.

3661
03:27:46,057 --> 03:27:47,973
Okay? And I can still make it right

3662
03:27:47,974 --> 03:27:50,891
- if you just let me try.
- It's too late.

3663
03:27:54,349 --> 03:27:55,724
At least we'll always have Alanis.

3664
03:27:57,432 --> 03:27:58,432
[Riri groans]

3665
03:28:02,891 --> 03:28:05,807
- [grunts]
- [beeping]

3666
03:28:07,432 --> 03:28:08,432
[groans]

3667
03:28:10,724 --> 03:28:12,515
[weapon charges up, dies]

3668
03:28:12,516 --> 03:28:13,848
Uh-oh.

3669
03:28:13,849 --> 03:28:15,391
[alarm beeping]

3670
03:28:15,891 --> 03:28:18,266
- [grunting]
- [♪ dramatic music playing]

3671
03:28:19,849 --> 03:28:21,807
[static warbling and crackling]

3672
03:28:24,141 --> 03:28:25,641
[gasping]

3673
03:28:26,432 --> 03:28:28,099
[Ezekiel breathing heavily]

3674
03:28:29,974 --> 03:28:31,307
[electricity bursting]

3675
03:28:32,391 --> 03:28:33,390
[gasps]

3676
03:28:33,391 --> 03:28:35,724
You know, I spent my whole life

3677
03:28:37,182 --> 03:28:38,391
trying not to become...

3678
03:28:39,932 --> 03:28:41,848
- Obadiah Stane...
- [metal clattering]

3679
03:28:41,849 --> 03:28:44,931
...just to find myself
right where he left off,

3680
03:28:44,932 --> 03:28:46,932
taking down an iron...

3681
03:28:48,099 --> 03:28:49,474
freak!

3682
03:28:50,266 --> 03:28:51,516
[panting]

3683
03:28:53,516 --> 03:28:55,141
- [crackling]
- [Riri groans]

3684
03:28:57,766 --> 03:28:59,099
[Riri] Please don't.

3685
03:29:03,141 --> 03:29:04,516
Please.

3686
03:29:05,057 --> 03:29:06,641
[electricity bursting]

3687
03:29:10,057 --> 03:29:12,266
- [groans]
- [♪ solemn music playing]

3688
03:29:15,182 --> 03:29:17,016
You need to leave Chicago now.

3689
03:29:18,474 --> 03:29:21,641
If Parker finds out you're still alive,
he won't be so forgiving.

3690
03:29:23,516 --> 03:29:25,974
[strained groaning]

3691
03:29:39,349 --> 03:29:40,349
[grunts]

3692
03:29:50,932 --> 03:29:51,932
[groans]

3693
03:30:00,141 --> 03:30:01,141
[Riri] Natalie.

3694
03:30:03,974 --> 03:30:05,807
[♪ solemn music continues]

3695
03:30:23,057 --> 03:30:24,057
[scoffs]

3696
03:30:26,682 --> 03:30:27,807
[breathing heavily]

3697
03:30:28,766 --> 03:30:31,057
- [door opening]
- [sighs]

3698
03:30:31,932 --> 03:30:33,182
[door creaking]

3699
03:30:35,766 --> 03:30:37,974
[Ronnie seething]

3700
03:30:38,766 --> 03:30:41,390
You have lost
your damn mind, Riri Williams,

3701
03:30:41,391 --> 03:30:43,556
and don't expect me to help you find it.

3702
03:30:43,557 --> 03:30:46,431
You fly off with this dangerous thing
from another dimension,

3703
03:30:46,432 --> 03:30:48,432
and you can't answer a text?

3704
03:30:51,432 --> 03:30:52,432
What happened?

3705
03:30:53,974 --> 03:30:55,641
Mom, I need your help. [breath shudders]

3706
03:30:56,224 --> 03:30:58,099
Okay. Oh, my.

3707
03:30:59,099 --> 03:31:02,432
[breathing heavily] What-- Let me see.

3708
03:31:07,807 --> 03:31:09,099
[sobs] Oh, baby.

3709
03:31:17,932 --> 03:31:20,349
[inhales sharply]
I wish you came to me sooner.

3710
03:31:21,974 --> 03:31:24,349
- I thought I had it under control.
- Mm. [scoffs]

3711
03:31:25,682 --> 03:31:27,432
Sorry I kept you in the dark.

3712
03:31:30,016 --> 03:31:31,224
- Are you mad?
- Yeah.

3713
03:31:32,682 --> 03:31:36,266
But mostly, I'm grateful that
I still have my baby in front of me,

3714
03:31:36,849 --> 03:31:38,015
and that you're safe.

3715
03:31:38,016 --> 03:31:42,890
Mom, I said there are crazies
in these streets looking for me.

3716
03:31:42,891 --> 03:31:44,723
We shouldn't even
be sitting down right now.

3717
03:31:44,724 --> 03:31:46,223
We should be packing our bags.

3718
03:31:46,224 --> 03:31:48,181
Riri, you can't keep runnin'.

3719
03:31:48,182 --> 03:31:50,473
Chicago is not safe for us.

3720
03:31:50,474 --> 03:31:54,432
I'm not talking about Chicago, Riri.
I'm talking about you. Y--

3721
03:31:56,724 --> 03:31:59,265
You can't keep running from yourself,
because everywhere you go,

3722
03:31:59,266 --> 03:32:03,390
whether it's here or Cambridge,
this comes with you.

3723
03:32:03,391 --> 03:32:04,891
I'm not following.

3724
03:32:05,474 --> 03:32:08,973
Your obsession with this suit
is the reason you got kicked outta MIT.

3725
03:32:08,974 --> 03:32:12,265
It got you involved
with a crime boss and a lunatic

3726
03:32:12,266 --> 03:32:15,056
who turned himself into a robot,
and it's the reason you ain't got a man.

3727
03:32:15,057 --> 03:32:17,390
Nothin' is worth all that damn trouble.

3728
03:32:17,391 --> 03:32:20,931
- My suit is special to me.
- Why? Huh?

3729
03:32:20,932 --> 03:32:23,890
Out of all the things you could've built
with that big brain of yours,

3730
03:32:23,891 --> 03:32:26,306
- why an iron suit?
- Because I could.

3731
03:32:26,307 --> 03:32:27,766
You wanna try that again?

3732
03:32:33,891 --> 03:32:35,307
I just wanna understand.

3733
03:32:36,099 --> 03:32:37,724
Help me understand.

3734
03:32:40,932 --> 03:32:43,682
Because it was the only thing
I could do to protect us.

3735
03:32:45,474 --> 03:32:47,266
After Gary and Natalie died...

3736
03:32:48,474 --> 03:32:50,556
That night I just froze.
I couldn't help them.

3737
03:32:50,557 --> 03:32:52,723
I just had to watch them bleed out

3738
03:32:52,724 --> 03:32:55,641
until the paramedics came
one minute too late.

3739
03:32:56,766 --> 03:32:58,515
I will never let that happen again.

3740
03:32:58,516 --> 03:32:59,598
If I lost you too--

3741
03:32:59,599 --> 03:33:01,557
Mm-mm. No, no.

3742
03:33:11,724 --> 03:33:15,057
It is my job to make you feel safe.

3743
03:33:15,641 --> 03:33:17,141
Not the other way around.

3744
03:33:18,141 --> 03:33:19,141
Do you hear me?

3745
03:33:20,349 --> 03:33:22,557
I hear you, Mom...

3746
03:33:24,057 --> 03:33:26,141
but this is so much bigger than you.

3747
03:33:26,682 --> 03:33:32,724
Without that suit, I can't protect us,
and that is why we need to leave now.

3748
03:33:35,141 --> 03:33:37,223
You know how when
people can sense danger,

3749
03:33:37,224 --> 03:33:39,599
they either fight, fly, or freeze?

3750
03:33:40,974 --> 03:33:44,807
Baby, you have flown,
you have frozen,

3751
03:33:45,599 --> 03:33:48,641
- but you haven't tried fighting.
- My fights get people hurt.

3752
03:33:52,141 --> 03:33:54,598
Riri, there are some demons
we just can't outrun,

3753
03:33:54,599 --> 03:33:57,973
but you don't have to fight alone.
I'm here to help.

3754
03:33:57,974 --> 03:33:59,682
I'll fight them with you.

3755
03:34:01,224 --> 03:34:02,890
- Me too.
- [both gasp]

3756
03:34:02,891 --> 03:34:04,974
I'm sorry, my ba--
[chuckles] My bad.

3757
03:34:07,307 --> 03:34:09,516
How am I even supposed to fight?

3758
03:34:22,891 --> 03:34:23,891
[switch clicks]

3759
03:34:31,266 --> 03:34:32,474
[switch clicks]

3760
03:34:33,349 --> 03:34:35,557
Okay, can you show me the thing
so we can go?

3761
03:34:37,557 --> 03:34:38,724
This is the thing.

3762
03:34:42,266 --> 03:34:43,307
Dad's garage.

3763
03:34:46,141 --> 03:34:48,098
Cool. Got it. Let's go.

3764
03:34:48,099 --> 03:34:50,432
- Riri--
- How can you be here?

3765
03:34:52,432 --> 03:34:55,390
Especially at a time like this.

3766
03:34:55,391 --> 03:34:58,640
- We have to go.
- Riri, listen to me.

3767
03:34:58,641 --> 03:35:02,015
You built things in this garage
that most people couldn't dream of.

3768
03:35:02,016 --> 03:35:03,473
Can't you see that?

3769
03:35:03,474 --> 03:35:04,932
All I see...

3770
03:35:05,974 --> 03:35:07,391
is where Natalie used to be.

3771
03:35:08,557 --> 03:35:11,516
And then I wish that she was still here...

3772
03:35:12,724 --> 03:35:19,057
to do my hair and talk shit,
and then I get angry that she's not.

3773
03:35:20,266 --> 03:35:23,474
- This place took so much from us.
- Yes.

3774
03:35:24,224 --> 03:35:26,932
But it also gave so much to us.

3775
03:35:34,474 --> 03:35:35,974
Just-- Hold on.

3776
03:35:39,932 --> 03:35:43,641
You remember this? "Property of Ironhead"?

3777
03:35:49,849 --> 03:35:51,182
I don't know what that is.

3778
03:35:53,474 --> 03:35:54,599
You sure about that?

3779
03:35:55,266 --> 03:35:58,557
[young Riri groans]
<i>Come on! Where are they?</i>

3780
03:36:00,266 --> 03:36:04,473
<i>Dad! Dad! Dad!</i>

3781
03:36:04,474 --> 03:36:06,223
<i>Have you seen my welding goggles?</i>

3782
03:36:06,224 --> 03:36:09,391
<i>I need to finish
my hydraulic modulation device.</i>

3783
03:36:10,724 --> 03:36:13,057
<i>Okay, where would it be?
Where would it be?</i>

3784
03:36:13,682 --> 03:36:14,766
<i>Oh!</i>

3785
03:36:17,432 --> 03:36:19,307
[Gary] <i>You need a break.</i>

3786
03:36:19,849 --> 03:36:22,723
<i>Do you think Mae Jemison took breaks?</i>

3787
03:36:22,724 --> 03:36:25,931
<i>I don't think so.
She was too busy breaking barriers.</i>

3788
03:36:25,932 --> 03:36:27,265
<i>You are eight years old.</i>

3789
03:36:27,266 --> 03:36:30,181
<i>You need to be outside riding a bike,
catching some fresh air.</i>

3790
03:36:30,182 --> 03:36:31,890
<i>Your inventions can wait.</i>

3791
03:36:31,891 --> 03:36:33,015
<i>I want my goggles.</i>

3792
03:36:33,016 --> 03:36:35,016
[♪ sentimental music playing]

3793
03:36:37,182 --> 03:36:38,182
[whistles]

3794
03:36:48,224 --> 03:36:51,182
<i>Just give me one song.
You can get these goggles right back.</i>

3795
03:36:52,266 --> 03:36:54,431
[shudders]

3796
03:36:54,432 --> 03:36:55,516
<i>Fine.</i>

3797
03:36:57,766 --> 03:36:58,766
[switch clicks]

3798
03:37:01,349 --> 03:37:02,974
[Natalie] Why did you turn it off?

3799
03:37:09,932 --> 03:37:12,224
What was the point of
projecting that memory?

3800
03:37:13,224 --> 03:37:15,349
To show you that when you try to forget...

3801
03:37:17,141 --> 03:37:20,057
all the memories that make you sad,
you wind up...

3802
03:37:21,516 --> 03:37:23,849
forgetting the ones worth remembering.

3803
03:37:29,224 --> 03:37:30,224
[shudders]

3804
03:37:31,557 --> 03:37:32,557
[Gary] <i>Mm-hmm.</i>

3805
03:37:35,016 --> 03:37:38,016
[♪ soul music plays on speakers,
Leon Bridges "Brown Skin Girl"]

3806
03:37:44,391 --> 03:37:46,474
<i>- ♪ Brown skin girl ♪</i>
- [Gary] <i>Mm-hmm.</i>

3807
03:37:47,432 --> 03:37:49,974
[Gary sings along] <i>♪ On the other side
of the world ♪</i>

3808
03:37:51,016 --> 03:37:52,016
<i>Yeah.</i>

3809
03:37:52,766 --> 03:37:55,140
<i>- Come on.
- ♪ Brown skin girl staring ♪</i>

3810
03:37:55,141 --> 03:37:56,432
<i>Spin it around.</i>

3811
03:37:57,099 --> 03:37:58,681
<i>♪ With her brown eyes ♪</i>

3812
03:37:58,682 --> 03:38:01,432
<i>Mm-hmm. Give me that spin.
You ready for it?</i>

3813
03:38:02,182 --> 03:38:03,681
<i>♪ Ooh, baby ♪</i>

3814
03:38:03,682 --> 03:38:06,223
<i>- Just like that.
- ♪ Don′t you know you're a ♪</i>

3815
03:38:06,224 --> 03:38:08,890
- <i>♪ Cutie pie? ♪</i>
- [Gary] <i>♪ Cutie pie ♪</i>

3816
03:38:08,891 --> 03:38:10,724
<i>Come on, come on. Come on.</i>

3817
03:38:12,016 --> 03:38:16,306
<i>♪ Princess, little honey
with the polka-dot dress on ♪</i>

3818
03:38:16,307 --> 03:38:17,391
[sniffles]

3819
03:38:20,557 --> 03:38:21,556
<i>Follow me, watch this.</i>

3820
03:38:21,557 --> 03:38:26,015
<i>♪ Ruby-lipped lady
whose name I don't know ♪</i>

3821
03:38:26,016 --> 03:38:28,474
[Gary] <i>♪ Cutie pie ♪</i>

3822
03:38:29,099 --> 03:38:31,181
<i>There you go. Right.</i>

3823
03:38:31,182 --> 03:38:33,598
<i>- Ooh. Ooh. Ooh.</i>
- [chuckling]

3824
03:38:33,599 --> 03:38:37,682
<i>♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh
Ooh, ooh, ooh, wo-ooh ♪</i>

3825
03:38:39,641 --> 03:38:42,224
<i>♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh
Ooh, ooh ♪</i>

3826
03:38:42,891 --> 03:38:44,349
[both chuckling]

3827
03:38:48,849 --> 03:38:51,099
- <i>♪ Brown skin girl with... ♪</i>
- [grunts]

3828
03:38:51,724 --> 03:38:54,307
- [Gary] <i>Ooh!
- Ow!</i> [whimpers]

3829
03:38:54,974 --> 03:38:56,599
<i>Let me see, let me see, let me see.</i>

3830
03:38:58,141 --> 03:39:01,432
<i>- Let it go.
- This is why I don't do breaks.</i>

3831
03:39:02,099 --> 03:39:03,599
<i>It didn't even make a scratch.</i>

3832
03:39:04,474 --> 03:39:05,932
<i>You got a good old iron head.</i>

3833
03:39:11,057 --> 03:39:13,224
<i>Come here. Mm.</i> [kisses]

3834
03:39:15,016 --> 03:39:16,016
[chuckles]

3835
03:39:21,516 --> 03:39:23,057
[breathing raggedly]

3836
03:39:24,641 --> 03:39:25,641
Thank you.

3837
03:39:28,266 --> 03:39:29,599
I'm sorry...

3838
03:39:30,349 --> 03:39:32,806
for what I said earlier
about how you're a problem,

3839
03:39:32,807 --> 03:39:35,473
- and--
- No, no, no, that's-- It's all good.

3840
03:39:35,474 --> 03:39:36,557
[Riri] No, it's not.

3841
03:39:38,266 --> 03:39:39,266
I didn't mean it.

3842
03:39:40,932 --> 03:39:42,016
Any of it. You're--

3843
03:39:44,057 --> 03:39:47,681
You're a glitch, but you're my glitch.

3844
03:39:47,682 --> 03:39:48,891
[chuckles softly]

3845
03:39:52,016 --> 03:39:53,266
Thanks.

3846
03:39:57,391 --> 03:39:58,557
You guys are right.

3847
03:40:00,182 --> 03:40:03,140
Chicago is home. Always has been.

3848
03:40:03,141 --> 03:40:06,641
There used to be a time where
I couldn't imagine being anywhere else.

3849
03:40:07,557 --> 03:40:09,432
I wanna fight for that feeling again.

3850
03:40:10,557 --> 03:40:13,432
It's only a matter of time
before Parker realizes that I'm not dead.

3851
03:40:14,891 --> 03:40:18,016
I need a suit,
and I have nothing to build it with.

3852
03:40:19,724 --> 03:40:21,807
[smacks lips] Well, I was thinking...

3853
03:40:23,516 --> 03:40:24,723
maybe this could help.

3854
03:40:24,724 --> 03:40:26,724
[♪ rousing music playing]

3855
03:40:31,057 --> 03:40:32,641
- Ta-da! [chuckles]
- How?

3856
03:40:33,224 --> 03:40:36,182
[Ronnie] When I realized you were
stayin' home, I bought it back.

3857
03:40:40,266 --> 03:40:41,266
[Riri gasps]

3858
03:40:42,974 --> 03:40:43,974
[Riri chuckles]

3859
03:40:45,307 --> 03:40:46,516
[chuckles] Oh!

3860
03:40:47,474 --> 03:40:50,307
When Dad gave me this car,
he told me it'd always keep me safe.

3861
03:40:52,891 --> 03:40:54,016
Thick and thin.

3862
03:40:58,224 --> 03:40:59,307
Let's get to work.

3863
03:41:00,266 --> 03:41:01,599
[door opening]

3864
03:41:08,391 --> 03:41:09,599
It's done.

3865
03:41:14,474 --> 03:41:15,807
Where's the rest of the suit?

3866
03:41:16,849 --> 03:41:17,849
Collateral damage.

3867
03:41:19,182 --> 03:41:20,724
How did you get rid of her?

3868
03:41:23,807 --> 03:41:26,057
- By killing her.
- I love this story already.

3869
03:41:26,932 --> 03:41:28,431
- Go on.
- There's not much to tell.

3870
03:41:28,432 --> 03:41:29,516
I just, you know...

3871
03:41:30,599 --> 03:41:34,932
kinda knocked her out.
She went down. Boom. Dead.

3872
03:41:41,391 --> 03:41:42,974
You know what this story lacks?

3873
03:41:44,349 --> 03:41:45,349
Drama.

3874
03:41:46,432 --> 03:41:47,432
[helmet thuds]

3875
03:41:48,557 --> 03:41:52,640
Yeah. And you know,
a story with no drama,

3876
03:41:52,641 --> 03:41:54,557
no emotion, no detail...

3877
03:41:56,099 --> 03:41:57,432
It lacks believability.

3878
03:42:01,391 --> 03:42:03,349
- Is he telling the truth?
- [♪ tense music playing]

3879
03:42:03,932 --> 03:42:04,932
No.

3880
03:42:12,724 --> 03:42:14,057
Not all of it, anyway.

3881
03:42:16,224 --> 03:42:17,599
Riri kicked all our asses.

3882
03:42:18,432 --> 03:42:19,931
- [scoffs]
- She would've gotten away

3883
03:42:19,932 --> 03:42:22,266
if Zeke hadn't stopped her,

3884
03:42:24,141 --> 03:42:27,974
and the only way to stop her
was to destroy her suit.

3885
03:42:29,349 --> 03:42:32,182
So he ripped it from her body,
piece by piece,

3886
03:42:32,766 --> 03:42:35,766
and then buried that Iron-bitch
in a pile of rubble.

3887
03:42:40,682 --> 03:42:42,016
That's how you tell a story.

3888
03:42:44,682 --> 03:42:45,766
Now that Riri's gone,

3889
03:42:47,099 --> 03:42:48,682
let's get back to business, shall we?

3890
03:42:49,141 --> 03:42:50,598
We're finally ready for the next hit.

3891
03:42:50,599 --> 03:42:52,306
Don't look at tomorrow
as just another job.

3892
03:42:52,307 --> 03:42:53,682
Tomorrow, we conquer.

3893
03:42:55,807 --> 03:42:56,849
And get some rest.

3894
03:42:57,932 --> 03:42:59,099
You all look like shit.

3895
03:43:02,599 --> 03:43:04,140
Let me walk you out.

3896
03:43:04,141 --> 03:43:06,057
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3897
03:43:11,724 --> 03:43:12,724
[door closing]

3898
03:43:13,932 --> 03:43:14,932
Yo.

3899
03:43:15,849 --> 03:43:16,974
Can you do me a favor?

3900
03:43:17,974 --> 03:43:19,807
As long as I can take a nap first.

3901
03:43:20,599 --> 03:43:23,182
I need you to hack into
some autopsy reports for me.

3902
03:43:30,932 --> 03:43:32,599
You know, Riri's gone, so...

3903
03:43:34,016 --> 03:43:35,349
There's an open spot in the crew.

3904
03:43:36,182 --> 03:43:37,306
I am not interested.

3905
03:43:37,307 --> 03:43:39,682
You'd still be locked up
if it weren't for me.

3906
03:43:40,391 --> 03:43:43,307
I took care of your Riri problem.
That was the deal.

3907
03:43:44,474 --> 03:43:46,723
You're right. A deal's a deal.

3908
03:43:46,724 --> 03:43:48,140
[door opening]

3909
03:43:48,141 --> 03:43:49,391
Just think on it.

3910
03:43:52,932 --> 03:43:55,016
Riri turned down my offer, too, you know?

3911
03:43:55,807 --> 03:43:57,182
Then she changed her mind.

3912
03:43:57,724 --> 03:43:59,849
I have a feeling you'll be doin' the same.

3913
03:44:06,432 --> 03:44:08,556
[♪ hip-hop music playing
on headphones]

3914
03:44:08,557 --> 03:44:10,182
[♪ music skipping]

3915
03:44:14,141 --> 03:44:15,141
[♪ music stops]

3916
03:44:16,432 --> 03:44:17,516
Are you kidding me?

3917
03:44:21,974 --> 03:44:22,974
[sighs]

3918
03:44:43,849 --> 03:44:44,849
[object falls]

3919
03:44:47,391 --> 03:44:49,224
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3920
03:44:53,391 --> 03:44:54,391
[sighs]

3921
03:45:07,807 --> 03:45:09,641
[♪ intriguing music playing]

3922
03:45:14,474 --> 03:45:16,349
Riri, you genius!

3923
03:45:18,599 --> 03:45:20,182
Riri, you idiot!

3924
03:45:24,849 --> 03:45:26,891
[Natalie] Well, back
to the drawing board, Ri.

3925
03:45:27,766 --> 03:45:32,224
Okay. This is everything from the list
that I could find in the junkyard.

3926
03:45:32,724 --> 03:45:36,307
Oh, and there's a certain young man
who wants to join the team.

3927
03:45:37,349 --> 03:45:41,348
Don't get it twisted.
I'm only here for my wagon back.

3928
03:45:41,349 --> 03:45:44,724
And you owe me, like, $600 at this point.

3929
03:45:45,891 --> 03:45:47,974
It's not the young man I was expecting.

3930
03:45:51,016 --> 03:45:52,015
[keyboard clacking]

3931
03:45:52,016 --> 03:45:53,099
[electricity thuds]

3932
03:45:53,641 --> 03:45:55,599
- Oh, shit.
- [Riri laughing]

3933
03:45:57,641 --> 03:45:59,348
[Riri grunts in frustration]

3934
03:45:59,349 --> 03:46:00,474
[Riri] Always something.

3935
03:46:01,557 --> 03:46:06,266
Always gotta be something.
Always gonna stay something.

3936
03:46:07,016 --> 03:46:09,640
I mean, I don't know why
I'm tryin' to be somebody's hero,

3937
03:46:09,641 --> 03:46:11,516
- but here I am. Still.
- Riri.

3938
03:46:12,266 --> 03:46:14,099
- I mean, I might as--
- [Ronnie] Riri.

3939
03:46:16,266 --> 03:46:17,432
- You good?
- [Riri] No.

3940
03:46:18,266 --> 03:46:21,765
No, I'm not good, okay?
I have added everything

3941
03:46:21,766 --> 03:46:24,390
I can think of to go up against somebody

3942
03:46:24,391 --> 03:46:28,515
that's got a frickin' demonic god
in their corner. Okay?

3943
03:46:28,516 --> 03:46:31,098
But I can't find
a sustainable power source

3944
03:46:31,099 --> 03:46:32,515
to support all these add-ons.

3945
03:46:32,516 --> 03:46:34,057
They're draining the battery.

3946
03:46:35,141 --> 03:46:38,181
What I need is something
comparable to Parker's hood.

3947
03:46:38,182 --> 03:46:42,932
I need something that connects me
to an infinite energy supply...

3948
03:46:45,141 --> 03:46:47,016
[Landon] I got a plug
on two extension cords.

3949
03:46:47,599 --> 03:46:48,599
Just say the word.

3950
03:46:50,516 --> 03:46:52,141
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3951
03:46:59,766 --> 03:47:01,849
As much as it pains me to say this...

3952
03:47:04,599 --> 03:47:06,682
I think I have to fight magic with magic.

3953
03:47:11,516 --> 03:47:13,641
[Parker] Everybody's gotta be
on their A-game.

3954
03:47:15,391 --> 03:47:17,556
Our next mission is gonna require
everyone's focus.

3955
03:47:17,557 --> 03:47:19,390
Communication needs to be flawless.

3956
03:47:19,391 --> 03:47:22,181
One wrong move, and it all goes to shit.
Any questions?

3957
03:47:22,182 --> 03:47:23,266
I got a question.

3958
03:47:27,349 --> 03:47:28,349
Did you kill Stuart?

3959
03:47:31,224 --> 03:47:32,224
Excuse me?

3960
03:47:38,016 --> 03:47:40,307
[Clown] Go ahead. Look at it.

3961
03:47:45,182 --> 03:47:49,432
That says that Stuart OD'd,
but we all know Rampage didn't do drugs.

3962
03:47:50,307 --> 03:47:51,932
- Watch your tone.
- [Clown] Or what?

3963
03:47:53,057 --> 03:47:54,473
You gonna kill me too?

3964
03:47:54,474 --> 03:47:56,640
[♪ tense music playing]

3965
03:47:56,641 --> 03:47:57,932
I have nothin' to hide.

3966
03:47:59,391 --> 03:48:01,348
I found you when you were nothin'.

3967
03:48:01,349 --> 03:48:02,557
Gave you purpose.

3968
03:48:04,099 --> 03:48:05,099
A home.

3969
03:48:08,766 --> 03:48:13,056
Um, look, maybe we should
just take a minute... and regroup.

3970
03:48:13,057 --> 03:48:15,931
- [voices whispering indistinctly]
- We got a big job at hand.

3971
03:48:15,932 --> 03:48:18,224
[Roz, muffled] Agreed.
Maybe it's just a misunderstanding.

3972
03:48:20,724 --> 03:48:22,266
[voices] <i>That guy wants blood.</i>

3973
03:48:24,141 --> 03:48:26,432
- Riri was right. You're a fraud.
- [whispering stops]

3974
03:48:28,599 --> 03:48:30,265
- Yo, just--
- [grunts]

3975
03:48:30,266 --> 03:48:32,057
- Get your hands off her!
- Stop! Stop!

3976
03:48:33,974 --> 03:48:35,431
[growls]

3977
03:48:35,432 --> 03:48:36,932
[chuckling]

3978
03:48:38,016 --> 03:48:40,432
Parker! This isn't you.

3979
03:48:40,891 --> 03:48:43,016
- That hood's got you messed up!
- [Parker] No.

3980
03:48:43,599 --> 03:48:46,348
No, it's got me right...
for the first time ever.

3981
03:48:46,349 --> 03:48:48,766
- Hey, we didn't sign up for this shit!
- Then leave!

3982
03:48:49,766 --> 03:48:51,265
- What?
- You all turn on me like that,

3983
03:48:51,266 --> 03:48:53,766
and you think you still work here?
You're fired.

3984
03:48:54,724 --> 03:48:55,724
All of you.

3985
03:49:01,724 --> 03:49:03,141
Why're you still standin' there?

3986
03:49:03,599 --> 03:49:04,766
Get out!

3987
03:49:06,849 --> 03:49:09,682
Fine. Let's go, Jer.

3988
03:49:10,932 --> 03:49:12,932
[♪ sentimental music playing]

3989
03:49:24,641 --> 03:49:25,807
All that about family?

3990
03:49:36,557 --> 03:49:38,016
[elevator whirring]

3991
03:49:43,391 --> 03:49:45,016
[flesh squelching]

3992
03:49:48,849 --> 03:49:51,265
You're gonna steal gas
from the King of Darkness?

3993
03:49:51,266 --> 03:49:53,056
[Zelma] Dormammu is more of a Lord.

3994
03:49:53,057 --> 03:49:54,931
[Ronnie] Uh-uh.
I don't like the sound of this.

3995
03:49:54,932 --> 03:49:57,306
Yeah, I don't wanna be that tethered
to the Dark Dimension.

3996
03:49:57,307 --> 03:49:58,640
What if I end up like Parker?

3997
03:49:58,641 --> 03:50:02,682
Just how sure are you that
Parker's magic even comes from there?

3998
03:50:04,016 --> 03:50:05,973
- 47% sure.
- [Riri] Forty-seven?

3999
03:50:05,974 --> 03:50:09,181
- But you said 50 last time.
- I was rounding up.

4000
03:50:09,182 --> 03:50:10,974
Well, this is a real downer.

4001
03:50:11,724 --> 03:50:13,057
[Xavier] Hey, Black people.

4002
03:50:13,641 --> 03:50:15,265
Thought y'all might need a little boost.

4003
03:50:15,266 --> 03:50:17,431
[Landon] All right! Coffee!

4004
03:50:17,432 --> 03:50:20,723
Hey, chill, Landon.
We got apple juice for you.

4005
03:50:20,724 --> 03:50:22,224
Disrespectful.

4006
03:50:25,349 --> 03:50:27,057
[Xavier] Reporting for duty, Captain.

4007
03:50:28,266 --> 03:50:30,099
- Hope I'm not too late.
- [Riri chuckles]

4008
03:50:31,849 --> 03:50:33,141
Right on time.

4009
03:50:33,724 --> 03:50:34,724
I read your note.

4010
03:50:36,057 --> 03:50:38,266
- Was it too cheesy?
- Yeah.

4011
03:50:39,682 --> 03:50:41,599
But that Captain Kirk quote got to me.

4012
03:50:42,182 --> 03:50:45,098
- "Of my friend, I can only say this."
- [chuckles]

4013
03:50:45,099 --> 03:50:50,766
"Of all the souls I've encountered
on my travels, hers was the most human."

4014
03:50:52,391 --> 03:50:54,598
- Well, "hers" was referring to...
- Natalie.

4015
03:50:54,599 --> 03:50:55,724
Yeah, I know.

4016
03:50:56,266 --> 03:50:58,224
[♪ nostalgic music playing]

4017
03:51:08,224 --> 03:51:10,431
I just wish you would've
told me about her, that's all.

4018
03:51:10,432 --> 03:51:12,098
And I'm sorry for that.

4019
03:51:12,099 --> 03:51:15,182
Please know I never set out
to make an AI in Nat's image.

4020
03:51:16,516 --> 03:51:17,931
And if you wanna get technical,

4021
03:51:17,932 --> 03:51:21,557
she's actually just
a holographic manifestation of my brain.

4022
03:51:25,974 --> 03:51:28,849
Having Nat around makes me feel
more like myself again.

4023
03:51:29,599 --> 03:51:31,182
Like she's supposed to be here.

4024
03:51:32,474 --> 03:51:35,265
And to be honest, I don't really wanna go
back to the way life was without her.

4025
03:51:35,266 --> 03:51:36,849
[chuckles] All right, look.

4026
03:51:37,891 --> 03:51:39,016
I'm not okay with it,

4027
03:51:40,266 --> 03:51:42,891
but I could try to understand
how much she means to you.

4028
03:51:52,724 --> 03:51:54,599
So we're building a new suit, huh?

4029
03:51:55,141 --> 03:51:56,141
What for?

4030
03:52:00,641 --> 03:52:01,681
Ri?

4031
03:52:01,682 --> 03:52:03,641
- Huh?
- [Xavier] What'd you do?

4032
03:52:04,766 --> 03:52:06,974
I'll explain it to you while we work.

4033
03:52:09,141 --> 03:52:12,141
[♪ electronic R&B music playing,
Santigold "Disparate Youth"]

4034
03:52:34,516 --> 03:52:36,766
<i>♪ Don't look ahead,
there's stormy weather ♪</i>

4035
03:52:39,432 --> 03:52:41,349
<i>♪ Another road block in our way ♪</i>

4036
03:52:42,682 --> 03:52:43,682
[Landon] Hey, Nat.

4037
03:52:44,307 --> 03:52:46,474
<i>♪ But if we go, we go together ♪</i>

4038
03:52:47,099 --> 03:52:49,140
- [Landon] Sorry.
- [both chuckling]

4039
03:52:49,141 --> 03:52:51,224
<i>♪ Our hands are tied here if we stay ♪</i>

4040
03:52:52,766 --> 03:52:55,265
<i>♪ Oh, we said our dreams will carry us ♪</i>

4041
03:52:55,266 --> 03:52:57,265
<i>♪ And if they don't fly, we will run ♪</i>

4042
03:52:57,266 --> 03:53:00,140
- [Landon coughs]
<i>- ♪ Now we push right past to find out ♪</i>

4043
03:53:00,141 --> 03:53:02,141
<i>♪ How to win what they all lost ♪</i>

4044
03:53:02,599 --> 03:53:04,432
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4045
03:53:05,307 --> 03:53:06,932
<i>♪ We know now we want more ♪</i>

4046
03:53:07,599 --> 03:53:09,723
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4047
03:53:09,724 --> 03:53:12,723
- Lights! Hey, I got lights!
<i>- ♪ A life worth fighting for ♪</i>

4048
03:53:12,724 --> 03:53:15,098
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4049
03:53:15,099 --> 03:53:17,223
<i>♪ We know now we want more ♪</i>

4050
03:53:17,224 --> 03:53:19,224
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4051
03:53:19,974 --> 03:53:21,682
<i>♪ A life worth fighting for ♪</i>

4052
03:53:23,516 --> 03:53:25,557
<i>♪ So let them say we can't do better ♪</i>

4053
03:53:28,349 --> 03:53:30,432
<i>♪ Lay out the rules that we can't break ♪</i>

4054
03:53:33,307 --> 03:53:35,391
<i>♪ They want to sit and watch it wither ♪</i>

4055
03:53:36,557 --> 03:53:38,015
[explosion]

4056
03:53:38,016 --> 03:53:40,016
<i>♪ Their legacy's too hard to take ♪</i>

4057
03:53:41,682 --> 03:53:44,265
<i>♪ Oh, we said our dreams will carry us ♪</i>

4058
03:53:44,266 --> 03:53:46,224
<i>♪ And if they don't fly, we will run ♪</i>

4059
03:53:46,724 --> 03:53:49,098
<i>♪ Now we push right past to find out ♪</i>

4060
03:53:49,099 --> 03:53:51,098
<i>♪ How to win what they all lost ♪</i>

4061
03:53:51,099 --> 03:53:52,557
[weapon charges up]

4062
03:53:54,391 --> 03:53:55,932
<i>♪ A life worth fighting for ♪</i>

4063
03:54:09,182 --> 03:54:11,348
<i>♪ In their heads, hedging their bets ♪</i>

4064
03:54:11,349 --> 03:54:12,807
<i>♪ In their eyes, it shows ♪</i>

4065
03:54:13,932 --> 03:54:16,056
<i>♪ And they all said I was misled ♪</i>

4066
03:54:16,057 --> 03:54:18,265
<i>♪ But now the odds all stand beneath me ♪</i>

4067
03:54:18,266 --> 03:54:20,474
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4068
03:54:21,224 --> 03:54:22,849
<i>♪ They're frozen to the core ♪</i>

4069
03:54:23,391 --> 03:54:25,349
<i>♪ Oh-ah, oh-ah ♪</i>

4070
03:54:26,057 --> 03:54:27,766
<i>♪ A life worth fighting for ♪</i>

4071
03:54:28,891 --> 03:54:29,974
[♪ music fades out]

4072
03:54:31,141 --> 03:54:32,974
[Heather] Hey! Hey!

4073
03:54:33,766 --> 03:54:34,765
[sighs]

4074
03:54:34,766 --> 03:54:36,099
I'm calling the cops.

4075
03:54:36,891 --> 03:54:39,640
Please don't, Heather.
You're never gonna see me again.

4076
03:54:39,641 --> 03:54:41,056
[Heather] I knew you were bad news.

4077
03:54:41,057 --> 03:54:43,557
I have a sixth sense about these things.

4078
03:54:44,807 --> 03:54:46,516
Good for you. Bye.

4079
03:54:47,182 --> 03:54:50,098
Your poor father
is probably rolling in his grave

4080
03:54:50,099 --> 03:54:52,766
- knowing what you've done to his legacy.
- [breathing heavily]

4081
03:54:55,849 --> 03:54:59,599
You know what?
I am sick of your shit, Heather!

4082
03:55:00,224 --> 03:55:01,723
Huh! No, no.

4083
03:55:01,724 --> 03:55:03,681
- Hey, you need to back up.
- Oh, do I?

4084
03:55:03,682 --> 03:55:04,765
- Yes.
- Really?

4085
03:55:04,766 --> 03:55:07,181
- I know karate. I'll take you down.
- Uh-oh. I'm in your driveway.

4086
03:55:07,182 --> 03:55:09,223
Oh, those flowers are really beautiful.

4087
03:55:09,224 --> 03:55:11,056
Jack! Jack! Call the police!

4088
03:55:11,057 --> 03:55:14,182
- [electricity bursting]
- Jack! Jack! Call the police!

4089
03:55:15,224 --> 03:55:17,432
Zeke! What's good?

4090
03:55:20,932 --> 03:55:23,557
Uh-oh. You don't like the upgrade?

4091
03:55:24,682 --> 03:55:25,682
What'd you do to me?

4092
03:55:30,557 --> 03:55:33,432
Well, as a thank you
for getting back all your stuff,

4093
03:55:34,141 --> 03:55:36,598
I now have control
over all the weird science

4094
03:55:36,599 --> 03:55:38,016
swirling around in your body.

4095
03:55:39,849 --> 03:55:41,141
So now, when I say jump...

4096
03:55:41,641 --> 03:55:44,099
- [energy whirring and thudding]
- [gasps]

4097
03:55:45,849 --> 03:55:46,849
You jump.

4098
03:55:47,891 --> 03:55:50,306
When I say kill anyone
who gets in my way--

4099
03:55:50,307 --> 03:55:52,098
That was not part of our agreement, Hood.

4100
03:55:52,099 --> 03:55:53,181
I'm not your puppet.

4101
03:55:53,182 --> 03:55:54,266
[The Hood] Hmm.

4102
03:55:55,349 --> 03:55:57,182
More like a Rock 'Em Sock 'Em Robot.

4103
03:56:01,099 --> 03:56:04,473
Now, let's go. We have somewhere to be.

4104
03:56:04,474 --> 03:56:06,391
- [energy whirring]
- [straining]

4105
03:56:10,724 --> 03:56:12,599
[♪ tense music playing]

4106
03:56:23,766 --> 03:56:25,141
[The Hood] All right, come on.

4107
03:56:30,391 --> 03:56:31,391
Where are we?

4108
03:56:32,016 --> 03:56:33,016
Get us in.

4109
03:56:34,099 --> 03:56:35,641
- Absolutely not.
- [energy whirring]

4110
03:56:42,141 --> 03:56:43,391
[alarm beeping]

4111
03:56:46,849 --> 03:56:49,806
[guard 1] This is zone A to zone B,
checking the front gate alarm.

4112
03:56:49,807 --> 03:56:51,016
[guard 2] <i>Copy that.</i>

4113
03:56:56,349 --> 03:56:57,931
[whooshing]

4114
03:56:57,932 --> 03:56:59,057
[grunts]

4115
03:56:59,974 --> 03:57:00,974
[groans]

4116
03:57:02,724 --> 03:57:04,516
[♪ tense music continues]

4117
03:57:08,641 --> 03:57:10,390
Hey, you guys need to leave.

4118
03:57:10,391 --> 03:57:11,766
I'm sorry.

4119
03:57:13,432 --> 03:57:14,516
It wasn't me, I swear.

4120
03:57:16,182 --> 03:57:17,181
Hey!

4121
03:57:17,182 --> 03:57:19,182
- [electricity crackling]
- Really?

4122
03:57:22,391 --> 03:57:23,973
This is insane. You know that, right?

4123
03:57:23,974 --> 03:57:25,057
Keep people out.

4124
03:57:27,807 --> 03:57:28,807
[guard 3 yelps]

4125
03:57:31,766 --> 03:57:33,182
[Ezekiel] Oh, I'm sorry.

4126
03:57:33,932 --> 03:57:35,641
- Uh, okay.
- [electricity crackling]

4127
03:57:36,391 --> 03:57:37,390
[guard 4 screams]

4128
03:57:37,391 --> 03:57:38,682
Nice to see you again.

4129
03:57:39,224 --> 03:57:40,307
[guard 1 groans]

4130
03:57:49,807 --> 03:57:50,806
[chokes]

4131
03:57:50,807 --> 03:57:51,891
Shit.

4132
03:57:52,599 --> 03:57:53,599
[The Hood] Wow.

4133
03:57:55,682 --> 03:57:57,473
That scotch, on those pants?

4134
03:57:57,474 --> 03:57:59,223
That's a thousand-dollar spill, Art.

4135
03:57:59,224 --> 03:58:00,391
What's this about?

4136
03:58:01,307 --> 03:58:02,432
I'll pour you another?

4137
03:58:05,807 --> 03:58:07,640
Still drinking the same Glenlivet, I see.

4138
03:58:07,641 --> 03:58:10,266
[Arthur] And you're still breaking
into places where you aren't wanted.

4139
03:58:11,557 --> 03:58:12,557
[soft chime]

4140
03:58:14,182 --> 03:58:17,599
The guard on the other end
of that button is all tied up.

4141
03:58:19,182 --> 03:58:20,182
You okay?

4142
03:58:21,182 --> 03:58:22,182
I'm fine.

4143
03:58:23,682 --> 03:58:25,890
You hired more security since last time.

4144
03:58:25,891 --> 03:58:28,348
You and your friend left
a lasting impression.

4145
03:58:28,349 --> 03:58:30,682
- That what this is about?
- No. No.

4146
03:58:31,432 --> 03:58:33,016
I'm not after the safe anymore.

4147
03:58:35,266 --> 03:58:36,391
I want something bigger.

4148
03:58:39,182 --> 03:58:41,641
It's all there. Boilerplate.

4149
03:58:42,766 --> 03:58:43,766
Boilerplate.

4150
03:58:47,307 --> 03:58:48,766
I'm not signing shit.

4151
03:58:53,016 --> 03:58:54,307
Let me walk you through it.

4152
03:58:54,849 --> 03:58:57,723
I already have majority stake
in all the top-performing companies

4153
03:58:57,724 --> 03:58:58,891
in your portfolio.

4154
03:58:59,432 --> 03:59:02,557
Think of me as an invisible partner...

4155
03:59:03,682 --> 03:59:05,099
with controlling interest.

4156
03:59:06,057 --> 03:59:11,224
TNNL, Gannon, Procoin,
and the list goes on and on.

4157
03:59:11,891 --> 03:59:14,682
But now, now I want the crown jewels.

4158
03:59:15,807 --> 03:59:17,931
You're gonna sign over ArtWorks,
this mansion,

4159
03:59:17,932 --> 03:59:20,640
- everything that was promised to me.
- [scoffs]

4160
03:59:20,641 --> 03:59:23,766
You strongarm a few startups
and you think you're a CEO?

4161
03:59:25,266 --> 03:59:28,306
You're a small-time crook
in ridiculous getup.

4162
03:59:28,307 --> 03:59:29,681
You'd have to kill me first.

4163
03:59:29,682 --> 03:59:31,265
Yeah, that can be arranged.

4164
03:59:31,266 --> 03:59:33,182
[♪ uneasy music playing]

4165
03:59:35,641 --> 03:59:37,182
What's that on your face?

4166
03:59:38,682 --> 03:59:39,974
What'd you do to yourself?

4167
03:59:46,182 --> 03:59:47,432
What do you want, Parker?

4168
03:59:48,474 --> 03:59:51,598
If you wanted my company, you could've
done this hostile takeover remotely.

4169
03:59:51,599 --> 03:59:52,891
So why are you here?

4170
03:59:56,224 --> 03:59:58,682
I had to look you in the eye and ask...

4171
03:59:59,682 --> 04:00:02,682
What kind of father puts his son
out of the house at 12?

4172
04:00:05,307 --> 04:00:06,306
[Arthur sighs]

4173
04:00:06,307 --> 04:00:08,973
I tried with you. I really did.

4174
04:00:08,974 --> 04:00:10,598
But you were a liability.

4175
04:00:10,599 --> 04:00:13,099
"Liability"? [scoffs]

4176
04:00:15,099 --> 04:00:16,391
I was a child.

4177
04:00:17,516 --> 04:00:20,181
After Mom died, the only way
to even get you to pay attention to me

4178
04:00:20,182 --> 04:00:21,599
was if I was in trouble.

4179
04:00:22,724 --> 04:00:23,724
What'd you expect?

4180
04:00:25,266 --> 04:00:26,266
I don't know.

4181
04:00:27,307 --> 04:00:28,307
I didn't want you.

4182
04:00:30,266 --> 04:00:33,891
So I thought it would be better for
both of us to cut our losses and move on.

4183
04:00:36,391 --> 04:00:37,390
Nothing personal.

4184
04:00:37,391 --> 04:00:39,641
It wasn't personal. Nothing personal.

4185
04:00:43,891 --> 04:00:44,891
Yeah.

4186
04:00:50,057 --> 04:00:51,599
[breath shuddering]

4187
04:00:55,474 --> 04:00:56,723
[ominous whooshing]

4188
04:00:56,724 --> 04:00:58,474
- [gun cocks]
- Sign it in ink,

4189
04:00:59,307 --> 04:01:00,681
[distorted] or sign it in blood.

4190
04:01:00,682 --> 04:01:02,599
[♪ ominous music playing]

4191
04:01:10,141 --> 04:01:12,306
You think you deserve all this,
but I'd bet good money,

4192
04:01:12,307 --> 04:01:13,599
I mean, real good money,

4193
04:01:14,432 --> 04:01:18,516
that to get where you are in this moment,
you screwed a few people.

4194
04:01:19,391 --> 04:01:20,807
Probably some who loved you.

4195
04:01:21,391 --> 04:01:23,141
It's the cost of doing business.

4196
04:01:23,891 --> 04:01:25,141
But the kick is...

4197
04:01:27,766 --> 04:01:29,141
It's never gonna be enough.

4198
04:01:32,682 --> 04:01:34,516
[♪ ominous music continues]

4199
04:01:51,391 --> 04:01:52,391
[in normal voice] Stay...

4200
04:01:53,557 --> 04:01:54,557
And I'll kill you.

4201
04:01:56,807 --> 04:01:57,849
Talk to the cops...

4202
04:01:59,099 --> 04:02:00,099
And I'll hunt you.

4203
04:02:01,724 --> 04:02:03,682
[distorted] Now get the hell out
of my house.

4204
04:02:05,849 --> 04:02:07,682
[♪ ominous music continues]

4205
04:02:28,141 --> 04:02:29,766
[voices whispering]

4206
04:02:30,641 --> 04:02:32,266
[flesh squelching]

4207
04:02:34,266 --> 04:02:36,266
[mechanical whirring and clacking]

4208
04:02:39,432 --> 04:02:41,640
- Do y'all think we should add, like--
- No!

4209
04:02:41,641 --> 04:02:44,016
- No.
- Girl, it's ready.

4210
04:02:45,599 --> 04:02:46,891
Go ahead and try it on.

4211
04:02:48,141 --> 04:02:50,141
- All right.
- [suit whirs]

4212
04:02:51,724 --> 04:02:53,016
Well, here goes nothing.

4213
04:02:54,641 --> 04:02:56,641
[♪ inspirational music playing]

4214
04:03:05,016 --> 04:03:07,098
Hmm. [chuckles]

4215
04:03:07,099 --> 04:03:08,474
Dang! Miss Riri!

4216
04:03:09,141 --> 04:03:11,016
Well, let's see if it works.

4217
04:03:12,474 --> 04:03:13,557
Power me up.

4218
04:03:14,807 --> 04:03:16,266
Let's fight magic with magic.

4219
04:03:17,724 --> 04:03:18,974
Guess that's my cue.

4220
04:03:21,599 --> 04:03:23,015
You sure about this?

4221
04:03:23,016 --> 04:03:24,099
Remember...

4222
04:03:24,724 --> 04:03:26,432
magic is a mutual exchange.

4223
04:03:27,099 --> 04:03:28,224
There's always a cost.

4224
04:03:29,099 --> 04:03:30,141
I'm sure.

4225
04:03:30,641 --> 04:03:31,641
[chuckles]

4226
04:03:35,891 --> 04:03:36,891
[sighs]

4227
04:03:40,182 --> 04:03:42,099
Hey, don't worry.

4228
04:03:42,807 --> 04:03:43,849
You got this.

4229
04:03:45,182 --> 04:03:46,182
Yep.

4230
04:03:54,599 --> 04:03:56,516
[♪ inspirational music continues]

4231
04:04:04,932 --> 04:04:05,932
Okay.

4232
04:04:11,724 --> 04:04:13,182
[soft crackling]

4233
04:04:18,932 --> 04:04:20,141
Whoa.

4234
04:04:25,599 --> 04:04:27,682
See? I told you.

4235
04:04:31,099 --> 04:04:32,098
Riri?

4236
04:04:32,099 --> 04:04:34,182
- [Riri] What's going on?
- [Zelma] I don't know.

4237
04:04:35,766 --> 04:04:36,765
Shit!

4238
04:04:36,766 --> 04:04:37,848
[distorted] Riri.

4239
04:04:37,849 --> 04:04:40,140
[in normal voice]
Something, something's off.

4240
04:04:40,141 --> 04:04:42,473
- Zelma, turn it off.
- [Natalie] Can you fix it?

4241
04:04:42,474 --> 04:04:43,556
I'm trying.

4242
04:04:43,557 --> 04:04:45,890
- What's happening?
- What is this? What's happening?

4243
04:04:45,891 --> 04:04:47,473
- [Riri] Zelma!
- I don't think the reactor

4244
04:04:47,474 --> 04:04:48,890
can't handle the magic and Natalie.

4245
04:04:48,891 --> 04:04:50,265
- Ri?
- [Gary] <i>Girls, run!</i>

4246
04:04:50,266 --> 04:04:52,806
- Natalie, just hold on, okay?
- Riri!

4247
04:04:52,807 --> 04:04:54,848
- Can you hear me?
- [Landon] Why is she glitching?

4248
04:04:54,849 --> 04:04:56,556
- [Natalie] Am I gonna be okay?
- It's okay.

4249
04:04:56,557 --> 04:04:58,556
- I'm gonna fix it!
- [Natalie] Am I dying?

4250
04:04:58,557 --> 04:05:00,348
Hold on.
I'm gonna tether you to the laptop.

4251
04:05:00,349 --> 04:05:03,348
- Help me! Riri, please!
- [Riri] Just hold on. All right?

4252
04:05:03,349 --> 04:05:06,932
- Ri, I can't... I can't stop this!
- Please, no!

4253
04:05:07,391 --> 04:05:10,306
- Ri, I'm scared!
- Just hold on! We're so close.

4254
04:05:10,307 --> 04:05:11,931
- [Landon] Do something, Zelma!
- I love you.

4255
04:05:11,932 --> 04:05:13,515
{\an8}- [Xavier] Natalie. Oh, Nat.
- [Roonie] Riri?

4256
04:05:13,516 --> 04:05:15,057
{\an8}- [Landon] Do something!
- I love you, Ri.

4257
04:05:16,807 --> 04:05:17,807
[gasps]

4258
04:05:20,016 --> 04:05:22,766
- [Riri] No.
- [Ronnie whispers] Where is she?

4259
04:05:24,224 --> 04:05:25,973
- Oh, my God.
- [Landon] Where'd she go?

4260
04:05:25,974 --> 04:05:27,849
[♪ somber music playing]

4261
04:05:30,849 --> 04:05:32,474
- Natalie?
- [♪ music stops]

4262
04:05:34,766 --> 04:05:37,391
[♪ trip hop music playing,
Sevdaliza "Hubris"]

4263
04:05:41,932 --> 04:05:44,474
<i>♪ Oh, my man ♪</i>

4264
04:05:48,141 --> 04:05:51,641
<i>♪ I hold your heart ♪</i>

4265
04:05:54,932 --> 04:05:58,182
<i>♪ Oh, pretend ♪</i>

4266
04:06:01,391 --> 04:06:05,974
<i>♪ You ain't my fault ♪</i>

4267
04:06:06,849 --> 04:06:09,349
<i>♪ And, oh ♪</i>

4268
04:06:10,807 --> 04:06:17,682
<i>♪ I don't love you anymore ♪</i>

4269
04:06:19,849 --> 04:06:22,974
<i>♪ And, oh ♪</i>

4270
04:06:23,891 --> 04:06:29,182
<i>♪ I don't love you anymore ♪</i>

4271
04:06:30,599 --> 04:06:32,641
<i>♪ No, I never did ♪</i>

4272
04:06:37,641 --> 04:06:38,641
<i>♪ Oh ♪</i>

4273
04:06:55,016 --> 04:06:57,016
{\an8}[♪ dramatic music playing]

4274
04:09:30,545 --> 04:09:31,961
What did you do to yourself?

4275
04:09:31,962 --> 04:09:33,794
I was bailed out by a mutual friend...

4276
04:09:33,795 --> 04:09:35,127
[screaming]

4277
04:09:35,128 --> 04:09:36,461
<i>Parker Robbins.</i>

4278
04:09:36,462 --> 04:09:37,962
What does he want in return?

4279
04:09:39,045 --> 04:09:40,045
You.

4280
04:09:41,295 --> 04:09:44,169
- Mom, I need your help. [breath shudders]
- What happened?

4281
04:09:44,170 --> 04:09:47,044
[♪ tense music playing]

4282
04:09:47,045 --> 04:09:50,836
The cloak that it's coming from
is likely possessing whoever's in it.

4283
04:09:50,837 --> 04:09:53,961
This entity doesn't possess,
it influences.

4284
04:09:53,962 --> 04:09:55,669
Does this entity have a name?

4285
04:09:55,670 --> 04:09:56,752
[Zelma] <i>It's Dormammu.</i>

4286
04:09:56,753 --> 04:10:00,377
<i>You could be dealing with one of the most
powerful beings in the universe.</i>

4287
04:10:00,378 --> 04:10:03,336
[Ezekiel] <i>I spent my whole life
trying not to become</i>

4288
04:10:03,337 --> 04:10:04,919
<i>Obadiah Stane,</i>

4289
04:10:04,920 --> 04:10:08,252
taking down an iron freak!

4290
04:10:08,253 --> 04:10:10,419
- [panting]
- You need to leave Chicago now.

4291
04:10:10,420 --> 04:10:13,461
If Parker finds out you're still alive,
he won't be so forgiving.

4292
04:10:13,462 --> 04:10:14,962
[scoffs]

4293
04:10:16,087 --> 04:10:17,378
Done.

4294
04:10:18,295 --> 04:10:21,127
What kind of father puts his son
out of the house at 12?

4295
04:10:21,128 --> 04:10:22,711
- [ominous whooshing]
- [gun cocks]

4296
04:10:22,712 --> 04:10:25,045
Sign it in ink,
[distorted] or sign it in blood.

4297
04:10:25,628 --> 04:10:27,003
It's never gonna be enough.

4298
04:10:28,170 --> 04:10:30,169
[Riri] <i>Won't be long
before Parker realizes</i>

4299
04:10:30,170 --> 04:10:31,252
<i>I'm not dead.</i>

4300
04:10:31,253 --> 04:10:33,836
I need a suit,
and I have nothing to build it with.

4301
04:10:33,837 --> 04:10:35,669
<i>I have to fight magic with magic.</i>

4302
04:10:35,670 --> 04:10:37,419
[Zelma] <i>Magic is a mutual exchange.</i>

4303
04:10:37,420 --> 04:10:39,336
<i>- There's always a cost.</i>
- [soft crackling]

4304
04:10:39,337 --> 04:10:41,127
- [crackles]
- Riri?

4305
04:10:41,128 --> 04:10:42,961
- Zelma, turn it off.
- What's happening?

4306
04:10:42,962 --> 04:10:45,794
I don't think the reactor can't handle
the magic and Natalie.

4307
04:10:45,795 --> 04:10:47,252
Help me! Riri, please!

4308
04:10:47,253 --> 04:10:48,794
- Hold on.
- [Landon] Do something.

4309
04:10:48,795 --> 04:10:50,127
[distorted] I love you, Ri.

4310
04:10:50,128 --> 04:10:51,753
[♪ tense music continuing]

4311
04:11:06,670 --> 04:11:09,670
- [high-pitched ringing]
- [voices whispering]

4312
04:11:13,795 --> 04:11:15,212
[loud bang echoes]

4313
04:11:21,003 --> 04:11:22,212
- [thuds]
- [guard] No, wait!

4314
04:11:22,670 --> 04:11:24,670
- [grunts]
- [alarm blaring]

4315
04:11:25,670 --> 04:11:27,503
[♪ tense music playing]

4316
04:11:27,628 --> 04:11:30,212
- We gotta go. Split up.
- [Parker] John. How do I find you?

4317
04:11:30,962 --> 04:11:32,502
I'm never too far away.

4318
04:11:32,503 --> 04:11:33,627
I'm always with you.

4319
04:11:33,628 --> 04:11:35,919
- [guard 1] Master bedroom, clear.
- [John] Go.

4320
04:11:35,920 --> 04:11:37,211
Go. Go!

4321
04:11:37,212 --> 04:11:39,794
- [guard 2] Switch to comm two.
- [guard 3] Right there.

4322
04:11:39,795 --> 04:11:41,128
[dogs barking]

4323
04:11:43,253 --> 04:11:44,419
[rattling]

4324
04:11:44,420 --> 04:11:46,211
[♪ tense music intensifies]

4325
04:11:46,212 --> 04:11:47,752
[guard 1] Secure the perimeter.

4326
04:11:47,753 --> 04:11:48,837
Oh, shit.

4327
04:11:49,503 --> 04:11:50,503
[guard 2] I see him.

4328
04:11:51,170 --> 04:11:53,044
- Son of a bitch.
- [guard 2] There he goes.

4329
04:11:53,045 --> 04:11:54,128
[guard 1] Fan out!

4330
04:11:58,420 --> 04:11:59,420
[panting]

4331
04:12:02,170 --> 04:12:03,962
- [guard] He went down this way.
- [gasps]

4332
04:12:04,670 --> 04:12:05,878
[panting]

4333
04:12:07,378 --> 04:12:08,919
[indistinct radio chatter]

4334
04:12:08,920 --> 04:12:10,877
- [guard 1] Here!
- [guard 2] There he goes.

4335
04:12:10,878 --> 04:12:11,961
[panting]

4336
04:12:11,962 --> 04:12:13,627
[guard] Hey, kid! I see you.

4337
04:12:13,628 --> 04:12:15,711
- [barking]
- There's nowhere to go.

4338
04:12:15,712 --> 04:12:17,670
We've got you surrounded.

4339
04:12:18,837 --> 04:12:20,586
[man echoing] I do not like your odds.

4340
04:12:20,587 --> 04:12:22,087
[panting]

4341
04:12:22,628 --> 04:12:23,877
There's no need for that.

4342
04:12:23,878 --> 04:12:25,836
[♪ mysterious music playing]

4343
04:12:25,837 --> 04:12:27,461
Where the hell did you come from?

4344
04:12:27,462 --> 04:12:30,670
[man] Well, I could answer,
or I could open the door.

4345
04:12:31,837 --> 04:12:34,002
What door--
What are you talking about, man?

4346
04:12:34,003 --> 04:12:35,628
[bell dinging]

4347
04:12:38,795 --> 04:12:41,044
[man whispering] Come on, let me help you.

4348
04:12:41,045 --> 04:12:42,587
Go in. Go in.

4349
04:12:43,420 --> 04:12:44,545
[dogs barking]

4350
04:12:45,170 --> 04:12:47,045
Hey, you coming?

4351
04:12:49,628 --> 04:12:51,002
[guard] We'll take care of it.

4352
04:12:51,003 --> 04:12:53,419
[man] Take the step. [echoes] The step.

4353
04:12:53,420 --> 04:12:54,961
[guard] Stop right there.

4354
04:12:54,962 --> 04:12:56,419
Stop!

4355
04:12:56,420 --> 04:12:59,002
- [guard 1] He's gone.
- [guard 2] Where'd he go?

4356
04:12:59,003 --> 04:13:01,044
[lively chatter, laughter]

4357
04:13:01,045 --> 04:13:03,336
It probably is. I know what you mean.

4358
04:13:03,337 --> 04:13:04,419
[boy] Yes, you are.

4359
04:13:04,420 --> 04:13:06,837
[♪ slow romantic music playing
on speakers]

4360
04:13:09,212 --> 04:13:10,752
Who the hell are you, man?

4361
04:13:10,753 --> 04:13:13,294
[man] Me? I'm just a fan,

4362
04:13:13,295 --> 04:13:16,294
a fan who wants to be
in the Parker Robbins business.

4363
04:13:16,295 --> 04:13:17,628
Can I ask you a question?

4364
04:13:18,712 --> 04:13:20,128
Do you mind if I stare at you?

4365
04:13:23,503 --> 04:13:25,461
Amazing. What a face.

4366
04:13:25,462 --> 04:13:28,461
- How do you even know me?
- [man] Oh, man. You are a legend.

4367
04:13:28,462 --> 04:13:31,503
Well, you're not currently,
but you deserve to be.

4368
04:13:32,878 --> 04:13:35,127
If we start working together,
I'm gonna make you

4369
04:13:35,128 --> 04:13:37,753
the greatest human of your generation.

4370
04:13:40,045 --> 04:13:42,587
- This is weird.
- [man] You know, how about a slice?

4371
04:13:45,170 --> 04:13:48,377
Come on, try that.
It's not right, we'll send it back.

4372
04:13:48,378 --> 04:13:50,544
Keep on bringing it till it's perfect.

4373
04:13:50,545 --> 04:13:51,627
Try it.

4374
04:13:51,628 --> 04:13:53,545
[kids laughing]

4375
04:13:55,503 --> 04:13:57,378
[chuckles] There he is.

4376
04:13:58,212 --> 04:13:59,586
Anyway, Parker,

4377
04:13:59,587 --> 04:14:02,378
you're not fulfilling your potential,

4378
04:14:02,962 --> 04:14:08,337
and I know how much that upsets you,
and it makes me very, very sad, too.

4379
04:14:09,212 --> 04:14:10,378
I'm sorry, bro, it's...

4380
04:14:11,003 --> 04:14:12,169
[woman] Oh, no...

4381
04:14:12,170 --> 04:14:14,544
This shit about me
fulfilling my potential--

4382
04:14:14,545 --> 04:14:17,087
- [music and chatter stops]
- I mean, how would I even...

4383
04:14:23,670 --> 04:14:24,753
You just did that?

4384
04:14:25,545 --> 04:14:29,211
Did you like it?
You want me to do it to someone else?

4385
04:14:29,212 --> 04:14:31,378
[softly] Shall I do it to the whole city?

4386
04:14:33,462 --> 04:14:39,753
[in normal voice] Now, let me ask you,
what is it that you most [echoes] desire?

4387
04:14:46,878 --> 04:14:47,878
Uh...

4388
04:14:49,128 --> 04:14:50,795
- I don't know.
- You... You know what?

4389
04:14:51,128 --> 04:14:53,294
Uh, I'm wasting your time.
Okay. Thank you.

4390
04:14:53,295 --> 04:14:55,711
Wait, wait. I... Hey, look, um...

4391
04:14:55,712 --> 04:14:58,377
- Huh?
- I guess I...

4392
04:14:58,378 --> 04:14:59,462
I...

4393
04:15:00,712 --> 04:15:02,628
You know, I wanna be powerful...

4394
04:15:04,795 --> 04:15:06,044
- and respected.
- Stop...

4395
04:15:06,045 --> 04:15:07,711
- [bangs table]
- ...bullshitting me,

4396
04:15:07,712 --> 04:15:11,878
and tell me what it is that you want.

4397
04:15:14,920 --> 04:15:15,920
I wanna...

4398
04:15:16,878 --> 04:15:17,877
I want to be rich.

4399
04:15:17,878 --> 04:15:19,420
Okay. How rich?

4400
04:15:20,462 --> 04:15:21,670
Like...

4401
04:15:23,295 --> 04:15:26,502
Like, stupid, disgusting, greasy rich.

4402
04:15:26,503 --> 04:15:29,545
Stupid, disgusting, greasy.
Okay, you got it.

4403
04:15:30,045 --> 04:15:31,045
[echoing] <i>Like him?</i>

4404
04:15:34,337 --> 04:15:37,128
<i>No. Richer than him.</i>

4405
04:15:41,378 --> 04:15:44,044
- You're gonna give me everything?
- No, of course I'm not,

4406
04:15:44,045 --> 04:15:45,462
you beautiful human being.

4407
04:15:46,795 --> 04:15:48,212
I'm gonna give you the tools

4408
04:15:48,962 --> 04:15:53,044
so that you can get yourself
everything that you deserve.

4409
04:15:53,045 --> 04:15:55,212
[♪ eerie music playing]

4410
04:15:56,170 --> 04:15:57,170
Okay.

4411
04:16:00,128 --> 04:16:01,295
I wanna be king.

4412
04:16:06,045 --> 04:16:07,086
[echoes] So be it.

4413
04:16:07,087 --> 04:16:10,587
- And what's in it for you?
- Oh. Something you won't even miss.

4414
04:16:11,795 --> 04:16:13,545
[♪ eerie music continuing]

4415
04:16:16,295 --> 04:16:17,378
[chuckles]

4416
04:16:22,128 --> 04:16:23,253
Whatever it is...

4417
04:16:26,253 --> 04:16:27,253
I'm in.

4418
04:16:28,462 --> 04:16:29,712
I knew you were smart.

4419
04:16:37,462 --> 04:16:39,753
[♪ music swells]

4420
04:16:41,170 --> 04:16:42,170
This is great.

4421
04:16:43,462 --> 04:16:44,462
I have to leave.

4422
04:16:47,128 --> 04:16:48,128
It's been a pleasure.

4423
04:16:49,045 --> 04:16:50,878
Hey, look. Yo, you forgot your thing.

4424
04:16:51,712 --> 04:16:53,128
Oh. No, that's yours.

4425
04:16:53,837 --> 04:16:54,837
[scoffs]

4426
04:16:56,837 --> 04:16:58,962
- It looks expensive.
- No, no, no.

4427
04:16:59,420 --> 04:17:00,503
[man scoffs]

4428
04:17:02,503 --> 04:17:05,045
Not too expensive for you, Your Majesty.

4429
04:17:16,878 --> 04:17:18,127
How do I look?

4430
04:17:18,128 --> 04:17:20,837
Right now, you look like shit,

4431
04:17:22,170 --> 04:17:26,462
but soon, you're gonna look like
the king you were born to be.

4432
04:17:28,462 --> 04:17:29,462
I'll be in touch.

4433
04:17:33,295 --> 04:17:34,752
- [snaps fingers]
- [kids laughing]

4434
04:17:34,753 --> 04:17:37,252
[♪ rap music playing,
Wakil and El Da God "Last Pick"]

4435
04:17:37,253 --> 04:17:39,212
<i>♪ Little giants, giants ♪</i>

4436
04:17:39,878 --> 04:17:42,170
<i>♪ Little, little, giants, giants ♪</i>

4437
04:17:43,087 --> 04:17:44,794
<i>♪ Little giants, giants ♪</i>

4438
04:17:44,795 --> 04:17:47,627
<i>♪ How should I begin this?
I am so terrific ♪</i>

4439
04:17:47,628 --> 04:17:50,669
<i>♪ They don't know what hit 'em
So they looking like what is this ♪</i>

4440
04:17:50,670 --> 04:17:53,252
<i>♪ Came a long way
from my dread-lock days ♪</i>

4441
04:17:53,253 --> 04:17:56,169
<i>♪ Now I'm putting beats
in the the grave for a living ♪</i>

4442
04:17:56,170 --> 04:17:58,919
<i>♪ What that make me?
A legend and I'm living ♪</i>

4443
04:17:58,920 --> 04:18:01,961
<i>♪ This is for anyone
who knows what it feels like ♪</i>

4444
04:18:01,962 --> 04:18:04,586
<i>♪ To be fully capable
but still picked last ♪</i>

4445
04:18:04,587 --> 04:18:05,877
<i>♪ Picked last ♪</i>

4446
04:18:05,878 --> 04:18:07,252
<i>♪ Hell nah, skip that ♪</i>

4447
04:18:07,253 --> 04:18:11,211
<i>♪ Nah, we don't quit fast, quit fast
'cause we are ♪</i>

4448
04:18:11,212 --> 04:18:15,919
<i>♪ Little, little giants ♪</i>

4449
04:18:15,920 --> 04:18:17,002
<i>♪ 'Cause we are ♪</i>

4450
04:18:17,003 --> 04:18:19,045
<i>♪ Little, little giants ♪</i>

4451
04:18:21,378 --> 04:18:24,044
[reporter] <i>Chicago-based
venture capitalist firm</i>

4452
04:18:24,045 --> 04:18:26,836
<i>ArtWorks' CEO has made an overnight exit,</i>

4453
04:18:26,837 --> 04:18:29,794
<i>now setting the table
for a so-called invisible partner</i>

4454
04:18:29,795 --> 04:18:31,002
<i>to take the helm.</i>

4455
04:18:31,003 --> 04:18:33,087
[♪ eerie music playing]

4456
04:18:36,295 --> 04:18:38,669
[The Hood] Don't be shy.
Have you tried the caviar?

4457
04:18:38,670 --> 04:18:42,003
Something about being held against
one's will kills the appetite.

4458
04:18:42,920 --> 04:18:45,712
Besides, eating animal babies
is unethical.

4459
04:18:47,170 --> 04:18:51,003
I said... eat.

4460
04:18:52,170 --> 04:18:53,462
[energy whooshes]

4461
04:18:58,753 --> 04:19:00,128
[breathing heavily]

4462
04:19:03,128 --> 04:19:04,711
So why do you want me here?

4463
04:19:04,712 --> 04:19:06,795
Well, you'll need a place to lay low.

4464
04:19:07,753 --> 04:19:09,170
Since you got your hands dirty.

4465
04:19:10,920 --> 04:19:11,920
With Riri?

4466
04:19:12,712 --> 04:19:15,253
- You did kill her?
- Yeah, I did kill her.

4467
04:19:20,003 --> 04:19:21,003
[The Hood] You know...

4468
04:19:23,378 --> 04:19:24,795
'cause if, for some reason,

4469
04:19:27,128 --> 04:19:28,503
you been less than honest,

4470
04:19:29,920 --> 04:19:31,753
you know we'd have a problem, right?

4471
04:19:34,087 --> 04:19:36,045
I would kill her again if I could.

4472
04:19:38,545 --> 04:19:39,545
Fine.

4473
04:19:42,462 --> 04:19:43,795
- Eat.
- I'm not doing this.

4474
04:19:44,128 --> 04:19:46,128
- [energy whooshing]
- [straining]

4475
04:19:47,337 --> 04:19:48,712
[panting]

4476
04:19:51,878 --> 04:19:53,003
- [groans]
- [warbles]

4477
04:19:54,295 --> 04:19:56,253
[breathing heavily]

4478
04:19:58,587 --> 04:20:02,544
And you're programmed
to prevent anyone from harming me.

4479
04:20:02,545 --> 04:20:04,003
[breathing heavily]

4480
04:20:04,795 --> 04:20:05,795
Even you.

4481
04:20:10,087 --> 04:20:11,086
Release.

4482
04:20:11,087 --> 04:20:13,170
[groans, panting]

4483
04:20:16,628 --> 04:20:20,212
Wow. You're a real piece of shit.

4484
04:20:21,503 --> 04:20:22,503
What?

4485
04:20:24,295 --> 04:20:25,961
You got something to say? Speak.

4486
04:20:25,962 --> 04:20:27,795
Do you know how silly you look?

4487
04:20:28,753 --> 04:20:31,503
You've got all this power
and you're doing what?

4488
04:20:32,503 --> 04:20:36,503
Holding me hostage
and playing dress up in Dad's house?

4489
04:20:39,837 --> 04:20:43,712
You don't belong here,
and everyone's gonna know that.

4490
04:20:50,962 --> 04:20:52,337
[breathing heavily]

4491
04:20:54,128 --> 04:20:55,253
You're absolutely right.

4492
04:20:57,378 --> 04:20:58,378
What?

4493
04:20:58,962 --> 04:20:59,962
I shouldn't be here.

4494
04:21:04,003 --> 04:21:06,002
- Come on.
- I'm not going anywhere with--

4495
04:21:06,003 --> 04:21:08,295
- [warbling]
- [♪ tense music playing]

4496
04:21:12,378 --> 04:21:13,378
[horn blares]

4497
04:21:17,337 --> 04:21:20,170
[tattoo gun whirring]

4498
04:21:26,795 --> 04:21:28,253
I'm gonna give you the tools

4499
04:21:29,087 --> 04:21:32,503
so that you can get yourself
everything that you deserve.

4500
04:21:33,587 --> 04:21:35,087
- Cheers. Cheers.
- [lively chatter]

4501
04:21:36,878 --> 04:21:38,503
- You got that...
- I love you.

4502
04:21:39,920 --> 04:21:40,920
[grunts]

4503
04:21:45,628 --> 04:21:47,670
[shuddering]

4504
04:21:49,795 --> 04:21:51,795
[voices whispering]

4505
04:22:00,212 --> 04:22:02,503
[♪ upbeat music playing]

4506
04:22:05,212 --> 04:22:06,962
[beeping]

4507
04:22:10,003 --> 04:22:11,003
[exhales deeply]

4508
04:22:14,170 --> 04:22:15,919
[system trills]

4509
04:22:15,920 --> 04:22:17,003
[system blares]

4510
04:22:18,128 --> 04:22:19,336
Nah, that can't be right.

4511
04:22:19,337 --> 04:22:20,836
[keyboard clacking]

4512
04:22:20,837 --> 04:22:21,920
Okay. Yeah.

4513
04:22:22,753 --> 04:22:23,753
[system blares]

4514
04:22:25,628 --> 04:22:27,044
[system trills, blares]

4515
04:22:27,045 --> 04:22:29,502
I don't understand.
Everything is exactly the same.

4516
04:22:29,503 --> 04:22:30,627
Why can't I map Nat?

4517
04:22:30,628 --> 04:22:33,377
[echoing] You know
it's not the real Natalie, right?

4518
04:22:33,378 --> 04:22:34,752
Give me Nat.

4519
04:22:34,753 --> 04:22:36,294
[system trills, blares]

4520
04:22:36,295 --> 04:22:38,419
Give me my friend back,

4521
04:22:38,420 --> 04:22:40,712
{\an8}- you stupid machine.
- [system trills, blares]

4522
04:22:41,087 --> 04:22:42,587
- [zaps]
- God!

4523
04:22:47,253 --> 04:22:48,253
What?

4524
04:22:50,753 --> 04:22:52,962
I'm sorry you lost her, Ms. Riri.

4525
04:22:54,545 --> 04:22:55,545
So am I.

4526
04:22:56,545 --> 04:23:00,087
- Yeah, it sucks, Ri.
- [Riri] I didn't lose her. [shuddering]

4527
04:23:00,670 --> 04:23:03,628
Magic took her,
and magic can bring her back.

4528
04:23:04,753 --> 04:23:07,252
I'll figure it out after I get that hood.

4529
04:23:07,253 --> 04:23:11,002
Whoa, Ri. We need to test your suit
to see how the magic's affecting it.

4530
04:23:11,003 --> 04:23:13,961
Like, we still don't even know
why adding magic deleted Natalie!

4531
04:23:13,962 --> 04:23:17,045
- Baby, maybe take a minute.
- [Riri] I'm okay, Mom.

4532
04:23:18,295 --> 04:23:20,378
I can't let all this work be for nothing.

4533
04:23:21,462 --> 04:23:24,212
And thank you... all of you.

4534
04:23:25,462 --> 04:23:28,336
I know I'm bad at showing it,

4535
04:23:28,337 --> 04:23:29,877
but this really means a lot.

4536
04:23:29,878 --> 04:23:32,587
I couldn't have done this alone.

4537
04:23:35,128 --> 04:23:36,586
Be careful.

4538
04:23:36,587 --> 04:23:37,670
I will.

4539
04:23:38,462 --> 04:23:40,587
- [♪ epic music playing]
- [whirring]

4540
04:23:41,212 --> 04:23:42,337
[whooshing]

4541
04:23:43,795 --> 04:23:45,003
[whooshes]

4542
04:23:49,128 --> 04:23:52,378
Hey, can you hear me?

4543
04:23:54,045 --> 04:23:55,087
Answer me, damn it.

4544
04:23:59,628 --> 04:24:00,627
Talk to me.

4545
04:24:00,628 --> 04:24:02,545
[man in accent] <i>I don't like your tone.</i>

4546
04:24:03,378 --> 04:24:04,378
That you?

4547
04:24:06,045 --> 04:24:07,420
When did you get an accent?

4548
04:24:08,045 --> 04:24:09,920
[man] When did you get an attitude?

4549
04:24:12,670 --> 04:24:14,169
And where the hell have you been?

4550
04:24:14,170 --> 04:24:17,836
Aw, I've been a little bit busy.
You see, you're not my only client.

4551
04:24:17,837 --> 04:24:19,502
Didn't you get my messages?

4552
04:24:19,503 --> 04:24:22,961
You mean these scars
and a vision whenever you feel like it?

4553
04:24:22,962 --> 04:24:25,377
There's gotta be a better way
to communicate.

4554
04:24:25,378 --> 04:24:26,462
Well, I'm here now.

4555
04:24:27,628 --> 04:24:31,127
- Is there something I can help you with?
- Yeah. I need you to come through.

4556
04:24:31,128 --> 04:24:32,794
You promised me everything,

4557
04:24:32,795 --> 04:24:35,669
and you didn't say it would be like this.
You lied to me.

4558
04:24:35,670 --> 04:24:38,003
[distorted] I said be careful
how you speak to me!

4559
04:24:38,545 --> 04:24:42,503
[in normal voice] I stuck to
our agreement, to every letter of it.

4560
04:24:43,337 --> 04:24:45,961
I gave you every tool you needed
to live your best life,

4561
04:24:45,962 --> 04:24:50,877
including this lovely hood
that you're so very, very fond of.

4562
04:24:50,878 --> 04:24:52,962
[whooshing]

4563
04:24:55,003 --> 04:24:57,127
[♪ epic music playing]

4564
04:24:57,128 --> 04:24:58,336
[thuds]

4565
04:24:58,337 --> 04:24:59,712
[whirring]

4566
04:25:00,295 --> 04:25:01,295
[bell dinging]

4567
04:25:07,670 --> 04:25:09,877
- Riri.
- Zeke.

4568
04:25:09,878 --> 04:25:12,877
Nice suit.
Something happen to the old one?

4569
04:25:12,878 --> 04:25:15,920
Weird. I'm detecting
a voice command program.

4570
04:25:17,045 --> 04:25:18,753
Yo, I think you got hacked.

4571
04:25:19,170 --> 04:25:20,169
Oh.

4572
04:25:20,170 --> 04:25:22,377
[electrical crackling]

4573
04:25:22,378 --> 04:25:24,336
You wanted to be rich.

4574
04:25:24,337 --> 04:25:26,877
Or as you so eloquently put it,

4575
04:25:26,878 --> 04:25:31,420
you wanted to be stupid,
disgusting, greasy rich.

4576
04:25:32,003 --> 04:25:35,419
Like a modern-day Shakespeare.
He was also a twat.

4577
04:25:35,420 --> 04:25:38,045
[Parker] I'm trying. I did everything
I was supposed to.

4578
04:25:39,337 --> 04:25:41,794
It just feels empty.
Can't you give me more?

4579
04:25:41,795 --> 04:25:44,587
[laughs] Are you having a laugh?

4580
04:25:45,837 --> 04:25:47,545
You are hilarious.

4581
04:25:48,503 --> 04:25:51,419
Why would I do that when you've made
such a dog's breakfast

4582
04:25:51,420 --> 04:25:52,961
of everything else?

4583
04:25:52,962 --> 04:25:54,587
I've got a better idea.

4584
04:25:55,712 --> 04:25:59,878
Why don't I just replace you
with someone more appreciative?

4585
04:26:00,670 --> 04:26:03,795
Yeah, that would be... lovely.

4586
04:26:04,378 --> 04:26:07,086
I know we need to talk,
but I have business with Parker.

4587
04:26:07,087 --> 04:26:09,086
Can... [inhales] Can you move?

4588
04:26:09,087 --> 04:26:13,127
I totally hear your request.
There's just one small, tiny, little snag.

4589
04:26:13,128 --> 04:26:14,961
Parker finds out you're alive,

4590
04:26:14,962 --> 04:26:17,919
- I'm dead, so...
- [Riri] So I gotta whoop your ass, too?

4591
04:26:17,920 --> 04:26:20,753
[electrical crackling]

4592
04:26:22,545 --> 04:26:26,461
[suit charging up]

4593
04:26:26,462 --> 04:26:28,669
[whooshing]

4594
04:26:28,670 --> 04:26:30,087
[grunting]

4595
04:26:33,295 --> 04:26:34,295
[Riri groaning]

4596
04:26:36,253 --> 04:26:37,753
[static, beeping]

4597
04:26:38,420 --> 04:26:39,627
[groans]

4598
04:26:39,628 --> 04:26:41,044
[grunts]

4599
04:26:41,045 --> 04:26:42,545
[softly] I'll tell you what,

4600
04:26:43,962 --> 04:26:46,587
if you manage to hold on
to what I gave you,

4601
04:26:48,628 --> 04:26:50,378
I'll consider giving you some more.

4602
04:26:52,587 --> 04:26:53,587
Okay?

4603
04:26:56,462 --> 04:27:00,337
S... So I hold on to the hood
and you make it more powerful, right?

4604
04:27:10,420 --> 04:27:12,044
- [grunting]
- [electricity crackling]

4605
04:27:12,045 --> 04:27:14,462
[Riri] Seriously, let me try to help you.

4606
04:27:15,128 --> 04:27:16,587
[Ezekiel screams]

4607
04:27:17,920 --> 04:27:19,878
Or is Parker gonna control you forever?

4608
04:27:22,503 --> 04:27:23,544
[grunts]

4609
04:27:23,545 --> 04:27:25,170
[whooshing]

4610
04:27:26,503 --> 04:27:29,294
- [Ezekiel] How can you help?
- I'm gonna knee you in the groin.

4611
04:27:29,295 --> 04:27:30,627
- [Ezekiel] What?
- I'm sorry.

4612
04:27:30,628 --> 04:27:32,336
But maybe there's no bionics there.

4613
04:27:32,337 --> 04:27:34,461
Your body's gonna respond in crisis mode.

4614
04:27:34,462 --> 04:27:37,461
[panting] And shut down enough
for you to manually override

4615
04:27:37,462 --> 04:27:40,211
via the processor
beneath the node in my neck.

4616
04:27:40,212 --> 04:27:41,294
That's smart.

4617
04:27:41,295 --> 04:27:42,753
[Riri] So are we doing this?

4618
04:27:43,295 --> 04:27:46,294
[Ezekiel] All right, Riri.
Let's try it, but I just,

4619
04:27:46,295 --> 04:27:48,087
I don't know if I can stop.

4620
04:27:50,503 --> 04:27:51,919
- Be careful.
- [Riri groans]

4621
04:27:51,920 --> 04:27:54,545
- Sorry. I don't mean to do this.
- [crackling]

4622
04:27:55,045 --> 04:27:56,294
Damn!

4623
04:27:56,295 --> 04:27:57,587
[panting]

4624
04:27:57,962 --> 04:27:59,127
All right. Watch out!

4625
04:27:59,128 --> 04:28:01,002
Stand still. I'll try to pull it, okay?

4626
04:28:01,003 --> 04:28:03,127
For the sake of the Stane family name.

4627
04:28:03,128 --> 04:28:05,003
Okay. [shouts]

4628
04:28:06,170 --> 04:28:07,837
[groans]

4629
04:28:08,837 --> 04:28:09,837
[groans]

4630
04:28:10,253 --> 04:28:11,837
Yep, good, clean blow.

4631
04:28:12,337 --> 04:28:14,087
That's some good hittin'. [gasping]

4632
04:28:15,878 --> 04:28:19,252
[Riri] Our last step is
to override Parker's hold.

4633
04:28:19,253 --> 04:28:21,627
The quick and dirty fix
is to automate a virus

4634
04:28:21,628 --> 04:28:23,919
that will put you
and the implants to sleep.

4635
04:28:23,920 --> 04:28:27,670
You'll hard reset
and start brand new. Cool?

4636
04:28:29,045 --> 04:28:30,087
Do I have a choice?

4637
04:28:32,253 --> 04:28:34,086
You know, I hate to leave you here.

4638
04:28:34,087 --> 04:28:35,587
But like I said,

4639
04:28:36,837 --> 04:28:39,712
I've gotta put
a hood-wearing asshole in his place.

4640
04:28:40,420 --> 04:28:42,045
You know, no big deal.

4641
04:28:46,837 --> 04:28:48,211
[Ezekiel panting]

4642
04:28:48,212 --> 04:28:49,795
So, we friends again, Joe?

4643
04:28:50,962 --> 04:28:53,253
Joe? Joe's gone.

4644
04:28:57,045 --> 04:28:58,045
I...

4645
04:28:59,378 --> 04:29:02,420
I have millions of dollars'
worth of weapons inside me

4646
04:29:03,170 --> 04:29:05,587
and no idea where to put this anger.

4647
04:29:09,003 --> 04:29:10,212
Go handle Parker.

4648
04:29:11,128 --> 04:29:14,087
Just... know you and I aren't done.

4649
04:29:14,837 --> 04:29:16,837
[♪ tense music playing]

4650
04:29:21,295 --> 04:29:22,294
[button clicks]

4651
04:29:22,295 --> 04:29:23,753
[elevator whirring]

4652
04:29:24,503 --> 04:29:26,503
[electric warbling]

4653
04:29:30,587 --> 04:29:31,670
[doors whirring]

4654
04:29:36,087 --> 04:29:38,087
[♪ tense music playing]

4655
04:29:41,878 --> 04:29:43,878
[footsteps approaching]

4656
04:29:50,253 --> 04:29:51,337
Riri.

4657
04:29:53,920 --> 04:29:58,170
I knew that if I wanted you dead,
I'd have to be the one to do it.

4658
04:29:59,170 --> 04:30:01,502
[Riri] I did not come here
to play with you, Parker.

4659
04:30:01,503 --> 04:30:04,127
So you came here to what? Fight me?

4660
04:30:04,128 --> 04:30:06,128
I need you to give me that hood.

4661
04:30:10,837 --> 04:30:12,253
[laughing]

4662
04:30:13,920 --> 04:30:16,212
[The Hood laughing] Yeah.

4663
04:30:16,837 --> 04:30:19,795
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I shouldn't laugh. It's just...

4664
04:30:20,628 --> 04:30:22,962
You were so sure that
you were one of the good ones,

4665
04:30:23,503 --> 04:30:24,794
but now look at you.

4666
04:30:24,795 --> 04:30:27,295
You have your fancy suit,
but you won't use it to...

4667
04:30:27,962 --> 04:30:31,212
to stop a speedin' train
or save the city from an asteroid.

4668
04:30:31,962 --> 04:30:34,462
No, you just want this power for yourself.

4669
04:30:34,962 --> 04:30:38,295
That's not why I'm here.
It's not worth the cost.

4670
04:30:38,837 --> 04:30:40,087
[The Hood] Face it, Riri.

4671
04:30:40,962 --> 04:30:41,962
You're a criminal.

4672
04:30:43,212 --> 04:30:44,212
Like me.

4673
04:30:45,295 --> 04:30:46,837
[warbling]

4674
04:30:52,087 --> 04:30:53,753
[energy whooshes]

4675
04:31:00,962 --> 04:31:02,753
[The Hood] Don't tell me that's magic.

4676
04:31:03,337 --> 04:31:04,878
I thought you were tech-only.

4677
04:31:07,795 --> 04:31:08,961
Well, now it's a fight.

4678
04:31:08,962 --> 04:31:10,878
[♪ tense music playing]

4679
04:31:13,253 --> 04:31:14,337
[whooshes]

4680
04:31:15,753 --> 04:31:16,752
[groans]

4681
04:31:16,753 --> 04:31:18,712
[powering up]

4682
04:31:18,962 --> 04:31:19,962
[groans]

4683
04:31:21,712 --> 04:31:23,962
- [groaning]
- [clanking]

4684
04:31:24,962 --> 04:31:27,002
- [distorted growling]
- Holy shit!

4685
04:31:27,003 --> 04:31:28,752
[distorted growling]

4686
04:31:28,753 --> 04:31:31,837
- Parker, look at what it's doing to you!
- [distorted shouting]

4687
04:31:34,878 --> 04:31:36,378
[The Hood grunts, laughing]

4688
04:31:37,337 --> 04:31:38,920
Give me the hood, Parker!

4689
04:31:40,337 --> 04:31:42,836
[The Hood distorted] You're gonna
have to kill me first!

4690
04:31:42,837 --> 04:31:45,753
[growling]

4691
04:31:46,587 --> 04:31:49,462
- [roaring]
- [scraping]

4692
04:31:50,878 --> 04:31:52,877
[Riri] Stop! You're gonna
get us both killed!

4693
04:31:52,878 --> 04:31:55,337
[roaring]

4694
04:31:55,628 --> 04:31:56,628
[grunts]

4695
04:31:57,378 --> 04:31:59,211
Let me go!

4696
04:31:59,212 --> 04:32:01,461
- Commence emergency protocol.
- [suit blaring]

4697
04:32:01,462 --> 04:32:03,294
[powering up]

4698
04:32:03,295 --> 04:32:04,837
[laughs maniacally]

4699
04:32:06,628 --> 04:32:07,670
[explosion]

4700
04:32:11,503 --> 04:32:13,003
[metal creaking]

4701
04:32:17,753 --> 04:32:18,753
[Riri groans]

4702
04:32:19,795 --> 04:32:21,294
[coughing]

4703
04:32:21,295 --> 04:32:23,545
[♪ sinister music playing]

4704
04:32:35,045 --> 04:32:37,587
[shuddering]

4705
04:32:38,503 --> 04:32:40,670
[wood creaking]

4706
04:32:44,920 --> 04:32:47,336
[energy whooshing]

4707
04:32:47,337 --> 04:32:48,627
[shuddering]

4708
04:32:48,628 --> 04:32:50,545
[The Hood breathing deeply]

4709
04:32:53,545 --> 04:32:55,712
[whimpering]

4710
04:32:56,587 --> 04:32:58,462
[crying] Please don't.

4711
04:33:00,003 --> 04:33:01,003
Please don't.

4712
04:33:04,545 --> 04:33:06,795
It sounds kinda stupid
when I say it out loud,

4713
04:33:07,962 --> 04:33:08,962
but I trusted you.

4714
04:33:11,545 --> 04:33:13,087
[distorted] Everyone trusted you.

4715
04:33:21,753 --> 04:33:23,045
This one's for John.

4716
04:33:25,295 --> 04:33:26,295
[gunshot]

4717
04:33:28,003 --> 04:33:29,253
What the hell?

4718
04:33:29,795 --> 04:33:31,462
Pretty sweet hologram, right?

4719
04:33:32,003 --> 04:33:35,086
[♪ triumphant music playing]

4720
04:33:35,087 --> 04:33:36,462
- [bones crack]
- [groans]

4721
04:33:40,337 --> 04:33:42,337
- [voices shriek]
- [Parker screaming]

4722
04:33:45,837 --> 04:33:48,628
[screams] Give it back! Give it back!

4723
04:33:51,170 --> 04:33:52,170
[Parker coughing]

4724
04:33:53,045 --> 04:33:54,045
You all done?

4725
04:33:55,920 --> 04:33:58,002
You don't know what it's like without it.

4726
04:33:58,003 --> 04:33:59,752
[shuddering]

4727
04:33:59,753 --> 04:34:00,837
It hurts.

4728
04:34:02,128 --> 04:34:03,128
It hurts.

4729
04:34:05,837 --> 04:34:06,837
I know.

4730
04:34:10,587 --> 04:34:11,587
Please.

4731
04:34:17,920 --> 04:34:18,919
[button clicks]

4732
04:34:18,920 --> 04:34:20,503
[elevator whirring]

4733
04:34:22,378 --> 04:34:24,378
[shuddering]

4734
04:34:27,962 --> 04:34:29,962
[crying]

4735
04:34:33,628 --> 04:34:36,253
[echoes] <i>It hurts. It hurts.</i>

4736
04:34:43,545 --> 04:34:45,461
[elevator creaking]

4737
04:34:45,462 --> 04:34:46,545
[clanks]

4738
04:34:48,837 --> 04:34:50,170
[cutlery scraping]

4739
04:34:51,503 --> 04:34:52,502
[door creaks opens]

4740
04:34:52,503 --> 04:34:54,212
[chewing] Mm.

4741
04:34:55,212 --> 04:34:56,212
[man] Mm.

4742
04:34:58,212 --> 04:34:59,212
Wow. Mm.

4743
04:35:00,337 --> 04:35:01,336
Who are you?

4744
04:35:01,337 --> 04:35:04,212
Ah. I'm just somebody
who ordered too much.

4745
04:35:04,837 --> 04:35:05,837
Are you hungry?

4746
04:35:09,753 --> 04:35:11,337
[both in unison] Always.

4747
04:35:14,378 --> 04:35:15,587
Do we know each other?

4748
04:35:16,253 --> 04:35:19,544
We have some mutual acquaintances,
but we'll... we'll get to that.

4749
04:35:19,545 --> 04:35:23,294
In the meantime, sit, eat.
You gotta be famished from...

4750
04:35:23,295 --> 04:35:24,962
from all the commotion, hmm?

4751
04:35:25,628 --> 04:35:27,753
- You heard that?
- Mm, yes.

4752
04:35:28,378 --> 04:35:30,461
Now, you don't wanna sit down,

4753
04:35:30,462 --> 04:35:32,837
